{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations","id":719260,"title":"[Ex3] In which we brainstorm Sorcerous Initiations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-23T08:30:58-07:00","id":719260,"title":"[Ex3] In which we brainstorm Sorcerous Initiations","content":"<b>The Five Station Path</b><br /> <br /> Ask most members of the Dynasty to think of a sorceror, and they will conjour an image of a woman, robed in azure and emerald, bearing charms of beaten bronze and staves of lightning struck oak.<br /> They will regale you with tales of graduates from the Heptagram; their odd ways of moving and speaking, their curious rituals, and the queer sacrafices they have made in their pursuit of their art.<br /> <br /> The Five Station Path is one of the few remaining means of studying to become initiated into the arts of Sorcery. Preserved through the fall of the First Age by the Sidereals, it now serves as the foundation of formal sorcerous study in the Realm.<br /> <br /> Initiation into the Five Station Path is characterized by a metaphorical journey through five stations; Humility, Study, Experience, Fear and Sacrifice. The first four Stations may be approached in any order, but the station Sacrifice always comes at the end.<br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals<br /> <br /> Sorcerors of the Five Stations understand the value of preparation; by dint of careful study, they can ready their mind and body to call forth a specific spell at a moment's notice. They may spend five hours studying a specific spell to prepare it. If they do, for the next week, they gain three sorcerous motes which may only be used to cast the prepared spell. Once spent, these motes are lost until another study session re-prepares the spell, unless the prepared spell is one of the sorceror's controll spells, in which case the motes return at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> The ultimate lesson of the Five Stations is the question- what will you sacrifice for your sorcery. Once per scene, you may offer up some significant sacrifice; this may be literal, such as destroying some valued object, or more figurative, such as swearing to take or avoid some action or vice. If the Storyteller approves of the sacrifice, the sorceror immediately gains (Essence) sorcerous motes. Should they fail to uphold their self-imposed geas, then Creation will bend against them; treat this as having broken an Eclipse caste oath. Stories are replete of sorcerors tricked into violating their oaths and being struck down therefrom.<br /> <br /> Some sorcerors are known for their curious habit of hop-skip walking, taking care to move in diagonals or curves, or to advance with an almost dancer-like gait on the balls of their feet. They are practicing Pacing the Stars; by moving in well understood patterns, they learn to coax Creation to their whim more easily. When using a Shape Sorcery action in combat, if you Pace the Stars, reduce your Defense by 1 for the turn, and add +1 die to their pool. If they are shaping their prepared spell, instead add one automatic success. Students of the Heptagram learn this ritual as 'Walking the Dragon Lines', but the effect is the same.<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> Ritual Tools (** or ****): Sorcerors of the Five Stations frequently make use of ritual tools and implements- most frequently staves, khakkhara, or prayer strips. A sorceror who makes use of their ritual tools while taking Shape Sorcery actions adds +1 die to their pool. Additionally, some sorcerors can make use of artifact tools, allowing them to draw forth powerful Evocations from them.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Society (* to *****): The Five Station Path is unusual in that it is so formalized; most students of it learn in classes with fellow students. Almost inevitably, secret societies form within these classes, bonds which are only strengthend once the sorcerors return to the wider world, where their eccentric habits often leave them socially snubbed. This merit indincates membership in such a society; at one dot, the society is relatively small- it may be as little as yourself and one fellow you keep in contact with via letters or infallible messangers. More dots indincates societies of greater numbers and deeper resources. Membership is not free, however; while your society may be able to help you with your studies, Projects and other workings, your fellow society members are likely to call upon you as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:53:00-07:00","id":719892,"title":"","content":"Ar Tonelico-inspired song magic needs to be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T14:40:52-07:00","id":720618,"title":"","content":"For my Exorcist concept, I was thinking a sorcerous path that has you recite a prayer that invokes the authoriy of Unconquered Sun, giving you sorcerous motes for the scene. You also get bonuses to spells that attack CoDs, or bind and/or cadt outghost, spirits and demons. Just not sure of the mechanics yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:00:19-07:00","id":726175,"title":"","content":"I really want to develop a blood magic initiation. Ritually spilling someone else's blood releasing power, and more power if the sacrifice actually dies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T09:33:01-07:00","id":726308,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking of one that borrows the basic idea behind the example shaping ritual in the book where you prepare sorcerous motes ahead of time through study, only in this case you acquire them by completing a basic project and rolling Intelligence + Crafts; it only works for Crafts involving the use of fire in their creation. It would be called Seared by Sacred Fire, and it came from when the student of a group of metallurgist-monks in the Far North burned his upper body in their holy forge terribly during instruction. He saw enlightenment in the fire and felt it in the pain.<br /> <br /> Also it's an excuse to steal The Burning Name from the Ifrit Lord initiation without having to kneel to something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T10:08:03-07:00","id":726373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726308#post726308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it's an excuse to steal The Burning Name from the Ifrit Lord initiation without having to kneel to something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Given the heights of power a Solar can reach, I'd be disappointed if you couldn't, at some point, fluff it as the Ifrit Lord swearing allegiance to <i>you</i> instead of the other way 'round. Though it would still require you to be some kind of shining hero. Ifrits still seem to have their &quot;Champions of Justice (as they see it)&quot;-theme going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T10:30:29-07:00","id":726472,"title":"","content":"Ridden by the Damned<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer's soul was subsumed and ridden by Nephwracks and shades to a degree that left it cracked and open for the energies of the underworld to pour in, transforming cracks into necrotic teeth that can channel the energies of Sorcery/Necromancy (not sure yet if Necromancy is going to be separate from Sorcery or just a different initiation + fluff).<br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals:<br /> <br /> - Whenever the character acts as a conduit for an underworldly creature, either through possession or acting as a medium, make a reflexive contested willpower roll between the creature and the sorcerer. If the sorcerer wins, they gain sorcerous motes equal to the successes on the roll and the creature loses that many motes (if no motes are available, the difference is lost). These motes last until the end of the story and can never exceed the character's permanent willpower rating.<br /> <br /> - At night or in a Shadowland, the Sorcerer's Po soul awakens and grows vicious and hungry, imposing a hunger that can only be satiated by blood and flesh, represented as a Major Intimacy : Flesh (hunger). Whenever the character consumes living flesh or bathes in fresh blood, they roll Stamina + Occult gaining a number of sorcerous motes equal to the successes, up to the amount of lethal or aggravated health levels that the gore represents, which last until the end of the scene. Each such success drains the life-force from the meet and blood, turning an appropriate amount of it to ash, rot or thin tar.<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> Voracious Soul (** or ****) : While being possessed, the character can call upon the motes of the possessing entity as though they were Sorcerous Motes, and can override the being's control to take Shape Sorcery actions to cast the character's Control Spell. The 4-dot version permits the casting of any spell in this way.<br /> <br /> (comments and suggestions are welcome)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 10-25-2015, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:00:44-07:00","id":726498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726308#post726308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it's an excuse to steal The Burning Name from the Ifrit Lord initiation without having to kneel to something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Showing respect to a teacher shouldn't be something a Solar is above.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:09:37-07:00","id":726540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726498#post726498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Showing respect to a teacher shouldn't be something a Solar is above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you could rename that initiation path &quot;Punked an Ifrit Lord and Rolled Him for the Secrets of Sorcery,&quot; if your character is the kind who would swindle the secrets of sorcery from a mighty spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:20:44-07:00","id":726565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=719892#post719892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ar Tonelico-inspired song magic needs to be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking on this: is there anything in Linguistics dealing with constructed languages? Because if we're talking song magic inspired by Ar Tonelico then we can't possibly leave out some benefit based on speaking Hymnos or some other &quot;invented&quot; language. So maybe one of the perks of the initiation is that you receive a &quot;language of the soul&quot; drawn from your magic and impossible for other people to learn without being taught directly by you. So yay for you and your associates, but too bad for anyone trying to listen in on your conversations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:25:18-07:00","id":726568,"title":"","content":"<b>Past Life</b><br /> <br /> The Solar's sorcerous might trickles from the ancestral memories of her Exalted soul. <br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals: <br /> <br /> - Whenever the Solar's anima reaches a new level for the first time during a scene, the Solar gains (Essence) sorcerous motes. These motes last until the end of the scene. <br /> - When the Solar begins casting a spell, she gains a number of sorcerous motes equal to the rating of any Artifact she holds which was wielded by her past incarnation. The Solar may gain this benefit once per scene per artifact. <br /> - When the Solar directly basks in the light of the sunrise, she rolls her full Appearance + Occult Excellency. Every success grants her one sorcerous mote, which lasts until sunset. Double 9s if the Solar is standing in a standard Solar-aspect manses or demesne, or double 8s if she is standing in a greater in a greater manse or demesne. <br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> This pact does not grant any particular merits. Instead, the Solar may Purchase Innate Merits that are somehow related to her past life. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:26:20-07:00","id":726569,"title":"","content":"I wrote this for an artifact I worked on (but never playtested)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Battlefury Meditation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shu\u2019s pages describe a trance which charges the mind by stilling the body. This ritual is a simple action which allows the sorcerer to exchange two initiative per sorcererous mote. This ritual can be used once per scene, but can be reset by raising initiative past 20.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:38:32-07:00","id":726591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=719892#post719892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ar Tonelico-inspired song magic needs to be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask and ye shall receive. That said, this is my first home-brew ever, so let me know what you think, everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Song of Creation<br /> Among members of the Irai on the coast of the Sea of Dreams, it is widely held that Creation is a work wrought from song, and Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style is one proof of this. A sorcerer who is initiated into the Song of Creation knows the truth of this statement, for her soul sings in harmony with the greatest of all music. Emotion, song, and bonds intertwine tightly with one another for these sorcerer-singers, and the emotional ties they forge with those around them strengthens their ability to shape and research spells.<br /> <br /> Initiation into the Song is a different journey for each sorcerer. Sometimes, a sorcerer-singer hears the sound of Creation simply by listening to everything that exists around her. Other times, something in Creation strikes the sorcerer as so beautiful that it must be expressed via song. Most frequently, however, a person hears the song of another soul first, reaching and hoping for something \u2013 this is the beginning of the discovery of the Song of Creation.<br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals<br /> All souls sing in harmony with the ever unfolding ultimate hymn that is Creation, and sorcerers who initiate into the Song of Creation know this better than most. To them, the emotion-sounds of others have the power to uplift and empower them, while disharmonious feelings might disrupt their concentration. When another character with whom a sorcerer shares a mutual positive Minor or better Intimacy (whether to one another or to someone else) within two range bands is actively working towards the benefit of or in the defense of that Intimacy, her shape sorcery actions count as having one extra success. If, however, there is another character for whom the sorcerer has a Minor or better negative intimacy within two range bands and there exists no character who fulfills the requirements above, the sorcerer takes a -1 penalty to her shape sorcery actions. (I\u2019m also thinking about maybe doing some more complicated stuff with the intimacies, but I don\u2019t have the time to expand on it now).<br /> <br /> Time spent with another in joy strengthens the soul, as all sorcerer-singers know. When a sorcerer-singer spends a scene with someone who shares a mutual positive intimacy with her, whether this takes the shape of an afternoon alone with a lover, a long discussion with an old friend, or visiting her parents and sharing old stories, she receives (Intimacy Level) sorcerous motes until week is out. Once spent, these motes do not reoccur until another scene is spent with a positive intimacy, unless they are used to cast her control spell, in which case they resurge after the scene ends.<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> Music is Feeling (***) \u2013 A sorcerer with this merit may use (Perception + Performance) to read intentions once per scene. She also gains an additional +1 to attempts to inspire emotions that are in line with any of her positive intimacies.<br /> <br /> Hymns are Power (***) \u2013 With two dots in this merit, a sorcerer may substitute her Performance for her Occult when using shape sorcery actions. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":7858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","user":"*End","date":".  Grammar errors. Oopsies. 11-06-2015, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T11:52:21-07:00","id":726644,"title":"","content":"Riven Beyond Flesh<br /> <br /> Those who dwell too close to the yasal fields of the deep south must take great care. The faintest yellow tinge to water or crystal sparkle to food is the only warning that it is tainted with fragments of gods and demons trapped in crystals worn to dust. For the vigilant it comes to little, a yellowing of the skin or eyes and perhaps a propensity to hear voices in the wyld-born wind. For the desperate or unlucky it is a sentence of slow and terrible death. Those who inhale and imbibe too much slowly go mad as countless speakers utter half formed words in their minds and their bodies are torn apart by half formed amalgamations of spirits that can no longer be made whole.<br /> <br /> For some though... for some it is the path to something so much more. Perhaps they assimilated it more slowly, perhaps the mix of sundered spirits was balanced in some auspicious way. For these lucky few, the yasal fragments accumulate and align in a majestic harmony that opens their eyes to the secrets of creation and their souls to its living essence. These yellow sorcerers occupy a place neither man nor ghost in the legends of the desert, appearing like ghosts from among the most downtrodden to upset the social order or ruling as sultans of spirit-courts full of wonder and power.<br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals:<br /> - Once per scene the character may draw a single sorcerous mote from every spirit they have summoned or bound as a familiar. After having been used in this way spirits are more pliant but less efficacious, becoming unable to use their native charms.<br /> <br /> - The bodies of failed yellow sorcerers, or the corpses of their peers, can be a source of much power. Each such corpse stores a number of sorcerous motes equal to the health levels it possessed in life. Drawing these motes forth causes the bodies of the dead to slowly crumble back to the yasal dust that once marked them and any damage to the body also reduces the number of sorcerous motes it contains. A yellow sorcerer wishing to make use of such a resource rolls their Charisma + Occult and draws one sorcerous mote per ten on their roll, inflicting an appropriate amount of damage. Rumor has it that the oldest yellow sorcerers maintain crypts full of such bodies, carefully preserved against time, for use in their most taxing rituals. Finding such a hidden vault would be the gate to tremendous riches and sure to bring down terrible wrath if the owner ever discovers such a theft.<br /> <br /> Merits: (No idea of what dot level)<br /> - Golden Ichor: Having incorporated yasal into their whole body, the blood of a yellow sorcerer becomes a vessel for spirits. They may treat their own body as a yasal crystal that cannot be lost or stolen. However, if more than half of their health levels are filled with lethal damage any spirit they have bound in themselves is automatically freed and they may not bind a new spirit until at least half their health levels do not contain lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:01:57-07:00","id":726686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726591#post726591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ask and ye shall receive. That said, this is my first home-brew ever, so let me know what you think, everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent beginning. Maybe for a third ritual the constructed language thing I mentioned could only be learned by characters who share a positive intimacy with the sorcerer?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T12:03:11-07:00","id":726687,"title":"","content":"Hey, brainstorm. Remember those rings from 1E Book of 3 Circles that held the spirit of ancient sorcerors? Those would make a great initiation talisman or something.<br /> <br /> I'll start thinking of how to work them....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:28:09-07:00","id":726875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726498#post726498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Showing respect to a teacher shouldn't be something a Solar is above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars in general, yes, you are correct. This specific Solar had a bad experience with people making bargains with/supplicating themselves before an external power for the secrets of the universe (his mother made a bargain with Mara and it eventually got her killed/disappeared). So he's seeking very much to 'do things on his own merit' with regard to sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:38:19-07:00","id":726905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726875#post726875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars in general, yes, you are correct. This specific Solar had a bad experience with people making bargains with/supplicating themselves before an external power for the secrets of the universe (his mother made a bargain with Mara and it eventually got her killed/disappeared). So he's seeking very much to 'do things on his own merit' with regard to sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sounds like Vance's proposed &quot;Ganked the power of an Ifreet&quot; reskinning would work for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:42:18-07:00","id":726908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726905#post726905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, sounds like Vance's proposed &quot;Ganked the power of an Ifreet&quot; reskinning would work for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, definitely. I just wanted to try my hand at a custom Initiation for him, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T13:55:31-07:00","id":726954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726498#post726498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Showing respect to a teacher shouldn't be something a Solar is above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of Solars are, shall we say, imperfect. This is a teensy bit of a setting element, I'm given to understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T14:10:49-07:00","id":727034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726175#post726175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want to develop a blood magic initiation. Ritually spilling someone else's blood releasing power, and more power if the sacrifice actually dies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be using a blood sorcerer for an antagonist, and I think I'll just take the second ritual of the Pact with an Ifrit Lord, substituting the Resources thing with the victim's Stamina. If the sacrifice lives, their effective Stamina is halved, rounding down; if he uses his own blood, round up instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T14:17:39-07:00","id":727043,"title":"","content":"Insight from Bllodborne feels like it could make a pretty awesome Initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T15:07:18-07:00","id":727129,"title":"","content":"I think a reversal of Mara's initiation would be cool.<br /> <br /> <b>COVENANT WITH THE SUN</b><br /> The character became a sorceror by meditating on her own Solar Essence, emulating one of the Mice of the Sun, or by being initiated into sorcerous enlightement by a Solar Exalt or the Unconquered Sun himself.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> \u2022 The sorcerer draws power from revealing light, channeling it into her spells. Whenever she begins a scene standing directly under rays of bright light, bearing aloft a lit torch or lantern, or ablaze with an anima banner at the burning level, she gains three sorcerous motes, which last until the end of the scene and can be spent towards any spells she casts. Additionally, whenever she takes a shape sorcery action to shape a spell while brightly illuminated and clearly visible, she gains an additional sorcerous mote as long as the spell\u2019s target is paying her his full attention and seeking to engage her in combat or debate.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The sorcerer\u2019s patron offers her power in exchange for burnt offerings, breathing in the smoke of her tribute and rewarding her with glory. The sorcerer may make a prayer roll (Charisma + Performance, difficulty 5 minus the Resources value of any sacrifices offered along with the prayer) seeking power from her patron. Success grants her sorcerous motes equal to (her Essence + extra successes on the roll). These motes last for the duration of the story, and can be spent towards any spell she casts. She cannot pray for power more than once a day, and receiving new motes replaces any granted by past prayers.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The sorcerer has learned to cultivate the light of virtue in her own heart, using it to charge the power of her spells. Whenever she would gain a point of Willpower from upholding an Intimacy that represents a passionate emotion or fervent belief, she may instead claim 5 sorcerous motes. These motes last until the next sunset, and can be spent towards any spell she casts. If upholding that Intimacy causes in-character hardship that would be sufficient to gain solar experience as though from a Flaw, she gains 10 sorcerous motes, which last for the duration of the story. After the first time this bonus is awarded in a story, subsequent awards are lowered to the sorcerer\u2019s (Essence).<br /> <br /> <b>Other Benefits</b><br /> \u2022 <i>Faithful Servant</i> (Merit \u2022): Like one of the Mice of the Sun, the sorceror gains a Defining Tie of loyalty to the Unconquered Sun, which cannot be weakened or altered by any influence rolls or magic.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Fed by Virtue</i> (Merit \u2022\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022): Like one of the Mice of the Sun, the sorceror may satisfy hunger or thirst by acting compassionately or courageously to aid another. At three dots, her hunger pains may be allayed by witnessing someone else do the same, provided she has a Defining positive Tie to the person performing the virtuous action.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Duke of Burning Light</i> (Merit \u2022\u2022): Light and fire answer readily to the sorcerer\u2019s will. Whenever the sorcerer casts a spell that creates light or fire as its primary effect, or manipulates fire, its cost is lowered by three sorcerous motes. If it\u2019s her control spell, she may also waive a single point of Willpower from its cost once per day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rejected Merits</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022 <i>Celestial Nobility</i> (Merit \u2022): Gods recognize the sorcerer as one favored by the Unconquered Sun. Minor gods are treated as having a Minor Tie of amazed awe towards her, while major gods have a positive Minor Tie of respect, or some variation suited to their nature. This merit is not available to Celestial Exalted... or rather, would be redundant, as they are already considered favored by a Celestial Incarna by the very fact of their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Distant Solar Patron </i>(Merit \u2022\u2022): The Unconquered Sun appears to the sorceror in visions, feeding her with ambrosia from heaven. Once per story, the sorcerer\u2019s player may declare that she is visited by the Unconquered Sun in a vision while praying or meditating during the day. She does not recover Willpower from that sleep, but receives some significant benefit determined by the Storyteller\u2014tutelage in a new spell in a single night, double 9s on all shape sorcery spells for the next day, the service of a Mouse of the Sun or other servitor as a gift from the Sun, or something similar. She also wakes with a Minor Principle of \u201cI take pleasure in life and virtue,\u201d or strengthens that Intimacy if she already possesses it.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-26-2018, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T16:38:30-07:00","id":727358,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Book of 3 Circles, though they became obsolete fairly quickly as canon marched on, I liked the Lunar and Sidereal initiations. So--<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lunar Initiation:</b><br /> <br /> You have undergone the traditional No Moon initiation into Sorcery, consisting of three trials. Obviously, this is almost unique to Lunars, though it is not impossible for outcaste Dragon-Blooded or Solars to be tutored in this fashion.<br /> <br /> <b>--</b>You survived the Full Moon trial, to survive in a punishing wilderness while completing tasks dictated by your master, and being hindered by spirits working for them, and you can draw strength from self-reliance and unbreakable toughness. When you are struck by an attack while using Shape Sorcery, the spell immediately gains 2 sorcerous motes if it was Withering, or 1 sorcerous mote per level of damage you took if it was Decisive. If you succeed at a Resistance or Integrity roll caused by an enemy attack while using Shape Sorcery, you gain sorcerous motes equal to half your successes, to a maximum of 3. Note that you can still only cast a spell during your action, even if the cost is met outside of it.<br /> <br /> --You prevailed in the Changing Moon trial, living peacefully amongst animals nominated by your tutor, and overcoming predators that prey on them. When you make a Shape Sorcery action, you gain an additional mote if one or more animals (including your familiar) with a Major or stronger Intimacy towards you are within long range. Additionally, when you would draw Essence or Willpower from a familiar, you may gain 5 sorcerous motes instead of the usual benefit, which must be used on the turn they are drawn. Only one familiar can aid each spell in this manner.<br /> <br /> --You overcame the No Moon trial, where you were trapped in an illusion and given a problem with no logical solution. Forced to rely on instinct and intuition instead of your senses, you can still draw power from that side of yourself. When you make a Shape Sorcery roll, you can choose to close your eyes to gain +2 sorcerous motes, or stop your ears to gain +1 sorcerous mote, along with the penalties of blindness or deafness for one round. If you actually have those Flaws, you gain the bonus every turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","user":"Elemental","date":". 10-26-2015, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T16:50:20-07:00","id":727378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=727129#post727129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Distant Solar Patron </i>(Merit \u2022\u2022): The Unconquered Sun appears to the sorceror in visions, feeding her with ambrosia from heaven. Once per story, the sorcerer\u2019s player may declare that she is visited by the Unconquered Sun in a vision while praying or meditating during the day. She does not recover Willpower from that sleep, but receives some significant benefit determined by the Storyteller\u2014tutelage in a new spell in a single night, double 9s on all shape sorcery spells for the next day, the service of a Mouse of the Sun or other servitor as a gift from the Sun, or something similar. She also wakes with a Minor Principle of \u201cI take pleasure in life and virtue,\u201d or strengthens that Intimacy if she already possesses it.</div> </div> </div> </div>2-point Merit for UCS to be constantly appearing in your dreams seems to be contradictory to pretty huge setting elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T17:10:57-07:00","id":727402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=727129#post727129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a reversal of Mara's initiation would be cool.<br /> <br /> <b>COVENANT WITH THE SUN</b><br /> The character became a sorceror by meditating on her own Solar Essence, emulating one of the Mice of the Sun, or by being initiated into sorcerous enlightement by a Solar Exalt or the Unconquered Sun himself.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> \u2022 The sorcerer draws power from revealing light, channeling it into her spells. Whenever she begins a scene standing directly under rays of bright light, bearing aloft a lit torch or lantern, or ablaze with an anima banner at the burning level, she gains three sorcerous motes, which last until the end of the scene and can be spent towards any spells she casts. Additionally, whenever she takes a shape sorcery action to shape a spell while brightly illuminated and clearly visible, she gains an additional sorcerous mote as long as the spell\u2019s target is paying her his full attention and seeking to engage her in combat or debate.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The sorcerer\u2019s patron offers her power in exchange for burnt offerings, breathing in the smoke of her tribute and rewarding her with glory. The sorcerer may make a prayer roll (Charisma + Performance, difficulty 5 minus the Resources value of any sacrifices offered along with the prayer) seeking power from her patron. Success grants her sorcerous motes equal to (her Essence + extra successes on the roll). These motes last for the duration of the story, and can be spent towards any spell she casts. She cannot pray for power more than once a day, and receiving new motes replaces any granted by past prayers.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The sorcerer has learned to cultivate the light of virtue in her own heart, using it to charge the power of her spells. Whenever she would gain a point of Willpower from upholding an Intimacy that represents a passionate emotion or fervent belief, she may instead claim 5 sorcerous motes. These motes last until the next sunset, and can be spent towards any spell she casts. If upholding that Intimacy causes in-character hardship that would be sufficient to gain solar experience as though from a Flaw, she gains 10 sorcerous motes, which last for the duration of the story. After the first time this bonus is awarded in a story, subsequent awards are lowered to the sorcerer\u2019s (Essence).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is solid stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Other Benefits</b><br /> \u2022 <i>Celestial Nobility</i> (Merit \u2022): Gods recognize the sorcerer as one favored by the Unconquered Sun. Minor gods are treated as having a Minor Tie of amazed awe towards her, while major gods have a positive Minor Tie of respect, or some variation suited to their nature. This merit is not available to Celestial Exalted... or rather, would be redundant, as they are already considered favored by a Celestial Incarna by the very fact of their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Faithful Servant</i> (Merit \u2022): Like one of the Mice of the Sun, the sorceror gains a Defining Tie of loyalty to the Unconquered Sun, which cannot be weakened or altered by any influence rolls or magic.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Fed by Virtue</i> (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Like one of the Mice of the Sun, the sorceror may satisfy hunger or thirst by acting compassionately or courageously to aid another. Additionally, her hunger pains may be allayed by witnessing someone else do the same, provided she has a Defining positive Tie to the person performing the virtuous action.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Duke of Burning Light</i> (Merit \u2022\u2022): Light and fire answer readily to the sorcerer\u2019s will. Whenever the sorcerer casts a spell that creates light or fire as its primary effect, or manipulates fire, its cost is lowered by three sorcerous motes. If it\u2019s her control spell, she may also waive a single point of Willpower from its cost once per day.<br /> <br /> \u2022 <i>Distant Solar Patron </i>(Merit \u2022\u2022): The Unconquered Sun appears to the sorceror in visions, feeding her with ambrosia from heaven. Once per story, the sorcerer\u2019s player may declare that she is visited by the Unconquered Sun in a vision while praying or meditating during the day. She does not recover Willpower from that sleep, but receives some significant benefit determined by the Storyteller\u2014tutelage in a new spell in a single night, double 9s on all shape sorcery spells for the next day, the service of a Mouse of the Sun or other servitor as a gift from the Sun, or something similar. She also wakes with a Minor Principle of \u201cI take pleasure in life and virtue,\u201d or strengthens that Intimacy if she already possesses it. </div> </div> </div>Fed By Virtue feels overcosted for a sorcery-gated Merit. I feel like Celestial Nobility and Distant Solar Patron may be incongruous with the presentation of gods and heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T17:14:41-07:00","id":727419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=727378#post727378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2-point Merit for UCS to be constantly appearing in your dreams seems to be contradictory to pretty huge setting elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what, the Zenith Caste?<br /> <br /> Granted, that Merit could use a note that it's only become available recently, and was NOT available for the period of time in which the Sun had turned his face from Creation.<br /> <br /> But also, these visions are happening in dreams. You're not conversing with the Sun so much as receiving whatever information he deigns to give you. I feel this keeps him sufficiently &quot;distant&quot;.<br /> <br /> If that's not enough, one can either jack up the Merit cost or have the visions being sent by the Sun's servitor solar spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T17:24:58-07:00","id":727456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=727419#post727419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what, the Zenith Caste?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I mean, is Zeniths get one clear-isn message once, ever, and the other Castes get at least some kind of feeling. Getting once-per-story dreams is kind of a lot. Making it from a lesser sun servant would definitely reconcile the issue of &quot;UCS is basically removed from the setting except in very short-term specific ways.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T17:57:18-07:00","id":727597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=727402#post727402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is solid stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second two rituals are cribbed almost entirely unchanged from the Ifrit initiation, and the first ritual is just the first ritual of Mara's initiation turned on its head.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fed By Virtue feels overcosted for a sorcery-gated Merit. I feel like Celestial Nobility and Distant Solar Patron may be incongruous with the presentation of gods and heaven. </div> </div> </div>Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T07:04:21-07:00","id":728746,"title":"","content":"I've been working on an artifact/initiation for a character concept. It's not quite done yet, still needs a shaping ritual and evocations/merits/secret(optional) history, but I'll post what I've got. I can edit/update when finished if people are interested.<br /> <br /> If anyone is familiar with them, it's loosely based off of &quot;So you want to be a Wizard?&quot;, by Diane Duane, and the Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Great Art (Artifact xx)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u201cThe first step to finding an answer, is asking a question.\u201d<br /> - </span></i></span></span>The Great Art<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the Age of Sorrows, the Sorcerer is a feared and distrusted figure. Even in the houses of the Realm, sorcerers are shunned and isolated, left alone to perform their strange rituals and research. In the Threshold, it only gets worse; most practitioners hold themselves away in Manses and ancient ruins, seeking power through forbidden lore.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This is an unavoidable truth for a modern sorcerer, who can only dream of a better time. A time before, when sorcery was respected (if feared), and communities could flourish and share in their art together.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If legend is to be believed, the Golden Dusk Society was one such community, in a time before. It is said that they were a widely spread group, accepting members from all social strata, from the greatest of the Twilight to a newly initiated Mortal. The only requirements for membership is to find your way into the possession of The Great Art (some say on accident, some say it\u2019s fate, some say it\u2019s a higher intelligence guiding where and when the book appears); the instruction manual for the society. It often first appears as a simple book, smaller then most tomes but larger than a pamphlet. As the sorcerer (or future sorcerer, if The Great Art is initiating them) reads and asks questions, the tome seems to add required information and grow in size, sometimes containing more information than is possible to fit in it\u2019s pages.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">After requesting information for their own experiments and research, the initiate will find several blank pages near the end of the tome. After recording their research and findings, they are finally a full member of the Golden Dusk Society, and can access the research of all other members, or even pass along notes and letters to each other (which fall from the pages of the recipient's book).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Savants who know of the society don\u2019t believe any members have survived into the Age of Sorrows...or even if they have, the society is no longer recruiting. A copy of The Great Art has not appeared to a prospective initiate since the Usurpation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Shaping Rituals</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Continuing research has always been a cornerstone to the Golden Dusk Society, in order to continue the growth of The Great Art. After a sorcerer completes a new, unique sorcerous project and records his research into the blank pages, he gains (Ambition x (2 for Terrestrial, 4 for Celestial, 6 for Solar)) sorcerous motes, which can be used on any spell. These motes last one story, and the sorcerer can only have one such pool of motes at a time.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Every student quickly finds that The Great Art contains more than sorcerous knowledge. Everything from personal observations of ancient savants to detailed illustrations of the anatomy of demons can be found within it\u2019s pages, and called upon. When a sorcerer uses a stunt to describe how he is using his superior knowledge to gain an upper hand on an opponent, he gains (stunt level + 3) sorcerous motes. The sorcerer can only have one such pool of motes at a time, and the ritual can only be used once per scene. This can be reset by recording a new and unique observation into The Great Art, a 2 dice Lore or Occult stunt.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Evocations</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">While a Sorcerer is attuned to The Great Art, he can consult the tome while using a Shape Sorcery action to gain additional sorcerous motes. The sorcerer gains 1 automatically, and can take additional defence penalties, up to his Essence rating, to gain an equal amount of additional sorcerous motes, as he blocks out the outside world to focus.</span></span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2043-ladikn","name":"Ladikn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T15:47:34-07:00","id":730227,"title":"","content":"Here's the Initiation idea I thought of earlier, fleshed out and refined a little more. All three of the shaping rituals are either lifted directly from the book, or are are from the book with some changes.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seared by Sacred Fire<br /> You have trained with a nameless cult of metallurgist-monks who maintain the secrets the manse known as the Forge of the Sacred Fire. In the process of mastering their holy craft you burned yourself on the divine flames of the forge and came away scarred. The pain of the flame was the ultimate teacher that opened your mind to the deepest secrets of metalwork, and the sorcerous structure of Creation.<br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals<br /> Once per story, the sorcerer may engage in a basic craft project in which the use of fire is necessary. Completing the project grants her further insight into the fabric of reality, and allows her to roll (Intelligence + Craft). She gains sorcerous motes equal to the successes that last for that story's duration. The sorcerer cannot use Charms to decrease the time it takes to complete the basic project to benefit from this ritual, but can make use of them for anything else pertaining to it.<br /> <br /> Whenever the sorcerer takes a shape sorcery action, she may draw an additional (Essence) sorcerous motes from any fire within medium range, coaxing its power into her spell. This diminishes the flame\u2014a hallway of torches will be extinguished by a single invocation, while a bonfire might die down to small flames after the first, then go out altogether after the second. However, if the sorcerer is fighting near (or in!) a burning building, she has a nearly endless source of sorcerous motes to draw on. She may draw from fire elementals or other spirits of flame as well, draining (Essence) motes from their pools, but only if her shape sorcery roll exceeds their Resolve, and no more than once per scene against any one spirit. When the sorcerer draws Essence to fuel her control spell, flames are not diminished, and spirits do not lose the motes drawn from them.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer may bathe in the geomantic fires that burn in her manse\u2019s heart to gain (Essence + Willpower) sorcerous motes, at the price of taking a level of aggravated damage. These motes last for a fortnight, or until she next claims motes from the manse. While within the bounds of the manse, she also gains one additional sorcerous mote each turn while casting a spell. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I figure it has The Burning Name as a merit, but I want at least one other and I'm not sure what it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T19:10:03-07:00","id":730709,"title":"","content":"I heard somewhere that someone wanted Bloodbourne's Insight as an Initiation.<br /> <br /> While I don't own the book and have no clue what sorcerous motes are, I'll take a crack at fluff:<br /> <br /> <b>Dreamer of the Poison Revelation</b><br /> <br /> There are things known only to the Yozis. The nature of the world they once lived in before making Creation (though not its name), the place where the Bridge to Nowhere leads, and the true name of the Unconquered Sun. To learn-or more accurately, infer-these things is to invite catastrophe in the form of Orabilis, End of All Wisdom and Librarian of Malfeas, who is permitted to travel anywhere in and out of the Demon City to silence those who would pry deeply into the minds of the imprisoned Titans. He lights the errant sorcerer's very soul aflame, and places it within the celestial firmament of Hell, simultaneously sentencing them to a long, slow death and honoring them for their intellect, for their death is a painless one in the court and presence of Ligier, the living Green Sun himself.<br /> <br /> Very rarely, a scholar's force of will controls the flames, and they remain as they were, with only a silver scar to mark them. From there, by definition whatever they learned is one not private to the Primordials, though Orabilis considers the surviving scholar a worthy personal rival from then on out. For the most part, these things are mere relative tidbits-that the Primordials former world is named &quot;Zen-Mu&quot; is largely pointless to the Creation-Born, or that there is something called a Shining Answer that Gaia seeks. A few are wonders whose release leads to golden eras, held back by the Primordials out of fear and later spite of their creations, such as the secret of forging orichalcum.<br /> <br /> At least one, however, was held back because of what <i>compassion </i>the Primordials had and have. In the ending days of the First War, when the great Dragon Beyond The World was imprisoned within his own wings, She Who Lives In Her Name attempted to free him through use of her laws, redefining his wings as something he may escape from. To her eternal regret, she succeeded-partially, allowing all who had gathered to save their brother to see what lay within. For the next five days and nights, Isidoros fled across the skies, Cecelyne declared herself ground for rebels, and Adorjan's passage made life from the ground. When the three recovered their senses, and coaxed their sister from hiding within the King's heart, all four agreed that no one deserved to know what it is they saw within Oramus.<br /> <br /> Naturally, a Solar Exalt discovered that in time. Among all of Malfeas' stars, his is unique in that it is the only one that was set alight long after feeling Orabilis' touch-his soul being ablaze was the only way he could not see.<br /> <br /> However, such a terrible thing could not be completely forgotten, though the Solar told no one and destroyed all that led him to that horrible wisdom, the idea has gained life . For Oramus' wings are forever chipped, and whenever someone invokes the secret laws of darkness and solitude that the Principle did on that auspicious day, so shall the Dragon's Revelation make itself known:<br /> <br /> <i>I'm not alone in here.</i><br /> <br /> <i>No one's ever alone anywhere.</i><br /> <br /> And those who learn that see why.<br /> <br /> (anyone up for mechanics? I see this as manipulation and twisting of perception; shaping rituals are generally based around confronting-or revealing-unpleasant truths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 10-27-2015, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-27T18:11:47-07:00","id":733582,"title":"","content":"a sorcerous initiation an ST wrote for my Twilight character:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Pact With Ligier:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is power in artifice, and the Infernal Architect draws it forth, hammering the essence of the world into shape as he would beat out metal on a forge. Whenever he acquires crafting experience, he also accumulates Sorcerous motes which last until he next completes another project of that level. Silver experience provides 1 mote, gold experience provides 2 motes per point, and white experience four motes per point.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">And with the following as Sorcerous Merits she might buy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">((Same as for the other demon path))</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Infernal Nobility (Merit \u2022): Demons recognize the sorcerer as one of Ligier's proteges. First Circle demons are treated as having a Minor Tie of terrified awe towards her, while Second and Third Circle demons have a positive Minor Tie of respect, or some variation suited to their nature.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">((Same as the fire elemental path)) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Burning Name (Merit \u2022\u2022): Speaking a syllable of her patron\u2019s name, the sorcerer may call forth green fire, sending it streaming from her eyes, fingertips, or mouth. She might use this to light a campfire or incinerate ropes that bind her hands, and can also use it as an attack, rolling (Intelligence + Occult) to direct the flames, which are treated as a light mundane weapon with the lethal, thrown (short), and mounted tags.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">((Adapted from another path based on Ligier's sense of superiority))</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Font of Disdain (Merit \u2022\u2022) A craftsman has no time for emotion, regret. There is only his work. Once per day, when his Resolve is overcome by influence that opposes an Intimacy based on conviction or determination, she may lower the Willpower cost to resist it by one point.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T05:31:05-08:00","id":753783,"title":"","content":"I kitbashed an initiation together from the ones in the Core;<br /> <br /> <b>Heir of the Palace of Clouds</b><br /> The character carries within her the blood of powerful spirits of the sky, or the air elementals which tend the clouds, which has kindled within her the rage of storms, as well as the benevolence of the merciful clouds that bring the relief of rain.<br /> At the moment of initiation she breathed her first <b>real</b> breath in her entire life, her life force and sorcerous power congealing into a Familiar *** spirit/elemental of Air, (which must be paid for seperately) through which she might channel her sorcerous powers, and which aids her in shaping sorcery.<br /> <br /> ((I have no idea for shaping rituals, any help there would be greatly appreciated. The familiar, and the power of clouds and fogs, as well as the nobility-association of the skies are supposed to be major themes))<br /> <br /> ((Ported over from Mara's initiation))<br /> * - Lofty Nobility - Minor positive tie (per storyteller discretion) with Air elementals, and gods and spirits assoicated with storms, clouds, or the sky, with spirits of increasing power being progressively less impressed.<br /> <br /> ((Stolen from the Ifrit Lord initiation)<br /> ** - Words as Storms - From the cauldron of storms within her soul, the Sorcerer exhales an eddy of air current, that carries with it a dense fog; this might be used to enable stunts in which the fog obscures sight or disorients enemies. More importantly, the air currents can develop surprising speeds and force, and be used to make attacks with a (Intelligence + Occult) roll, and the traits of a light mundane weapon, with the bashing, mounted, and thrown (medium) tags, attacks of which reduce the cost for a knockdown gambit by 1.<br /> <br /> ((Stolen from Mara's initiation again)<br /> Mark of Clouds - Tattoo-like markings of clouds, and air currents, manifest on the characters skin, allowing her to develop Evocations that deal with the controll of the winds, clouds, fog, and at higher Essence scores, entire weather patterns, such as summoning violent thunderstorms.<br /> <br /> OOC notation: The actual aesthetics of this initiation are supposed to be less of an outright imitation of Air Elemental powers, but also to contain themes of nobility, and the elevated nature of the skies and clouds; weather manipulation within this path is supposed to be less outright destructive, and rather provide means of utility, like conjuring a healing mist, or bringing fertilizing rains, not just calling down lightning storms or ragdolling fuckers with air bending, because that would be boring. So lofty sky-god shit in the sense of Tibetan Sky Burials, or &quot;up there be the sun&quot; holy effects are welcome, if you guys can come up with any.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T05:34:17-08:00","id":753787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726954#post726954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lots of Solars are, shall we say, imperfect. This is a teensy bit of a setting element, I'm given to understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every human being is imperfect. This has no bearing on the original point, which is wholly correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:16:56-08:00","id":753827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=753783#post753783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kitbashed an initiation together from the ones in the Core\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Might I suggest that the elemental in your initiation is a fairly &quot;zen&quot; huraka? What they do is less &quot;airbending&quot; and more pushing clouds hither and yon. Some sort of lord of cloud people could also work. Perhaps your tattoos could enable you to walk on smoke/mist/clouds, or otherwise handle them as if they were solid? <br /> <br /> (You could achieve a limited form of &quot;flight&quot; by having a burning censer dangling on a rope below you to generate smoke for you to walk on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T06:36:39-08:00","id":753873,"title":"","content":"I like the treating of clouds as solid and you definitely vibe with me with the cloud herding, though this initiation decidedly doesn't entertain the notion of sorcery being external to the character and it being granted by an elemental. Not that you contradict this, I just felt like emphasizing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T21:15:56-08:00","id":755805,"title":"","content":"<b>Pact with a Forge-God(dess)</b><br /> <br /> A Forge-God or Goddess will only form a pact with a notable craftsman who practices at least one craft that deals in metal. Learning their sorcery through the ring of metal, the shaping of steel, and the heat of the forge, they temper themselves much like they would a fine blade. <br /> <br /> <i>Shaping Rituals</i><br /> <br /> Initiation reveals to the Sorcerer the sorcerous essence in all items forged by their own hand. As part of a shaping action, the craftsman may sacrifice one item that they had made themselves and have at hand. An item created as a Basic Project grants them 1 sorcerous mote, Major 2, Superior 4, and Legendary 8. Items sacrificed in this way are destroyed, but may be repaired with appropriate time, resources, and skill, though any item that is unique and cannot be recreated (Daiklaves and other artifact weapons, Legendary artifacts) is permanently destroyed if it is sacrificed a second time.<br /> <br /> As part of a crafting effort, the Sorcerer may dedicate their effort to their Pact. In doing so they do not gain crafting xp of the highest type they would gain (no Silver for Basic, no Gold for Major, no White for Superior or Legendary). Instead they are granted power based on their skill and the resolve to make the item. Make a crafting roll at a forge after finishing a Project, putting their strength into it (Strength + Craft, difficulty 5 minus the value of the Project Basic -1, Major -2, Superior -3, Legendary -4). Success on this roll grants motes equal to the sorcerer's (Essence + extra success on the roll). If the finished item either hit all three basic objectives or was completed exceptionally well add additional motes equal to the value of the project (Basic 1, Major 2, Superior 3, Legendary 4). These motes last until the end of the current Story and may be replaced no more then once per day.<br /> <br /> <i>Other Benefits</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ritual Crafting</b> (Merit \u2022\u2022) As part of using a Charm with a Craft Roll that takes at least one hour, the Sorcerer may do a Shape Sorcery action to gather motes. These motes may then be spent on the Charms being used to aid in the Craft Roll. No project may benefit from this more then once per day.<br /> <br /> <b>The Forge Knows It's Master</b> (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) In a ritual lasting twenty minutes to an hour (ten minutes per dot, N/A count as six), the sorcerous artificer may roll a Shaping Sorcery roll with no aid from Charms when handling an artifact they have made. Every hit on this roll lowers the Attunement cost of the artifact by 1, to a maximum of it's Attunement cost, for one week. No artifact may undergo this ritual more then once a week.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> What do people think? Is it any good? Is it crap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T22:59:49-08:00","id":755862,"title":"","content":"So a friend of mine has a concept for a Twilight who Exalted by inventing a new form of Sorcery independent of the Salinian Method. This was prior to Ex3's reveal, and of the Initiations.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea was that there's magic in numbers and in calculations, so charting out Essence flow with runes, numbers, and graphs... As well as preparing runes in solid objects, such as carving a rune that fires Death of Obsidian Butterflies from the wall when activated.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;Exalted by inventing her own Initiation&quot; is an easy enough port, but it's tough to come up with some Shaping Rituals. I'm thinking like... Spending a few minutes centering herself in the morning to do the needed math, gaining (Int + Lore) Sorcerous motes for the day. I <i>did</i> think of a Merit!<br /> <br /> <b>Working Optimization</b> (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022) The understanding of the flow of Essence around her, the Sorcerer can improve their Workings through proper planning. When determining the total number of Means for a Sorcerous Working, the Sorcerer may attempt to lay a rune foundation for her Working. The Sorcerer makes an Intelligence + Lore check (Difficulty 3 for a Terrestrial Working, Difficulty 5 for a Celestial Working, Difficulty 7 for an Adamant Working). Upon a success, the Sorcerer has earned an additional Means. A failure means that the Sorcerer does not benefit from their plans. A botch on this roll can lead to a Sorcerer working from a flawed design, resulting in a Complication, as though she had botched one of the rolls on her working (even if she does not botch any rolls on the Working itself)<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for Spell Maths and Runes would be appreciated!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T23:23:36-08:00","id":755930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HK-87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=719892#post719892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ar Tonelico-inspired song magic needs to be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know that reference, but I desperately want a musical form of Sorcery for my Orpheus-based character, so nature itself will respond to his music.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T23:27:53-08:00","id":755931,"title":"","content":"Well, there's already one example initiation for musical sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T23:33:14-08:00","id":755936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=755931#post755931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there's already one example initiation for musical sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the sample Shaping Ritual without a full archetype on page 471?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T23:57:08-08:00","id":755940,"title":"","content":"Yes, sorry I should have said one example ritual rather than initiation.<br /> <br /> So, if you were a Terrest\u200brial sorcerer, you could use that. If you were a higher-ranked one, you'd need to make more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T04:50:18-08:00","id":756265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=726175#post726175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want to develop a blood magic initiation. Ritually spilling someone else's blood releasing power, and more power if the sacrifice actually dies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty much into Necromancy's alley too, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T09:51:22-08:00","id":756695,"title":"","content":"Here's something that I thought of for a character of mine. Thoughts?<br /> <br /> --- Whenever the Sorcerer successfully protects another from harm while using the Defend Other action, whether by taking the blow meant for their charge or blocking it entirely, they gain sorcerous motes. If the attack was denied completely, they gain the difference between their Defense and the attack's rolled successes. If they are the one struck, roll dice equal to the lost Initiative or Health Levels; for ever success, they gain one sorcerous mote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2781-bursting-eagerness-soul","name":"Bursting Eagerness Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:39:09-08:00","id":756996,"title":"","content":"Cross-posted from another thread, if this is the place where we're collecting these then so be it!<br /> <br /> <b>Grimoire of the Primal Song</b><br /> <br /> &quot;It is said by the Eldar that in water there lives yet the echo of the Music of the Ainur more than in any substance else that is in this Earth; and many of the Children of Il\u00favatar hearken still unsated to the voices of the Sea, and yet know not for what they listen.&quot; -J.R.R. Tolkien, Silmarillion<br /> <br /> It sang through Creation, and it sang of creation in refrains too faint for ears to hear, patterns too subtle to be seen, reverberations that carried traces of the first and foremost act of Creation. There was a man of great learning and wisdom - and possibly madness; through dark science he recovered a fragment of the universal song. He wrote down what he could determine of its strains, its stanzas, its choruses and its refrains, its shifts to red and its shifts to blue. Written upon hardened bandages and bound in behemoth-skin, the result looks absolutely nothing like a song, for it dips between aspects of reality at will. Why would one call the movement of a universe a song, anyway? Perhaps there was no song which birthed Creation and the man was just a crazy person, but if so the tangled web of his madness alone is sufficient to tell the laws of Being to sit down and giddy-up. Would that be more impressive or less?<br /> <br /> The Grimoire is badly damaged, pieces and parts of the song incomplete or missing. Pieces of the text continually <i>go</i> missing and reappear again years or decades later, a whole page becoming torn-out when the book is opened again and vice-versa, suggesting that its damage is much more than physical. Nonetheless, sufficient study of its ways and patterns is more than sufficient to initiate a man into the higher mysteries of sorcery.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer may draw upon the power of surrounding music, letting it flow across his spellwork and give definition to it. Whenever she takes a Shape Sorcery action, ambient music grants her up to (Essence) sorcerous motes for the rest of the scene. No more than (Essence)*5 sorcerous motes can be gathered thus during a scene.<br /> <br /> The solidity and attunement to the framework of Creation allows the sorcerer a keener grasp on what lies outside it. When she Joins Battle against a being with an origin outside Creation, she gains a number of sorcerous motes equal to her successes on the Join Battle roll, to a maximum of 3+(Essence).<br /> <br /> Merit 3: Fortissimo - The fragment of the song allows manipulation of the fine aspects of Creation in dynamic (but ephemeral) ways. Creation-born being as eminently practical as they are, the book's bearers have occasionally decided to shape these ephemeral shifts in reality into weapons. The sorcerer might manifest ice knives, wind-blades, rob the edge from a man's sword to strike him with it or turn a man's fear into a ravenous monster - for a moment. In concrete terms, the sorcerer can create light mundane throwing weapons with the Thrown (Medium), Lethal, Mounted characteristics. These do aggravated damage to faeries and other creatures of the Wyld, as it assails them with the raw Stuff of Reality.<br /> <br /> Merit 4: Composition - This shaping ritual benefit can only be purchased by a being with the Wyld-Shaping Technique charm or some equivalent. As the sorcerer shapes the raw unreality of the Wyld, it echoes with the essence of the First Creation. The sorcerer enjoys double 9s on all rolls to Wyld-shape lands or demesnes and adds one success to them, ensuring that whatever else happens the land of the Wyld will not turn on the sorcerer. The resulting land is rawer and fresher, with very large plants and animals (if appropriate) and an exceptional levity in the chest upon breathing its air.<br /> <br /> Merit 5: Bridge - They made doorways. Bridges, to other strains. To other parts. Did they know? Could they know? The sorcerer gains mastery of Distance, allowing them to perceive doorways wrought in the stuff of Creation. Most of these are too small to send a pin through, much less an animal, much less a person. Every now and then one is large enough to move through. The sorcerer may automatically perceive gates to Yu-Shan, to Malfeas, to Zen-Mu and to the Underworld, and once per story may teleport up to 1,000 miles with a specialized Rush action that uses Intelligence+Occult. He may specify a direction but not a specific destination, for the bridges are ever-shifting. Taking a doorway is never straightforwardly fatal, but the other end may not necessarily lie in Creation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T14:14:17-08:00","id":757279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=755930#post755930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't know that reference, but I desperately want a musical form of Sorcery for my Orpheus-based character, so nature itself will respond to his music.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an obscure little JRPG series that I'm quite fond of. Song magic casters wield magic that is shaped strongly by both their emotions and arcane lyrics in a constructed language called hymmnos, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u1GtMiKXE_E\" target=\"_blank\">which sounds like this</a>. The setting gimmick that they interface with to summon their magical power even provides feedback that simulates instrumentation and a supporting chorus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:24:39-08:00","id":763643,"title":"","content":"I've broken out the old sorcery books from !E and 2E. seeing a lot of stuff that while back then didn't seem to have purpose, now could be used for Sorcerous Initiations. I'll post some if I det ideas how to work it.<br /> <br /> That's the fun of 3E sorcery. It's actually made sorcery, which I thought was lame in the previous editions, into something fun I wanna play with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T19:32:37-08:00","id":763678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=755862#post755862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a friend of mine has a concept for a Twilight who Exalted by inventing a new form of Sorcery independent of the Salinian Method. This was prior to Ex3's reveal, and of the Initiations.<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea was that there's magic in numbers and in calculations, so charting out Essence flow with runes, numbers, and graphs... As well as preparing runes in solid objects, such as carving a rune that fires Death of Obsidian Butterflies from the wall when activated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black and White Treatise has a magical system similar to this, the Theanoan school. Apparently it is practiced by most Sidereal sorcerers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T21:39:05-08:00","id":763743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=763678#post763678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Black and White Treatise has a magical system similar to this, the Theanoan school. Apparently it is practiced by most Sidereal sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I'll flip that open to it. Is that 2E or 1E, because if there's a 1E Black and White I may have to do some digging for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T21:50:45-08:00","id":763750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=755862#post755862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the idea was that there's magic in numbers and in calculations, so charting out Essence flow with runes, numbers, and graphs... As well as preparing runes in solid objects, such as carving a rune that fires Death of Obsidian Butterflies from the wall when activated.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I prepared explosive runes this morning.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T22:04:06-08:00","id":763759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=763750#post763750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I prepared explosive runes this morning.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;And by Explosive Runes, I mean Flight of the Brilliant Raptor.&quot; *BOOM*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T22:57:09-08:00","id":763798,"title":"","content":"&quot;Strange. This Old Realm rune says 'Death Ra-'&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T23:39:32-08:00","id":763815,"title":"","content":"Idea brainstorm (after rereading the City of the Mad from Bo3C): how about a sorcerous initiation based on giving up your sanity. Percieving reality is holding you back. Madness gives you the insight to work magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T00:35:13-08:00","id":763834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=763815#post763815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idea brainstorm (after rereading the City of the Mad from Bo3C): how about a sorcerous initiation based on giving up your sanity. Percieving reality is holding you back. Madness gives you the insight to work magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would it would be distinct from <i>Scarred by Nightmares</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T00:55:06-08:00","id":763849,"title":"","content":"Scarred by nightmares is about dreams. This is Malkavian style insanity.<br /> <br /> Its just a thought. Havnt worked it out yet<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T01:34:08-08:00","id":763860,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping the new sorcery book will have an initiation akin to Words of Power.<br /> In my dreams:<br /> During shape sorcery, spellcaster may recite the words of power that materialize in her mind. <br /> Roll Lore+Int to determine additional motes gathered with a difficulty set by the circle of spell<br /> On fail, it increases the required motes<br /> On botch, it misfires<br /> Reciting the Words of Power causes the caster's voice to mystically reverberate across the immediate surroundings up to medium range. This is both good and bad. <br /> Silencing the caster is one way to make sure she fails.<br /> The words are always different, always changing. They are determined by the situation and the spell being prepared which is amazing stunt fodder.<br /> <br /> Additionally the caster may use her key, which are a set of words that resonate deeply with her. These words always remain the same, but also reveal an important intimacy or tie that the caster has. This provides even more motes when recited along with the Words of Power, determined by how deep or damning is the connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3364-sodina","name":"sodina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T01:38:02-08:00","id":763862,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it could be a rather nice one.<br /> <br /> And definitely sounds like one that my primary character idea would want to take eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:26:49-08:00","id":764001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=763743#post763743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, I'll flip that open to it. Is that 2E or 1E, because if there's a 1E Black and White I may have to do some digging for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's 2e, the 1e sorcery books were the Book of Three Circles and Savant and Sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T06:58:22-08:00","id":772269,"title":"","content":"Hello there! I am in the process of making my first Exalted character in the 3rd edition and I decided to homebrew some areas of the character (such as artifacts and Shaping Ritual). I did a small internet search to see what was out there (and I shamelessly borrowed heavily from one (enlightenment of the Imperfect lotus)) but none was close to what I envisioned from my char, so I combined many ideas and made a new one myself. <u>Please critic and find any problems/solutions</u>. Would you allow it in one of your games?<br /> <br /> <b>BATTLEFORGED ASCENSION</b><br /> <br /> Life is a continuous battle, existence is a continuous battle. Furthermore it doesn\u2019t matter if you won or lost; what matters is that you fought, learned and survived. This is the first truth one has to comprehend upon which his eyes open to new horizons and his initiation to sorcery can begin. Yours is a sorcery rooted on the enlightenment of the Dao of battle.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> <br /> The most challenging enemy is always oneself. The sorcerer knows that he would rather conquer his self that win a thousand battles. Once per day the Sorcerer may enter a deep brief meditation lasting 15 minutes. During this meditation he enters an imaginary battle with himself. The outcome isn\u2019t important but the enlightenment gained is. He may roll (Wits + Occult) and gain one sorcerous mote per success. These motes last until the next time she sleeps, and can be spent towards any spell she casts. If the sorcerer spends only sorcerous motes granted by the meditation casting her control spell, each counts as two motes towards meeting the spell\u2019s cost.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer finds hidden meaning and a chance to improve himself in any battle as he struggles to bring success against all odds. Whenever the sorcerer strikes with a withering attack he may opt to covert the initiative he would have gained into half as many (round up) sorcerous motes instead. Sorcerous motes gained through this ritual fade at the battle\u2019s end (when the combatants leave Initiative).<br /> <br /> All Battleforged sorcerers know that when facing death it\u2019s the moment they most feel alive. The pure instinct to survive, the adrenaline from evading a death blow, the surge of essence as they try to endure a strike, they all become a source of power for them. Whenever the sorcerer successfully dodge, block or completely soaks an attack from a non-trivial opponent he gains 1 sorcerous mote .If the sorcerer spends only sorcerous motes granted by avoiding or successfully absorbing an attack, casting her control spell, each counts as two motes towards meeting the spell\u2019s cost. Sorcerous motes gained through this ritual fade at the battle\u2019s end (when the combatants leave Initiative).<br /> <br /> <b>Other Benefits</b><br /> <br /> Tame Ones Fears (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The sorcerer has learned to battle his fears and instead of numbing his thoughts and action it helps his fuel them. Rather that becoming immune to fear instill actions the sorcerer overcomes them despite being frighten. If an opponent has succeeded in a fear instill action, roll (Wits + Integrity) against a difficulty set by the opponents essence. If you succeed it counts as if you had spent willpower to negate the effect. Furthermore you gain the opponents success on the attempt as sorcerous motes or essence motes your choice.<br /> <br /> Loyal Armament Endowment (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The sorcerer has fought many battles together with his loyal artifacts overcoming the boundaries of the self and becoming one with them. Whenever he wants to activate an evocation of an artifact he owns and has used for at least a story he may pay part or the whole essence cost with sorcerous motes instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9774-archangelazrael","name":"ArchangelAzrael","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T11:13:08-08:00","id":772414,"title":"","content":"For a character for an upcoming game, a custom initiation has been brainstormed where the barely intact animating intelligence of a lost first age facility sacrificed itself to form an additional sorcerous soul for a young new Lawgiver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5670-kalad2","name":"kalad2","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T03:08:32-08:00","id":775888,"title":"","content":"Another Initiation. Let me know if people think it's any good. I know someone wanted a blood magic type one...<br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <b>Bargain with Baashael, the Apostle of Blood</b><br /> <br /> You have met with Baashael, the column of blood that seethes in the Market of Rage in Malfeas. The law of the market, and a being without mercy, he has the control of a rare substance in Malfeas, blood. For that reason he is willing to make a pact with one who can spill it for him, in Creation where it is more common. Somehow you have convinced him to spare you from the rage of the place he calls home, even as he teaches you secrets of his blood sorcery. Though be careful, for Baashael is one without mercy or favor, only the law of the Market tempers him.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i>Shaping Rituals</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Blood is the price of power, or so you have learned. You may spill blood of a willing or helpless target that has blood to power your sorcery as part of a Shaping Action. This is not a decisive attack, instead a willing target dictates the maximum number of non-temporary health levels you can you take at no roll. Against an unwilling helpless target you instead use a Shaping roll to determine how many you can take, either separately or as part of the casting of a spell. Each success over their Resolve is one non-temporary health level, as your ritual beats their trying to fight against it. A target that is bound completely immobile or sleeping is treated as Resolve 0. Each non-temporary lethal health level dealt in this manner becomes one sorcerous mote, unless a willling target lets you kill them with it, in which case double the number of motes. These motes last for one week, and can be added to on a first in first out rate, though additional motes into a pool can only be gathered if you deal half the remaining health levels as lethal. If you choose to target yourself with this you are always considered willing. Unless the target is yourself, you must have or be able to stunt lethal damage to use this ritual, or otherwise be able to draw blood.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">The blood craved by the Apostle is there for the taking in some places. You may draw (Essence) motes from already spilled blood as part of a shaping action from any source of blood that is within medium range. No one that has been targeted by a blood ritual that scene may be targetted by this, regardless of if it was from a different ritual and regardless of if they are living or dead. A single body will be exhausted after a single use, whereas a battlefield can fuel your sorcery for a long long time. Living targets need to have their Resolve beaten by your shape sorcery roll in order to draw the motes from them, but the dead have no such protection. Demons with blood fear this power even uninjured, as it allows the sorcerer to draw blood directly from them in the form of motes from their pool. The bodies of the dead and demons can be targetted always when drawing Essence to fuel a control spell. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">(Third Ritual? Maybe base if off Mara's third ritual?)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><i>Other Benefits</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Infernal Nobility</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> (Merit \u2022): Demons recognize the sorcerer as one favored by Baashael. First Circle demons </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">are treated as having a Minor Tie of terrified awe towards her, while Second and Third Circle demons have a positive Minor Tie of respect, or some variation suited to their nature. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Demonic Tattoos:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> Baashael marks those he bargains with in blood, dark red tattoos the same color of blood as himself adorn their bodies in sworls and First Age runes, each person marked differently but always following the flow of blood in their bodies in some manner. Formed of a combination of his own blood and the sorerers, these tattoos are unable to replicated, and all of them grant control over blood. Evocations that the sorcerer unlocks from these affect blood or their own body in some way, allowing manipulation, gathering, and drawing extra power from blood. They may alter the control spells of the sorcerer to incorporate elements of blood or rage, or they can manipulate or change summoned demons into creatures of empowered blood. Evocations that empower the sorcerer's own body always require one of the following bee met to be able to be used: that they be wearing no armor other then that granted by spells or charms with a good amount of the tattoos visible, be covered in blood, or be bleeding.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">(One more merit? Unsure.)</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T06:13:32-08:00","id":775939,"title":"","content":"Any ideas for the 'normal' shaping ritual of Ysyr?<br /> <br /> A society where you are either a sorcerer or a slave has got to have some regulations on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T13:27:31-08:00","id":776175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=775939#post775939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas for the 'normal' shaping ritual of Ysyr?<br /> <br /> A society where you are either a sorcerer or a slave has got to have some regulations on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... it doesn't state that they have a school or similar. Or that it is outright inborn, just the potential to learn sorcery is. Personally I took that perfection thing to be them doing a working after first gaining sorcery to make themselves like that, though I suppose a different shaping method with a low or no cost Merit might be more appropriate. If the sorcery isn't inborn to them, then it would likely be a school type system for those born to parents already in the ruling class. <br /> <br /> Given the society I thought of it as the sorcery is simply a way for the ruling class to keep the slaves in line more, sort of waving it as a carrot 'if you can become a sorcerer you can be one of us' while really only planning on using sorcerers that weren't born into the ruling class only in the military, though sorcerer children of theirs would have full opportunity. This gives the slave society a way to have hope while still keeping it unlikely to have their power broken. In the rare situations where someone does manage to initiate without them it gives them a new military sorcerer, as well as a new shaping ritual for them to study and possibly try to learn to incorporate into their own methods.<br /> <br /> After re-reading the section, I would suggest something that speaks to it being inborn more then taught for the majority of Ys sorcerers I think, which means that my view of it would just be those sorcerers that don't have it inborn would be the ones that are only used in the military. Hmm... not sure the best way to represent that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T15:27:14-08:00","id":776236,"title":"","content":"One of my players very much wants an initiation and ritual that interacts with Martial Arts, but I cannot for the life of me figure out a way for it to work well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T15:27:55-08:00","id":776237,"title":"","content":"Probably the only regulation is &quot;you probably aren't going to learn any sorcery unless one of the existing sorcerer-kings deigns to teach you&quot;. I have a couple half formed ones I've been working on - one where the sorcerer is an debauched alchemist that is basically constantly poisoning themselves to induce visions and for power, another where you're practicing blood magic that I had in mind for two &quot;common&quot; Ysyr initiations. I'll see about polishing them up and posting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T23:31:24-08:00","id":776460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foorish Shamurai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=776236#post776236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players very much wants an initiation and ritual that interacts with Martial Arts, but I cannot for the life of me figure out a way for it to work well.</div> </div> </div> </div><u>Not mine</u> but here is one already made.<a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/foolfuuka/boards/tg/image/1446/13/1446139646146.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://boards.fireden.net/foolfuuka...6139646146.pdf</a> . Its called <b>Enlightenment of the Imperfect lotus</b> and I used it heavily as an inspiration for the BATTLEFORGED ASCENSION (bottom of page 4). Hope that works for you (and that the link works).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9774-archangelazrael","name":"ArchangelAzrael","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T23:41:08-08:00","id":776461,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I agree about Ysyr.<br /> <br /> The city is built on top of broken First Age engines that warp and twist the people. Most are turned into mutants; a small number are turned into sorcerers. Foreigners are banned from entering, lest they learn sorcery.<br /> This would make me think that:<br /> The &quot;sorcerous perfection&quot; is part of what is essentially their mutation.<br /> Their initiation is living on top of Ysyr, not, say, pacting with a demon to gain the power of sorcery. They already have it.<br /> So, I'd say that rituals might be something to do with Ysyr itself, such as meditating in a tower above Ysyr, or perhaps using the blood of Ysyr's natives, or sleeping in soil from Ysyr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T00:05:40-08:00","id":776466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchangelAzrael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=776460#post776460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u>Not mine</u> but here is one already made.<a href=\"https://boards.fireden.net/foolfuuka/boards/tg/image/1446/13/1446139646146.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://boards.fireden.net/foolfuuka...6139646146.pdf</a> . Its called <b>Enlightenment of the Imperfect lotus</b> and I used it heavily as an inspiration for the BATTLEFORGED ASCENSION (bottom of page 4). Hope that works for you (and that the link works).</div> </div> </div> </div>Whaaaaaaaa-<br /> <br /> Brilliant! Thank you so much, I'll look over this with my player straight away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Formerly Exodan","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/715-foorish-shamurai","name":"Foorish Shamurai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T00:23:52-08:00","id":776472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=776461#post776461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I agree about Ysyr.<br /> <br /> The city is built on top of broken First Age engines that warp and twist the people. Most are turned into mutants; a small number are turned into sorcerers. Foreigners are banned from entering, lest they learn sorcery.<br /> This would make me think that:<br /> The &quot;sorcerous perfection&quot; is part of what is essentially their mutation.<br /> Their initiation is living on top of Ysyr, not, say, pacting with a demon to gain the power of sorcery. They already have it.<br /> So, I'd say that rituals might be something to do with Ysyr itself, such as meditating in a tower above Ysyr, or perhaps using the blood of Ysyr's natives, or sleeping in soil from Ysyr.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are quite possible, it's why I gave two readings to how the sorcerous perfection could be. One has it as part of their initiation, similar to how the Demonic Tattoos are part of the Mara initiation. The other has it as them doing a working. <br /> <br /> Curious now, I don't recall the section on Ysyr saying that foreigners are banned from entering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T00:41:40-08:00","id":776476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=775939#post775939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas for the 'normal' shaping ritual of Ysyr?<br /> <br /> A society where you are either a sorcerer or a slave has got to have some regulations on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My ST made a set of rituals and merits for our Dreaming Sea game. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\">Sorcerous Archetype: Sorcerer-King of Ysyr</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You were born and trained on Ysyr, gifted with the power of sorcery and welcomed into their ranks as a Sorcerer-King. Your body is perfectly formed, you may command legions of slaves and lesser thaumaturges according to your whims, and you cloak yourself in Wyld energies. None save the Magnus may place themselves above you, for your blood is Sorcery itself.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Shaping Rituals:</i></span></span><ul><li>Your fingernails are painted with a Wyld-born solution, one for every spell you have mastered, to a maximum of ten. Each fingernail painted in this way grants you a single sorcerous mote per day that can be applied to any spell. Motes applied to your control spell refresh at the end of the scene rather than the day.</li> <li>Your slaves worship you alone, granting you exceptional magical power. You may add your Cult rating to all shape sorcery rolls. The first time you cast your control spell per scene, you add your Cult rating in successes rather than dice.</li> <li>You have made a pact with the Fair Folk for greater power. Once per scene you may consume one of your Intimacies, gaining sorcerous motes equal to its rating, but reducing its rating by one step. Intimacies weakened in this way recover at a rate of one step per week. Casting your control spell does not count against the once per scene limit</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Other Benefits</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perfect Body (Merit ****)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your body is shaped by sorcery, perfect in every way. You gain two successes on all rolls to resist disease and poison, and your Appearance is treated as one higher when comparing against Resolve. Finally, you become immune to Wyld mutation.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Lesser Fuel (Merit ****)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You have learned how to divert the cost of Sorcerous Workings onto your lessers. By sacrificing sentient beings and draining their power, you can reduce the xp cost of Workings. For every 50 being sacrificed, you may reduce the xp cost by 1. Each circle above Terrestrial doubles the required number.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9090-deathsworn","name":"Deathsworn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T01:02:24-08:00","id":776483,"title":"","content":"That's pretty good. I like the powered by slaves one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T20:37:26-08:00","id":778784,"title":"","content":"Dammit! Finally got around to working on the sorcerous initiations I was thinking up, typing them out on an older word processor program I use (I dont wanna pay more money to microsoft). But then, it wouldnt let mesave it and all the stuff I wanted to share got lost. So, I no longer have any to shre. And I hate Windows 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T20:51:38-08:00","id":778788,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of a wuxia / quick draw gunslinger hybrid Initiation for my Night Caste now, to complement his gun fu.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any mechanical ideas for how it would work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T05:35:59-08:00","id":778933,"title":"","content":"So let me try to come up with a few things, so you can tell me what I'm doing horribly (because when was the last time I did something right?).<br /> <br /> <b>Disciple of the Golden Exhalation </b><br /> <br /> In the South, firewands and flame pieces are often viewed as premier weapons of war, owing to the relative ubiquity of firedust. For most people of the desert, the terrifying power of fire at their command is all they need. Some warriors, however, have a more mystical bent, and through intensive study of their weapon, their fuel and their bodies, they can unleash the might of sorcery itself. These occultist disciples often speak of an entity they call only the Golden Exhalation, which they say is the source of firedust -- Ingenious Flame, the god of firedust weapons, often reacts with bemusement at this claim. Regardless of the truth of their words, the spells they can coax out of the mingling of Wyld and elemental fire are undeniable, and most disciples prefer to let their firewands and spells do their talking for them.<br /> <br /> <i>Rituals</i><br /> <br /> It is better to shoot last than it is to shoot first, but the true Disciple strives perfection in all moments of the battle. If the Disciple acts before all his opponents in battle, on his first turn, he can reflexively convert as many Initiative as he wants to gain sorcerous motes on a one-on-one basis. This does not affect his place in the acting order on the first round, but it does normally affect it in any subsequent rounds. Sorcerous motes received in this fashion have to be used towards the first spell the sorcerer casts, and cannot be divided between spells. Any sorcerous motes received in this fashion fade once the battle is over. If the Disciple uses the sorcerous motes to cast his control spell before he is crashed, he can add a bonus to the spell's damage equal to half the sorcerous motes he received in this fashion.<br /> <br /> There is power in the purity of form when the flames of battle rage around, and the Disciple knows how to power his spells through his graceful movements. Whenever the Disciple receives a stunt bonus in combat when he makes an attack or uses a gambit with a weapon bearing the Flame tag, or uses the Rush or Disengage actions, he gains one sorcerous mote. In addition, he can convert bonus successes received from such stunts into sorcerous motes one a one-on-one basis. These sorcerous motes can be used to cast any spell The sorcerer can receive a maximum of (Wits + Occult) sorcerous motes per conflict in this fashion. If the sorcerer receives sufficient sorcerous motes to cast his control spell as a result of a stunt, he can immediately reset his combat action for the round and use it to cast his control spell, if applicable.<br /> <br /> Firedust is more than just a source of ammunition. It is born of the union of the chaotic energies of the Wyld and the pure inferno of the Elemental Pole of Fire. The sorcerer who follows the Golden Exhalation can disperse such a volatile union into nothingness, feeding on the energies released from the act. Once per scene, as a part of a shape sorcery action, the Disciple can sacrifice any firedust he has loaded in a flame weapon to add (relevant combat ability, generally Archery or Martial Arts) non-Charm dice to his shape sorcery roll. If he is gathering sorcerous motes to cast his control spell, he can do this as many times as he wants as long as he has a weapon loaded with firedust available, but any such sacrifices after the first in a scene count as dice added by Charms.<br /> <br /> <i>Other Benefits</i><br /> <br /> The Ascendant Flame (Merit 2): The Disciple is considered to have the one-dot version of the Quick Draw benefit with regards to any flame weapons she wields, regardless of the Ability used. In addition, the Disciple can use two sorcerous motes (either unaligned or gained for a specific spell) to fire any flame weapon she is wielding that is not already loaded with firedust or another fuel. This allows the sorcerer to shoot without needing a source of ammunition or spending a miscellaneous action to reload, but it does not remove the Slow tag or allow the Disciple to get sorcerous motes from ammunition created in this manner.<br /> <br /> The Resplendent Flame (Merit 4): The Disciple reveals her true glory when surrounded by flames of conflict, whether it is to exacerbate it or to quench it. When the scene the sorcerer is in contains sufficient fire (a single candle does not count, but a hundred candles probably will), she gains (Occult / 2, rounded down) bonus dice to all attempts at social influence, and one bonus die to all physical or mental actions targeting another character (for clarification, these count as dice added by Charms).<br /> <br /> The Descendent Flame (Merit 2): Having been purified through the ignition of battle and the conflagration of the Golden Exhalation, the Disciple has little to fear from the least flames of Creation. Use the rules for Unburnt Majesty (EX3, p. 468) to reflect this.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For what it's worth, a mortal using this initiation would be considered to have a bonus dice cap of (Occult).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":8891,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","user":"Khantalas","date":". 12-03-2015, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T08:28:19-08:00","id":779024,"title":"","content":"<b>The Broken-Winged Crane</b><br /> <br /> For quite some time, you've been dreaming of a book that is not in your library when you awake. But these dreams feel less like dreams, and more like memories. Indeed, as you begin to try to copy down your dream-visions into notes, to make sense of them, you get a rushing sense of deja vu, like you are living out your premonition, forging that memory now that you have already experienced.<br /> <br /> As you work, the memories become clearer, and you recall without sleeping what you will have written. Perhaps not perfectly, but how could it not be, when you only can remember what you've read?<br /> <br /> At some point, no less than five days after you began to have these dreams, you will encounter a copy of this book in another's possession, and learn it is titled <i>The Broken-Winged Crane</i>. You may acquire it for yourself, to better finish your own copy or simply to abandon the effort, now that you have your own. Or you may simply borrow it, or steal moments to read from it - these moments are when you are most thoroughly enmeshed in the deja vu, as if THIS is when you forge the memories from which you wrote your own (perhaps not yet complete, and perhaps not 100% accurate) copy.<br /> <br /> In any event, the book, your study of it and your transcription of it, have taught you the underpinnings of reality, and how distorted what SEEMS to be is from what IS. And from these twisted differences can you draw power to shape the warps and cracks therein.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> <br /> * The future's true blasphemies are a source of power, but the difference between a prophecy and a promise is very fine. When you write a future event in your copy of the book (making it more complete from memory of future events), and make public your prophecy of that event which is to come in no more than five days' time, you gain 3 sorcerous motes at the start of each scene, which may only be used on spells and workings shaped specifically to bring this prophecy to pass. If the prophecy fails to come to pass, you gain a Derangement deemed appropriate by the Storyteller as your mind fractures, trying to reconcile the truth you know your words contained with the lies Creation presents to you.<br /> <br /> * <i>The Broken-Winged Crane</i> contains encyclopedic knowledge on the summoning of the denizens of Malfeas. When casting any spell involving demons, you gain an extra sorcerous mote with every Shape Sorcery roll. These motes do not fade until the end of the scene, even if you're forced to abandon the Shaping for extended periods. If Demon of the First Circle is your Control spell, the demons called by it will serve you for five days even if you fail to bind them, even if you don't bother with the proper binding circles.<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> <i>Walk the Desert on Broken Wings (*-**) </i>You have learned from the tome you write how to traverse to a mystical city across an endless silver desert, inhabited by beings of wonder and terror and wherein things strange and marvelous can be obtained and learned. The trip either way always takes five days from wherever you set out, and is not without its own perils. For one dot, you know the way, but are a stranger without protections you do not bring with you when you arrive. For two dots, you also know the local customs and present yourself in a manner which receives a certain measure of respect from the denizens of that city. While it does not wholly protect you, you are as safe there as if you were in a major city in Creation, and receive no special molestation for your strange, vulnerable, human appearance.<br /> <br /> <i>The Scarlet Bargain (*-*****)</i> You have, in your copy of the book, the instructions for making a bargain for long life, but at the end of your life, you will be required to complete a task of commensurate worth to the extension of your life. The longer your life has been, the greater the task to which you must agree. The first dot doubles your lifespan, restoring youth and vigor immediately and preserving it until the time added by the pact is over...at which point you will feel age creep upon you once again. The second and third dots add this time again, each. The fourth dot preserves your youth and vigor for the entire time, extending your life for an additional century beyond the others before your death is brought about at an agreed-upon time for you to begin your posthumous task. The fifth dot grants true eternal life...but the piper must still be paid his due, and an agreed-upon task that will last the rest of your eternity (or until you are robbed of it by unnatural death) will begin at an agreed-upon time. Usually immediately, but sometimes with a grace period. Whatever the task, be it &quot;marrying a third circle demon&quot; or &quot;pushing a boulder to the peak of Qaf,&quot; it will be forever, and will have implications greater than you probably know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:18:36-08:00","id":779105,"title":"","content":"I really dig the Broken Wing Crane one. The demon summoning ritual is clever. The prophecy ritual feels off somehow. Small benefit for a potentially rough drawback. Thematically very cool though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T11:25:05-08:00","id":779114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=779105#post779105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dig the Broken Wing Crane one. The demon summoning ritual is clever. The prophecy ritual feels off somehow. Small benefit for a potentially rough drawback. Thematically very cool though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it. I figured the most infamous book in the setting deserved an initiation.<br /> <br /> I agree on the prophecy one. I was struggling with it. I am open to suggestions for replacement or to make it better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T16:07:37-08:00","id":779343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=779114#post779114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad you like it. I figured the most infamous book in the setting deserved an initiation.<br /> <br /> I agree on the prophecy one. I was struggling with it. I am open to suggestions for replacement or to make it better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to start you can either buff the mote gain (maybe all sorcery actions, though that seems really powerful), or you can lower the derangement (by making it temporary). If you went with the temporary derangement maybe make it last one week per day in advance that you told your prophecy (this five days in advance would be 5 weeks, and 1 day would be 1 week), possibly with a discount of one day per sorcery action you took to aid it (though that might be too much book keeping).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:36:16-08:00","id":779664,"title":"","content":"I would instead heighten the severity of the Derangement. Make the Derangement supply the afflicted Sorcerer with a 2nd Limit Trigger (or first one, if not a Solar) befitting the theme of a certain Derangement, and make it last for Five Days, keeping with the theme.<br /> <br /> Also since I'm already typing a post I want to say that the Broken Winged Crane Initiation is awesome as fuck and I'm stealing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:37:41-08:00","id":779665,"title":"","content":"So can anyone tell me why exactly my initiation is horrible, and how I can fix it so my players can play with it this week?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:47:26-08:00","id":779672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=779665#post779665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can anyone tell me why exactly my initiation is horrible, and how I can fix it so my players can play with it this week?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Besides firewands really not being my cup of tea, I think the initiation is fine. The only beef I have is with the Resplendant Flame (oooo) Merit; I'm a bit torn on that. The bonus seems a bit generic to me, but only experience will tell how often it'll come up. If you find that your players are drawing on this very often, it maybe needs some kind of cost added to it.<br /> On the other hand it basically duplicates the effects of a Charm with almost no prerequisites and costs just as much, so it's probably fine.<br /> <br /> All in all, if I were the ST, I would allow that initiation, I see no overt problems with it. And I like the way you fluffed it, with again, a side note, that I really don't like flame pieces and firewands. Which probably means that your initiation is even better than you think, because I still kind of like it, even though I dislike the theme. So it's probably even really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:19:40-08:00","id":779691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=779665#post779665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can anyone tell me why exactly my initiation is horrible, and how I can fix it so my players can play with it this week?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it, although a character with a lot of initiative boosters can use it to <i>very</i> easily pop off something like FotBR at high damage at the start of the round. (Using the first ritual.)<br /> <br /> I wouldn't bother actually mucking with it unless you see someone doing that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T14:38:02-08:00","id":791800,"title":"","content":"Trying another crack at the prophecy shaping ritual:<br /> <br /> * The future's true blasphemies are a source of power, but the difference between a prophecy and a promise is very fine. When you write a future event in your copy of the book (making it more complete from memory of future events), and make public your prophecy of that event which is to come in no more than five days' time, you cast spells without having to first gather the sorcerous motes as long as the spell is directly applicable to bringing to pass your prophecy. You may perform the mote-gathering actions at any later point before the prophecy is completed, and if the prophecy comes to pass, it will turn out that any motes you have not yet gathered were retro-actively accumulated by the turning of events leading up to its fruition. If your prophecy is proven false, however, the consequences are dire. For the next five days after the falsehood of your prophecy is proven, you must gather as many motes as you had not yet paid back before taking even mundane action, or the action fails on a success, and botches on a failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T15:54:11-08:00","id":791832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=779024#post779024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* <i>The Broken-Winged Crane</i> contains encyclopedic knowledge on the summoning of the denizens of Malfeas. When casting any spell involving demons, you gain an extra sorcerous mote with every Shape Sorcery roll. These motes do not fade until the end of the scene, even if you're forced to abandon the Shaping for extended periods. If Demon of the First Circle is your Control spell, the demons called by it will serve you for five days even if you fail to bind them, even if you don't bother with the proper binding circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Summoning demons is usually something you do in private, in safety, and with some leisure. While the subsidiary benefit is nice, that should probably just be homebrewed into Demon of the First Circle directly. I'd instead consider something like, you can draw sorcerous motes from a summoned demon within the same range band at a steady pace, or a one-time large burst that will consume the demon entirely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The future's true blasphemies are a source of power, but the difference between a prophecy and a promise is very fine. When you write a future event in your copy of the book (making it more complete from memory of future events), and make public your prophecy of that event which is to come in no more than five days' time, you cast spells without having to first gather the sorcerous motes as long as the spell is directly applicable to bringing to pass your prophecy. You may perform the mote-gathering actions at any later point before the prophecy is completed, and if the prophecy comes to pass, it will turn out that any motes you have not yet gathered were retro-actively accumulated by the turning of events leading up to its fruition. If your prophecy is proven false, however, the consequences are dire. For the next five days after the falsehood of your prophecy is proven, you must gather as many motes as you had not yet paid back before taking even mundane action, or the action fails on a success, and botches on a failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Free spells for five days based on a big risk of ruining your next five days is the kind of extreme balancing act that I don't think is great for the system. In particular, it's kinda hard to screw up when you can just spam every spell you know for most of a week.<br /> <br /> Maybe instead, when you write down a prophecy scheduled exactly five days into the future, you gain a Defining Intimacy towards bringing the prophecy to pass and shaping actions benefit from that Intimacy as if they were social, gaining the usual +4/-3. Completing the prophecy immediately grants, say, 10 sorcerous motes that persist for (Essence) days and are nonstackable. Failing the prophecy causes you to lose instead of gain Willpower each morning for the next five days.<br /> <br /> The persistent issue is how to define what's suitable as a prophecy. &quot;In five days, I will execute this prisoner that I've already captured&quot; or &quot;in five days, I will make another prophecy&quot; aren't exactly ideal game-states. Needs a clear way of communicating that the event should be initially out of your control and significant enough to pose a challenge to at least a heroic mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1075-kingdom-of-one","name":"Kingdom of One","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T23:11:26-08:00","id":792003,"title":"","content":"Good call on the prophecy needing clarification of what &quot;qualifies.&quot; I like some of the ideas in there, too. I'll try again later. I am less enthused by the ideas on the demon one, though I understand the concerns raised, so I'll give it a bit more thought, too.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T22:19:25-08:00","id":792566,"title":"","content":"First off: Hi, I'm new to this forum, and fairly new to Exalted, starting my first third edition game in early January. I did study 2E pretty extensively, but never got the chance to play it except in a single rather short one-shot.<br /> <br /> I've been spending the past couple of weeks tinkering with my character, a Dawn caste sorcerer-general, including his custom artifact + sorcerous initiation combo which, upon finding this thread, I decided to share with you guys for help with fleshing it out.<br /> <br /> <b>The Demonblade</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The idea is that he has this daiklave that he took from a barbarian warlord (outcaste DB or exigent maybe) he defeated in battle. When he attuned to the blade, a voice started whispering into his mind, offering him power. It claimed to be a demon, imprisoned within the daiklave by a solar in the First Age. In fact, the demon went on, that solar was the previous incarnation of my character's exaltation, and he bound him there so that he might seek out the <i>next</i> incarnation of his essence and teach him sorcery, thereby preserving his most valuable tool between reincarnations. Whether this is <i>actually true</i> is up to my ST to decide, I just assume it will be interesting either way.<br /> <br /> The daiklave itself is a red jade leaf-shaped double-edged daiklave, inlaid with oricalchum Old Realm runes spelling out its name. The blade is patterned like folded (Damascus/wootz) steel, and when held by an attuned wielder, the pattern seems to shift slowly. The hilt is solid oricalchum set with emeralds, and green-dyed leather is wrapped around the grip. It does not exhibit any obvious outward signs of being possessed.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Ritual</b><br /> The demon thirsts eternally, and drinks eagerly whenever the daiklave draws blood. Indeed, blood staining the blade seems to quickly seep into it and vanish. When the sorcerer makes a decisive attack with the daiklave to an opponent that bleeds, he gains sorcerous motes equal to the health levels inflicted as damage. Withering attacks against battlegroups instead grant one sorcerous mote for every three points of post-soak damage. Sorcerous motes granted by this ritual last until the end of the scene and are technically stored in the daiklave rather than the sorcerer himself. As such, they may only be used if the sorcerer still has the blade within reach (it does not need to be unsheathed). Only up to (Sorcerer\u2019s Essence + Permanent Willpower) sorcerous motes may be stored in the blade. When the sword is holding any sorcerous motes in this way, flames seem to dance inside the emeralds adorning the hilt.<br /> <br /> I didn't create any custom merits yet (being new to the system, homebrewing seems kind of intimidating) but I did snag The Burning Name, mainly because being able to throw fire around at will seems awfully useful and the kind of thing a sorcerer should be able to do and a demon able to teach.<br /> <br /> The things I need help with:<ul><li>The identity and name of the demon, name of the daiklave (note that it was created before the demon was bound to it)</li> <li>Does the shaping ritual I wrote seem balanced?</li> <li>More shaping rituals</li> <li>Associated custom merits</li> <li>Evocations for the daiklave (these should probably go in a separate thread, which I'll gladly set up with some more info if anyone expresses interest in this part)</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","name":"Swooper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10437_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T23:33:37-08:00","id":792618,"title":"","content":"@Swooper: I like the concept. Not sure if it should gain motes from both decisive and withering attacks. Otherwise looks like a good start","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T09:41:46-08:00","id":792759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=792618#post792618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Swooper: I like the concept. Not sure if it should gain motes from both decisive and withering attacks. Otherwise looks like a good start</div> </div> </div> </div>Only withering attacks on battlegroups, because you can't decisive strike them. It made sense that the demon be able to drink blood from soldiers too, I put in the 1/3 rate because losing magnitude isn't just direct casualties. Maybe it should be 1/2 or 1/5 or something, not sure how it plays out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","name":"Swooper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10437_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T23:14:15-08:00","id":792962,"title":"","content":"I have just created a new subsection for Sorcerous Initiations in my <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/home:home\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3E wiki</a>. Who would be okay with me using their material to test the submission form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:53:53-08:00","id":793011,"title":"","content":"When I finally pist some, feel free to steal it<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T06:38:19-08:00","id":793061,"title":"","content":"A constructed langauge, and possibly an affinity for Chosen of Venus , assuming their design keeps certain elements this edition. Although this may cross into Loom of Fate territory, being able to take a ritual to construct imaginary phenomena based on the constructed langage too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10320-altaristide","name":"Altaristide","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T18:15:23-08:00","id":793871,"title":"","content":"So I've been brainstorming more shaping rituals for my demonblade sorcerous archetype. Here's one fairly complete:<ul><li>The magic taught by the demon is dark and insidious, twisting the sorcerer to slowly turn his love to hate. By focusing his will, the sorcerer can reduce the level of one of his positive ties by one (a minor tie goes away completely), gaining (Essence x Intimacy level) sorcerous motes instead. When the sorcerer next gains Willpower from resting, he must roll Wits+Integrity (difficulty 5 \u2013 Intimacy level) to remember the intimacy again. If succeeds, the intimacy returns to the previous level, else it stays as it is. If the intimacy was a minor one, it is instead replaced with a minor tie of hate towards the same subject. The sorcerer may use the motes at any time until he sleeps, and may only keep motes from one reduced intimacy.</li> </ul><br /> It kind of scares me how destructive this one is... Not sure I want my character to go down this path. The mechanics on this might not be right, the intention was that it's harder to lose stronger ties, but as soon as they start to go down it becomes a slippery slope to hate. I think what I wrote probably just ends up rewarding only using your Defining intimacies (more motes for them, less risk of losing them)... hmm...<br /> <br /> Another idea I had was to take the ritual from Mara where you get motes from unrequited love, but change it to either hate and/or fear. Maybe those ties are easier to build than unrequited love via Presence, especially with the Dawn anima bonus? <br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> PS. J\u00fcrgen, feel free to use mine when it's ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","name":"Swooper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10437_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T20:40:09-08:00","id":793924,"title":"","content":"Feel free to use any of the versions I've got up in this thread. I'm still trying to come up with better (more balanced and interesting and usable) shaping rituals, but I don't mind you using what's there for your wiki at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T20:44:20-08:00","id":793925,"title":"","content":"Wrote up this hate-fueled alternate version of Mara's thing:<br /> <br /> The sorcerer\u2019s has learnt to draw power from his negative emotions. When he takes a shape sorcery action with the intention to harm (directly or indirectly) targets of one of his appropriately negative ties (hate, anger, loathing etc.), he gains sorcerous motes equal to the strength of the tie to fuel the casting of that spell. In the case of a spell who might harm more than one target of separate negative ties, he may draw motes from all of them. The sorcerer may draw up to ten motes per scene with this ritual.<br /> <br /> Gods this character is accidentally turning much darker than I intended.<br /> <br /> Side note: Does it bug anyone else that shaping rituals aren't named? I want to be able to write which ones I know concisely on my character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","name":"Swooper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10437_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T22:26:13-08:00","id":793962,"title":"","content":"I had a pretty cool premise for one.<br /> <br /> The idea basically came because I had the idea of a character who's learned sorcery from Plentimon, the God of Gambling.<br /> I also had a vague idea of being able to use an artifact set of dice/playing cards in order to build sorcerous motes while you gamble with them.<br /> <br /> If anyone who's better with the system could build something with this, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Oh boys! Look what I got here!&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, where the Dynast women at?&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/814-dreamking89","name":"dreamking89","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T10:35:04-08:00","id":794266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dreamking89</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=793962#post793962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a pretty cool premise for one.<br /> <br /> The idea basically came because I had the idea of a character who's learned sorcery from Plentimon, the God of Gambling.<br /> I also had a vague idea of being able to use an artifact set of dice/playing cards in order to build sorcerous motes while you gamble with them.<br /> <br /> If anyone who's better with the system could build something with this, go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. My immediate idea for this is:<br /> <br /> When you have built up some sorcerous motes for a spell through either a regular shape sorcery action or another shaping ritual, you can roll your magic dice or draw a card or something and make a Wits+... wait, what Ability is used for gambling? Larceny? Yeah, so Wits+Larceny, difficulty something like the number of motes you have gathered already. If you succeed, you double your motes, if you fail you lose them all. Usable once per scene.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","name":"Swooper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10437_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:10:29-08:00","id":797108,"title":"","content":"Here's a quick question: Can you purchase merits that are mechanically identical to one in a different sorcerous initiation, but change the fluff to make it thematically appropriate? I think I read that somewhere, but I can't recall where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T18:18:09-08:00","id":797114,"title":"","content":"Well, considering the current sorcerous initiations are suggestions more than anything, why couldn't you?<br /> <br /> Hell, I just offered a player Unburnt Majesty and the Burning Name to represent his character's divine heritage, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T13:05:18-08:00","id":797478,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's explicit in the rules, but the sidebar on page 471 indicates that you're expected to refluff the sorcerous initiations and mix and match the merits and rituals to fit your game.<br /> <br /> Side note: Would really appreciate feedback on my demonblade stuff above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","user":"Swooper","date":". 12-31-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","name":"Swooper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10437_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T23:25:30-08:00","id":801181,"title":"","content":"So, I've been thinking this week about a sorcerous initiation based on the powers of stone. This is still a work in progress, and I'll post it to the wiki when it's done. I don't like the name yet.<br /> <br /> <b>The Flowing Stillness of the Stone</b><br /> <br /> The sorceress has been enlightened by meditating upon the nature of stone. It is widely known that stone is permanent, immutable, and as unchanging as the very laws of creation. Yet, stone flows subtly, moving and changing through the earth. Stone is eroded by the winds and the waves, it is cracked by the roots of trees, and it can be melted by flame, Indeed, the unchanging, permanent nature of stone can be changed even by mortal hands. Such is the nature of creation; that which seems permanent, immutable and fundamental may yet be transformed.<br /> <br /> The rituals of this initiation embody the nature of stone. They are slow moving, powerful, and permanent. But their power is tempered by their inflexible nature. The weight of a mountain is enough to crush an entire nation, yet the mountain is helpless before stonemasons and their chisels.<br /> <br /> <b>Rituals:</b><br /> <br /> Essence flows through the earth, slowly and imperceptibly, and when the flow of this essence hits a snarl it begins to crystallise, transforming base stone into precious stones and jewels. The sorceress has learned to draw upon the essence contained in the treasures of the earth. At any time, she may consume the essence contained in jewels and semiprecious stones in short range, gaining (Resources value of jewels + Essence) sorcerous motes. The jewels are utterly consumed by this process, turning to chalk, sandstone, glass or even powdery dust. The sorceress may choose which jewels to consume, and if the opportunity presents itself she may even draw power from an enemy's treasures. The sorceress may also draw up to essence sorcerous motes from earth elementals and other spirits of the earth. When casting her control spell, jewels are only reduced to a lesser form, losing 1 dot of their resources value.<br /> <br /> <i>This is modelled on the ifrit power, however I've increased the mote gain to reflect the the rather more permanent cost of consuming wealth.</i><br /> <br /> The stone is still and immutable, and the flow of essence through the earth is directed and constrained. The sorceress may harness this power by inscribing a great mandala into the stone. First, she must spend a month studying the flow of essence through the earth around a certain site. She then choses one of her spells, and carves into the earth an occult diagram to direct essence into the shape of the spell. This is an Intelligence + Occult roll, difficulty five. Whenever she is standing at the centre of this diagram, she may gain (essence + extra successes) sorcerous motes to cast that spell. This diagram must usually be cut directly into the stone of the earth, rather than bricks, cobblestones, stone slabs, or other artificial such surfaces. A well constructed diagram may also aid summoning spells, granting (Essence) dice to the binding roll of these spells.<br /> <br /> <i>While the power of these diagrams is significant, they are limited. While a sufficiently capable sorceress might construct a diagram sufficient to cast &quot;death of obsidian butterflies&quot; nearly every turn, she is exceptionally vulnerable while she does so. She stands in the middle of a clear stone diagram, with no cover, leaving her vulnerable to hidden snipers or stealthy assassins. Should an enemy approach her, she is limited in her capacity to dodge. Enemies might choose to wait her out, forcing her to come to them, and and savvy enemies might even disrupt the geomancy of the local area until her diagram no longer functions.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Merit: Follow the Flow of the Earth. \u00b0\u00b0\u00b0</b><br /> The sorceress has gained a deep understanding of the flow of essence in the earth, and can feel the subtle, timeless currents that run through the stone. She recognises a curve in the grain of stone that speaks to a passage beneath it, and the subtle distortions that suggest the presence of a vein of ore. May roll intelligence + occult to find geological features (such as caves or passages leading in her preferred direction), or to prospect for jewels, ores, or magical materials. The storyteller should bear in mind that such treasures remain scarce; while the sorceress might be able to follow the currents of stone to find a deposit of jade on the other side of a small kingdom, she is unlikely to find more nearby.<br /> <br /> <b>Merit: Kin to the Bedrock. \u00b0\u00b0</b><br /> Through her meditations on the nature of stone, the sorceress has taken the essence of earth into her very self. Creatures of stone, such as earth elementals and spirits associated with the earth, recognise her as their kin and gain a minor positive tie towards her. The nature of this tie depends on the spirit. Least gods and minor earth elementals might feel awe, love, or filial piety, more powerful beings might have a tie of respect, solidarity, or loving jealousy, and ancient creatures such as the gemlords might have a tie of proud parental indulgence, or perhaps more possessive feelings. Even the least forms of stone accept her as their sister and welcome her; she treats damage from falling onto stone surfaces as though she had fallen one less range band, and other sources of environmental damage from stone are similarly reduced.<br /> <br /> <br /> The sorceress has gained a deep understanding of the flow of essence in the earth, and can feel the subtle, timeless currents that run through the stone. She recognises a curve in the grain of stone that speaks to a passage beneath it, and the subtle distortions that suggest the presence of a vein of ore. May roll intelligence + occult to find geological features (such as caves or passages leading in her preferred direction), or to prospect for jewels, ores, or magical materials. The storyteller should bear in mind that such treasures remain scarce; while the sorceress might be able to follow the currents of stone to find a deposite of jade on the other side of a small kingdom, she is unlikely to find more nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10317,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10317-skina-stonedottir","user":"Skina Stonedottir","date":".  Added Kin to the Earth merit 01-05-2016, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10317-skina-stonedottir","name":"Skina Stonedottir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10317_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T23:39:11-08:00","id":801187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Swooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=793925#post793925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrote up this hate-fueled alternate version of Mara's thing:<br /> <br /> The sorcerer\u2019s has learnt to draw power from his negative emotions. When he takes a shape sorcery action with the intention to harm (directly or indirectly) targets of one of his appropriately negative ties (hate, anger, loathing etc.), he gains sorcerous motes equal to the strength of the tie to fuel the casting of that spell. In the case of a spell who might harm more than one target of separate negative ties, he may draw motes from all of them. The sorcerer may draw up to ten motes per scene with this ritual.<br /> <br /> Gods this character is accidentally turning much darker than I intended.<br /> <br /> Side note: Does it bug anyone else that shaping rituals aren't named? I want to be able to write which ones I know concisely on my character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder about this from a balance perspective; mara's power is difficult to leverage because you need to spend time building unrequited love in the people likely to be around you; it's much easier for you to build hate in yourself something that it is to instil feelings in others.<br /> <br /> I say this knowing I've just posted the most overpowered initiation I could think of\u2026<br /> <br /> Also,yes. NAMES. WHY NO NAMES?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10317-skina-stonedottir","name":"Skina Stonedottir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10317_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T03:17:12-08:00","id":801257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Swooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=792566#post792566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off: Hi, I'm new to this forum, and fairly new to Exalted, starting my first third edition game in early January. I did study 2E pretty extensively, but never got the chance to play it except in a single rather short one-shot.<br /> <br /> I've been spending the past couple of weeks tinkering with my character, a Dawn caste sorcerer-general, including his custom artifact + sorcerous initiation combo which, upon finding this thread, I decided to share with you guys for help with fleshing it out.<br /> <br /> <b>The Demonblade</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The idea is that he has this daiklave that he took from a barbarian warlord (outcaste DB or exigent maybe) he defeated in battle. When he attuned to the blade, a voice started whispering into his mind, offering him power. It claimed to be a demon, imprisoned within the daiklave by a solar in the First Age. In fact, the demon went on, that solar was the previous incarnation of my character's exaltation, and he bound him there so that he might seek out the <i>next</i> incarnation of his essence and teach him sorcery, thereby preserving his most valuable tool between reincarnations. Whether this is <i>actually true</i> is up to my ST to decide, I just assume it will be interesting either way.<br /> <br /> The daiklave itself is a red jade leaf-shaped double-edged daiklave, inlaid with oricalchum Old Realm runes spelling out its name. The blade is patterned like folded (Damascus/wootz) steel, and when held by an attuned wielder, the pattern seems to shift slowly. The hilt is solid oricalchum set with emeralds, and green-dyed leather is wrapped around the grip. It does not exhibit any obvious outward signs of being possessed.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Ritual</b><br /> The demon thirsts eternally, and drinks eagerly whenever the daiklave draws blood. Indeed, blood staining the blade seems to quickly seep into it and vanish. When the sorcerer makes a decisive attack with the daiklave to an opponent that bleeds, he gains sorcerous motes equal to the health levels inflicted as damage. Withering attacks against battlegroups instead grant one sorcerous mote for every three points of post-soak damage. Sorcerous motes granted by this ritual last until the end of the scene and are technically stored in the daiklave rather than the sorcerer himself. As such, they may only be used if the sorcerer still has the blade within reach (it does not need to be unsheathed). Only up to (Sorcerer\u2019s Essence + Permanent Willpower) sorcerous motes may be stored in the blade. When the sword is holding any sorcerous motes in this way, flames seem to dance inside the emeralds adorning the hilt.<br /> <br /> I didn't create any custom merits yet (being new to the system, homebrewing seems kind of intimidating) but I did snag The Burning Name, mainly because being able to throw fire around at will seems awfully useful and the kind of thing a sorcerer should be able to do and a demon able to teach.<br /> <br /> The things I need help with:<ul><li>The identity and name of the demon, name of the daiklave (note that it was created before the demon was bound to it)</li> <li>Does the shaping ritual I wrote seem balanced?</li> <li>More shaping rituals</li> <li>Associated custom merits</li> <li>Evocations for the daiklave (these should probably go in a separate thread, which I'll gladly set up with some more info if anyone expresses interest in this part)</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, although I wonder if it might end up being overpowered in play; I haven't tested the new combat rules much so I'm not sure how much lethal damage a sorcerer might be expected to deal over the course of combat, but if you're garnering twenty sorcerous motes over a battle I wonder if it might be unbalanced, at least without some kind of drawback or limit (eg: sorcerous motes may only be used for spells that directly deal violence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10317-skina-stonedottir","name":"Skina Stonedottir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10317_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:05:13-08:00","id":801286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Swooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=794266#post794266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. My immediate idea for this is:<br /> <br /> When you have built up some sorcerous motes for a spell through either a regular shape sorcery action or another shaping ritual, you can roll your magic dice or draw a card or something and make a Wits+... wait, what Ability is used for gambling? Larceny? Yeah, so Wits+Larceny, difficulty something like the number of motes you have gathered already. If you succeed, you double your motes, if you fail you lose them all. Usable once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the idea of gambling your motes. Clearly, this is the initiation used by the Exigent of Plentimon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10317-skina-stonedottir","name":"Skina Stonedottir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10317_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T09:30:41-08:00","id":801452,"title":"","content":"I don't have the mental energy for this right now. But in one of my previous games, I had a human thaumaturgic mercenary named Third-Eye Gamal, so named because he had bound a fire elemental directly in to his third-eye chakra and in so doing merged the two of them in to a single more potent entity. Any similar spiritual symbiosis/parasitosis initiation based on permanently joining with a spiritual force to become a sorcerer would be interesting.<br /> <br /> Monsters are mostly magic, and humans are mostly water, etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/587-kukla","name":"Kukla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T04:01:10-08:00","id":801929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=801452#post801452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the mental energy for this right now. But in one of my previous games, I had a human thaumaturgic mercenary named Third-Eye Gamal, so named because he had bound a fire elemental directly in to his third-eye chakra and in so doing merged the two of them in to a single more potent entity. Any similar spiritual symbiosis/parasitosis initiation based on permanently joining with a spiritual force to become a sorcerer would be interesting.<br /> <br /> Monsters are mostly magic, and humans are mostly water, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If one of his Merits is not going to Sparky Sparky Boom Man's forehead-cannon, I'll... be slightly dissapointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T12:23:45-08:00","id":803927,"title":"","content":"I have the base for a initiation for a player raised by ghosts in Sajin, still need to flesh it out and get a third ritual. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dead Remembrances</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Among the dead in Sajan there are thousands of years of sorcerous knowledge. Unfortunately the shades can not cast the spells they knew in life. The caster has listened to their stories and methods and has gleaned the intricacies of spell casting from the dead and how to fear those who use Necromancy and serve the Neverborn. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Has the following effects</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Once a day the caster can make a prayer and burned offering to an undead teacher. The ghost gives the Solar some arcane lost knowledge. The caster gains motes equal to the strength of the intimacy of the teacher plus the level of stunt. These motes stay with the Solar untill he uses this ability again. The motes count double for control spells.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-The ancient dead try to deal with Necromancy and servants of the Void. They hone their senses to sense hatred and oblivion and teach it to their students. When joining battle with Undead or servants of oblivion (Deathknights, Specteres, Nephracks, Deathlords etc) the caster gains the opponents essence +2 motes to be used on sorcery. The caster does get a measure of the of the power they are up against, although a being using supernatural stealth does not ping this ability. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-The caster has no negative modifiers for counterspelling or recognizing Necromancy. (kind of iffy right now because Necromancy does not have any rules)</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deathtalker *:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You are marked by death and the underworld, ghosts have a minor tie of respect to the player. Ghost see someone who could help them and someone they could trust. Unfortunately servants of Oblivion can see this as well. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Living with Death***: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You are used to living and studying the dead. Your body becomes accustomed to the feeling of death, you can respire motes in a Shadowland like it was normal creation. </span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/363-muscadomestica","name":"MuscaDomestica","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-09T09:10:49-08:00","id":804494,"title":"","content":"<b>The <span style=\"color:#417394\">Salinan</span> Working</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In the First Age, the idealistic sorceress Salina and her students convinced the Solar Deliberative to permit the embedding of sorcerous knowledge in various \u201ccaches\u201d around Creation, such as with spirits and elementals, or concealed in patterns of light and shadow on a forest floor, reflections of sunlight on a pond at certain times of day, and more beside. But Salina did more than this: she and her students embedded into the structure of Creation a guaranteed path to sorcerous initiation, open to anyone with the knowledge and determination instead of being guarded by corruptible academies or inimical creatures such as rakshasa or demons. But being an idealist, she wanted to be sure that those followed her path were at least decent people, not aspiring tyrants and warlords. So it was that her working included many trials intended to either eliminate or enlighten the unsuitable, and teaches shaping rituals based in the simple things Salina valued before all others: love, care, and respect for Creation and its inhabitants. You have followed the clues Salina and her students wove into Creation, and gained both insight and a measure of enlightenment along with sorcerous knowledge.</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Shaping Rituals</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">A </span></span><span style=\"color:#417394\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Salinan</span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> sorceror can draw strength from the bonds of family and friendship. Whenever she takes a shape sorcery action while within medium range of a character with a mutual Tie of love, friendship, or a similar emotion towards him, he may reap additional sorcerous motes equal to that Intimacy\u2019s value (for example, four motes from a Defining Tie). A given Intimacy can only be tapped for motes in this fashion once per day, and the sorcerer cannot harvest power from unreciprocated feeling. Normally he may only draw upon one Intimacy to fuel the casting of a spell, but he may draw power from any available Intimacies when casting a control spell. He cannot draw more than ten sorcerous motes per scene with this ritual.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">As a steward of Creation, tending it and inhabitants strengthens the sorceror both emotionally and spiritually. A scene spent in tending to the wellbeing of an aspect of Creation allows the sorceror to roll (Intelligence+Occult) and harvest a number of sorcerous motes equal to the successes rolled, plus the value of any relevant Intimacy he holds toward it. These motes last for one day, and a given aspect or action can only be tended to once a day. No more than ten sorcerous motes can be harvested in any such scene. Valid examples of such tending include, but are not limited to, tending an herb garden, working on a mural to beautify a city, ministering to the sick or injured, or setting a controlled burn to keep a forest healthy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">By singing certain songs, performing certain dances, or playing certain pieces of music, often accompanied by the burning of rare incenses, the scattering of exotic oils, or similar offerings, the sorceror can request spirits and elemental to give her some measure of power. The sorcerer may make a performance roll (Charisma + Performance, difficulty 5 minus the Resources value of any sacrifices offered along with the performance) seeking power from her supporters and allies in the spirit courts. Success grants her sorcerous motes equal to (her Essence + extra successes on the roll). These motes last for the duration of the story, and can be spent towards any spell she casts. She cannot undertake these performances more than once a day, and receiving new motes replaces any granted by past performances.<br /> <br /> <i>Merits</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Creation is Your Classroom</b><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> \u2022\u2022 Those who have completed this initiation can locate fairly easily teachers or instructions for new spells they wish to learn, either in the form of spirits and elementals tasked with holding that knowledge, or in natural phenomena encoded with the relevant instructions, such as a species of butterfly whose swarms hold in the markings on their wings the instructions for casting Death of Obsidian Butterflies, or a lake in which the bronze-coloured light of the rising and setting sun shows rippled reflections which instruct the watcher in the casting of Invulnerable Skin of Bronze. Locating such a source is modelled as a sorcerous working of Ambition 1 and the same Circle as the spell desired. Failure of the working merely indicates that the sorceror must look elsewhere; a botch indicates that the source had been damaged in some way. Perhaps the butterflies are in their caterpillar state, or the lake has been polluted and must be cleaned to be read. A spirit or elemental might want or need something done before sharing its knowledge, as with a volcano god that wants to try octopus before it will consent to teach Magma Kraken. This working costs no XP; the learning of the spell does. Time and assistance can affect the terminus, but components and infrastructure do not normally apply.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 01-09-2016, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:29:24-08:00","id":808361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skina Stonedottir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=801187#post801187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder about this from a balance perspective; mara's power is difficult to leverage because you need to spend time building unrequited love in the people likely to be around you; it's much easier for you to build hate in yourself something that it is to instil feelings in others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, and one I wondered about myself. I'd like to point out however that Mara's ritual allows you to draw motes from multiple people present for your control spells AND they only need to be present, while my version only lets you tap one person (if multiple targets are affected by the spell, only the highest intimacy counts for motes) and can only draw from the actual target. The idea was to go for a Sith-esque &quot;use your anger&quot; type of thing, but maybe reversing it will work just as well - gain motes when casting spells at people that hate <i>you</i>? Would that be more balanced?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skina Stonedottir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=801257#post801257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this, although I wonder if it might end up being overpowered in play; I haven't tested the new combat rules much so I'm not sure how much lethal damage a sorcerer might be expected to deal over the course of combat, but if you're garnering twenty sorcerous motes over a battle I wonder if it might be unbalanced, at least without some kind of drawback or limit (eg: sorcerous motes may only be used for spells that directly deal violence).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm worried this one is on the strong side as well, but not convinced. There are already lots of things keeping it in check though:<br /> - Only works on decisive attacks (so you'll need to spend at least some effort to build up initiative before you can start gathering motes)<br /> - Only works with this one weapon (so casting DoOB or BBQing some chumps with The Burning Name won't help me gather motes)<br /> - Only works if the target bleeds, and there are several categories of enemies that don't (automatons, elementals, ghosts and most other undead, probably some fair folk...)<br /> - Needs to be able to hold the daiklave to access the motes<br /> - Limited number of motes held at once, meaning even if you manage to gather a lot of motes over a combat scene, you'll have to spread them out on several spells rather than save up for a big one.<br /> It may still end up being too strong, in which case I'm leaning towards limiting it to Essence+WP motes/scene rather than held at once. I've started playing a game with this ritual now, will report how it feels after a while.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MuscaDomestica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=803927#post803927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-The caster has no negative modifiers for counterspelling or recognizing Necromancy. (kind of iffy right now because Necromancy does not have any rules)</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like it would be a merit - shaping rituals only grant sorcerous motes, not benefits like this one. No idea how many dots it should be - as you said, the rules on Necromancy aren't out yet.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MuscaDomestica</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=803927#post803927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Living with Death***: You are used to living and studying the dead. Your body becomes accustomed to the feeling of death, you can respire motes in a Shadowland like it was normal creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but I don't think there's anything in 3E that says you respire motes slower in Shadowlands. I think there was someone who mentioned this on the Q&amp;A thread?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1184\" data-vbnamecard=\"1184\">LadyLens</a>: Love it. Very flavourful. The second ritual seems a bit on the strong side though, maybe it should be limited to once per story rather than once per day?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10437-swooper","name":"Swooper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10437_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:16:14-08:00","id":812946,"title":"","content":"I'm admitedly not a backer, and thus do not know how I mechanically would write it out, but one idea I like is an Initiation based off the idea of Martial Enlightenment, using meditation and ritualized kata in order to channel the power of the world around them. It's probably one of the few paths of mortal sorcery explicitly approved by the Order, with those who achieve it being hailed as one who is destined to be Of the Dragons in their next life. Motes might be gained through hours of meditation, or maybe by forgoing all damage on a MA attack roll? Again, not a backer, so not sure how broken that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T21:37:04-08:00","id":813168,"title":"","content":"I have one. Warning: this is extremely silly and should only rarely be used in serious games.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Visions of Bacchanalia</b></span><br /> Congratulations, you've forged a pact with one or more of the gods of the Cerulean Lute of Harmony. Now, your revelries are for more than just their own benefit. In the thrumming of music, the laughter of friends, and the heady rush of wine you see visions of the inner workings of the world. As you peel away the world and grasp towards chemical joy, you are rewarded with assistance in the sorcerer's art.<br /> <br /> When you begin a scene suffering a dice pool penalty due to intoxication, you receive 1 + Penalty sorcerous motes that can be spent at any point during the scene. These sorcerous motes vanish at the end of the scene or in the event that the character stops receiving a penalty from their revels. <br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b><i> Drinky Crow is absolutely obliterated by the time the assassins burst into the palace. Because he has helped himself to the lions share of the Satrap's hard liquor, he is suffering a -3 penalty to all actions he takes; for such epic debauchery, fate rewards him with 4 sorcerous motes. As the assassins cluster together in an extremely 'Obsidian Butterfly Deathable' formation, he finishes the last of his drink.</i><br /> <br /> As an added bonus, you no longer subtract penalties due being drunk or otherwise inebriated from any pool drawing on your occult skill.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:18:08-08:00","id":822407,"title":"","content":"So a lot of folks have been taking example initiations from the book and reflavoring them, which is a great foundation to start with.<br /> <br /> So I wondered, what if you learned sorcery from a different elemental than an Ifrit? What if you had an Earth patron? Or a wood patron? Or an air or water patron?<br /> <br /> How would you reflavor or rework the initiation and merits of Pact with Ifrit Lord with the other elements?<br /> <br /> I can imagine Air turning The Burning Name into either a forceful air attack or a freezing attack. Freezing would probably be easiest as you could just relabel the same stats as cold damage. But perhaps Wood would be a poison spit attack? Or perhaps you summon roots out of the ground to grapple them?<br /> <br /> Perhaps an initiation for Water would be when you're near a body of water big enough to submerge in you get a mote. Or if you're actually submerged or it's raining you get Essence motes. Maybe a version of Unburnt Majesty would be you can breathe in water (would require more merit dots)<br /> <br /> What are you thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:50:49-08:00","id":822435,"title":"","content":"A 2e game in which I played featured a PC Solar sorcerer making a pact with a King of the Forest, which was sealed by them swapping their right eyes. All the lesser elementals from the wood-king's forest saw the sorcerer's wooden eye and knew to obey his commands as if the wood-king himself had issued them. I think it'd make a pretty awesome sorcerous initiation in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:28:53-08:00","id":822544,"title":"","content":"I had an initiation based on a particularly heretical view of Mela, because I love Air but also love Burning Name. The Word of Thunder unleashes a thunderclap that does bashing but has the smashing tag, aka Fus Ro Dah. One of the shaping rituals involved juicing off damage from harsh weather (suggested in core) and another involved living up to Mela's standards of perfection, though I'm not particularly happy with that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:54:19-08:00","id":822570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=822544#post822544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an initiation based on a particularly heretical view of Mela, because I love Air but also love Burning Name. The Word of Thunder unleashes a thunderclap that does bashing but has the smashing tag, aka Fus Ro Dah.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me so happy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:43:32-08:00","id":840557,"title":"","content":"I could use your input on an initiation I'm doing for a PC in my soon-to-Exalt mortals game.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer in question made contact with a powerful entity she calls &quot;the Observer&quot;, a Lovecraftian mass of dark tentacles and disembodied inhuman eyes that is very knowledgeable when it comes to dark secrets of the universe and willing to share with her in exchange for every bit of First Age lore she can uncover.<br /> <br /> Since we didn't have time to homebrew it before the first game (crazy schedules), so far I gave her the choice from two existing rituals: the one from Scarred by Nightmares that lets you describe strange prophetic dreams and gain sorcerous motes instead of Willpower from sleeping, and the one from the Talisman of the Thousand eyes that lets gives motes for stunting the casting with the use of Talisman, except instead of the bauble she uses an occult symbol branded onto her right palm. I'm generally content with keeping these, as they fit the theme and the player likes them, but I wanted to give her something unique and to expand on the theme of knowledge, so I thought to myself: why not something that gives sorcerous motes for introducing facts? Here's what I came up with:<br /> <br /> <i>Whenever the sorcerer introduces a fact that pertains to ancient secrets, magical places and/or beings, she gains a number of sorcerous motes equal to her Lore rating that last for the remainder of the scene. If she uses these motes to cast a spell affecting the being or place that was the subject of the introduced fact, each counts as two motes for the purpose of spell completion.</i><br /> <br /> What do you think? I'm not sure about giving a flat amount of motes, sounds kinda boring and might overly incentivize getting to Lore 5 ASAP. Maybe give motes equal to the number of successes on the Int+Lore roll? Half of that maybe?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T18:41:23-08:00","id":841641,"title":"","content":"I've got an idea for a merit as part of the Sorcerer's Apprentice initiation. The sorcerer may, once per story, gain access to a spell he does not know for the remainder of the scene, but actually USING the spell is dangerous in some way. This is to play up that old trope of the apprentice that tries to take shortcuts instead of doing things the &quot;right&quot; way. How, though, would a merit like this actually function? I even had the idea that one might learn a spell of a level above those they are capable of casting, but only by accepting a danger that may cost them their life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T21:57:31-08:00","id":841715,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Path of the High and Low</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This peculiar form of initiation is currently practiced only by a small group of a half-dozen women in the Wavecrest archipelago. The witches have varied in number between as few as two, at their founding, to as many as a dozen. The founders were explorers of sensation, and found though their experiments in pleasure and pain, of subjugation and domination, a path to sorcerous might, which they later taught to their initiates. They do not initiate men, though men could, in theory, learn and use these secrets. The rituals listed below are lengthy, requiring at least a full hour each. Spending a full day in performing a combined ritual adds three motes total. All rituals add motes equal to the rating of the lowest relevant Intimacy the participants share.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Through certain rituals, the initiate can harvest sorcerous motes from pain, whether inflicting or suffering it. Roll (Stamina+Occult); each success grants one mote. If both inflictor and sufferer are initiated in this tradition, both roll, and gain motes equal to the higher roll. The sufferer also takes at least one level of bashing damage, but also an additional mote. These motes last for the duration of a story, and motes from successive rituals replace existing motes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Certain other rituals provide a similar benefit from sexual pleasure; this ritual\u2019s success is determined by an (Appearance+Performance) roll, and no damage is inflicted.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The final ritual involves the domination of another, or being subjugated by another. This ritual is performed much as the rite of pain, but the roll is (Charisma + Occult), and no damage is inflicted.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Merits: I have no idea. All suggestions are welcome; currently, I'm thinking that a given pair should get some sort of benefit in partnered casting, or targeting each other. Perhaps they could develop something like a familiar bond with each other.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Yes, this is sect of lesbian BDSM sorceresses. I couldn\u2019t resist, the idea was just so odd yet appropriate (and the image too appealing). And yes, I'm quite aware that this group would have a distinct advantage when it comes to sorcerous workings.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 03-04-2016, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T22:09:36-08:00","id":841721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=841641#post841641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got an idea for a merit as part of the Sorcerer's Apprentice initiation. The sorcerer may, once per story, gain access to a spell he does not know for the remainder of the scene, but actually USING the spell is dangerous in some way. This is to play up that old trope of the apprentice that tries to take shortcuts instead of doing things the &quot;right&quot; way. How, though, would a merit like this actually function? I even had the idea that one might learn a spell of a level above those they are capable of casting, but only by accepting a danger that may cost them their life.</div> </div> </div> </div>The simplest would be to allow the casting of a spell not learned at a dual penalty: a 50% surcharge on the mote cost (round fractions up) and any failure on shaping or casting is considered a botch. A spell one circle too high seems an excessive benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:45:05-08:00","id":842169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=841721#post841721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The simplest would be to allow the casting of a spell not learned at a dual penalty: a 50% surcharge on the mote cost (round fractions up) and any failure on shaping or casting is considered a botch. A spell one circle too high seems an excessive benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure there's no way to make it work? I love the idea of a precocious apprentice get hold of power beyond their ken.<br /> <br /> Also, what exactly happens when you botch a shape sorcery roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":899,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","user":"The Free Man","date":". 03-04-2016, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:18:59-08:00","id":842312,"title":"","content":"It's not defined apart from any other botch. You gather no motes, and you have to deal with a dramatically interesting complication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T06:28:13-08:00","id":842963,"title":"","content":"I've got another merit that I'm having a bit of an issue with, in that I'm not sure if I'm wording it properly, and I'm not sure about the number of dots.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Spite-Honed Will (?): Your master is many things. Intelligent, powerful, and even magnetic are all words that might describe them, but kindness appears nowhere on this list. Constant exposure to your mentor's unpleasantness has inured you to the unpleasantness of others. Whenever a character fails to overcome your Resolve with influence meant to inspire a negative reaction, you gain a point of temporary willpower.</span></span><br /> <br /> Essentially, your will is stronger because your mentor was a big meanie pants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T07:56:55-07:00","id":863648,"title":"","content":"Can someone check this initiation for balance?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Legacy of Wonders</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Artifacts are a legacy of wonders, a shining testament to the might of the Chosen, a burning glyph in the face of Creation that embodies all that is fundamentally Right and Just. A pentagram of five wondrous metals can be alloyed in any way to set right any problem of the world, with only ingenuity, determination and vision, any artificer may forge the wonders to determine the course of an age.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Shaping Rituals</i></span></span><ul><li>Whenever the sorcerer forges an artifact of at least 3 dots, she gains (Craft + [Essence]) Sorcerous Motes that last for the rest of the story. These may never be restored, only replaced with new iterations of this shaping ritual.</li> <li>When the sorcerer takes the first shape sorcery action to begin casting a spell and stunts it with a description of how she casts the spell through the artifact, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes towards completing this spell. This benefit can only be received once per scene. Stunts to enhance the sorcerer\u2019s control spell do not count against the once per scene limit.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Other Benefits</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Right Hand of Power (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sorcerer may attune to artifacts. This causes them to add the artifact\u2019s attune cost as a difficulty to all shape sorcery actions, gaining 1 sorcerous mote per threshold success instead of 1 per success. This is cumulative, though many never attune more than one artifact due to the increased difficulty. They may also use the artifact\u2019s Evocations as spells, replacing their cost in motes with sorcerous motes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Puissant Crown Unvanquished (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sorcerer may count as a Dragon-Blooded for the purposes of learning and using Evocations for a single artifact.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:23:35-07:00","id":863671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863648#post863648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone check this initiation for balance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the direction you're going with this, but your flavor text in the beginning doesn't actually talk about gaining insight into sorcery through your crafting. It just says &quot;You're a great crafter! Keep crafting great!&quot; Could use a line or two relating it to sorcery in some way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863648#post863648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Whenever the sorcerer forges an artifact of at least 3 dots, she gains (Craft + [Essence]) Sorcerous Motes that last for the rest of the story. These may never be restored, only replaced with new iterations of this shaping ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the difficulty and time involved in doing this act, it almost feels like too small a payoff. For something that will take a portion of a story to complete and only getting AT BEST 10 motes, which even then is unlikely (more likely 6 or 7). I'm not sure that bigger numbers are the key, but something feels a little weak about it. I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863648#post863648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]When the sorcerer takes the first shape sorcery action to begin casting a spell and stunts it with a description of how she casts the spell through the artifact, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes towards completing this spell. This benefit can only be received once per scene. Stunts to enhance the sorcerer\u2019s control spell do not count against the once per scene limit.[/LIST]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Other Benefits</i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863648#post863648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Right Hand of Power (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sorcerer may attune to artifacts. This causes them to add the artifact\u2019s attune cost as a difficulty to all shape sorcery actions, gaining 1 sorcerous mote per threshold success instead of 1 per success. This is cumulative, though many never attune more than one artifact due to the increased difficulty. They may also use the artifact\u2019s Evocations as spells, replacing their cost in motes with sorcerous motes.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Is the only benefit getting to use sorcerous motes to channel evocations? It's worded like the stuff before that is supposed to be a good thing, but it's actually just a big drawback. As worded, it's an interesting merit, but I don't think it's so strong as to warrant 5 points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863648#post863648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Puissant Crown Unvanquished (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sorcerer may count as a Dragon-Blooded for the purposes of learning and using Evocations for a single artifact.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>THIS is an interesting one. Useless to Solars, but very useful to most other exalts. The cost feels good. I think I dig it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:30:13-07:00","id":863674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863671#post863671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the direction you're going with this, but your flavor text in the beginning doesn't actually talk about gaining insight into sorcery through your crafting. It just says &quot;You're a great crafter! Keep crafting great!&quot; Could use a line or two relating it to sorcery in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I knew I had forgotten something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863671#post863671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the difficulty and time involved in doing this act, it almost feels like too small a payoff. For something that will take a portion of a story to complete and only getting AT BEST 10 motes, which even then is unlikely (more likely 6 or 7). I'm not sure that bigger numbers are the key, but something feels a little weak about it. I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original version was ([Craft] + [Essence] + [Willpower])<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863671#post863671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically a copypaste word-for-word of The Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863671#post863671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the only benefit getting to use sorcerous motes to channel evocations? It's worded like the stuff before that is supposed to be a good thing, but it's actually just a big drawback. As worded, it's an interesting merit, but I don't think it's so strong as to warrant 5 points.</div> </div> </div> </div>It allows mortal sorcerers to use Artifacts for one. I think I'll make it a 1-dot Merit for Exalts, and a 5-dot Merit for mortals.<br /> <br /> As well as allow the Exalted to subtract (Esssence) from the attunement cost of artifacts, attuned this way to a minimum of 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863671#post863671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THIS is an interesting one. Useless to Solars, but very useful to most other exalts. The cost feels good. I think I dig it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:36:08-07:00","id":863677,"title":"","content":"New version!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Legacy of Wonders</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Artifacts are a legacy of wonders, a shining testament to the might of the Chosen, a burning glyph in the face of Creation that embodies all that is fundamentally Right and Just. A pentagram of five wondrous metals can be alloyed in any way to set right any problem of the world, with only ingenuity, determination and vision, any artificer may forge the wonders to determine the course of an age. You might have studied at the Valkshawsen Academy for Sorcerers at Lookshy, or you might have studied the art of thousand crafts under the emerald sun of Ligier himself to learn from his skill, perhaps your passion for the craft allowed you to initiate yourself into the art of Sorcery.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Shaping Rituals</i></span></span><ul><li>Whenever the sorcerer forges an artifact of at least 3 dots, she gains (Craft + [Essence] + [Willpower]) Sorcerous Motes that last for the rest of the story. These may never be restored, only replaced with new iterations of this shaping ritual.</li> <li>When the sorcerer takes the first shape sorcery action to begin casting a spell and stunts it with a description of how she casts the spell through the artifact, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes towards completing this spell. This benefit can only be received once per scene. Stunts to enhance the sorcerer\u2019s control spell do not count against the once per scene limit.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Other Benefits</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Right Hand of Power (Merit </b></span></span><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> or </b></span></span><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>):</b> The Sorcerer may attune to artifacts. This causes them to add the artifact\u2019s attune cost as a difficulty to all shape sorcery actions, gaining 1 sorcerous mote per threshold success instead of 1 per success. This is cumulative, though many never attune more than one artifact due to the increased difficulty. They may also use the artifact\u2019s Evocations as spells, replacing their cost in motes with sorcerous motes. This merit costs three points for the Exalted, and five points for mortals, it also allows Exalted to subtract (Essence) from the attunement cost of any artifacts attuned in this way to a minimum of one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Puissant Crown Unvanquished (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Sorcerer may count as a Dragon-Blooded for the purposes of learning and using Evocations for a single artifact.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:41:51-07:00","id":863682,"title":"","content":"<br /> Well, you should have a third ritual. And the phrasing is a bit awkward for both. Try this:<ul><li>Whenever the sorcerer forges an artifact, she gains (Intelligence + Occult) Sorcerous Motes, plus two motes times the Artifact's dot rating. These motes last for the duration of a story. Motes gained from further performances of this ritual replace the motes gained by previous performances.</li> <li>When the sorcerer stunts a shape sorcery action with a description of how she casts the spell through the artifact, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes towards completing this spell. This benefit can only be received once per scene per spell. Stunts to enhance the sorcerer\u2019s control spell can receive this benefit any number of times.</li> <li>Through study of an artifact, a sorceror can gains momentary insights and so gather wisps of power. By spending a scene in study of an Artifact, other than her own creations, the sorceror can gain sorcerous motes equal to the threshold successes on an Intelligence + Occult roll with a Difficulty equal to the Artifact's rating. These motes last for a day.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 04-11-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:44:14-07:00","id":863683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=863674#post863674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It allows mortal sorcerers to use Artifacts for one. I think I'll make it a 1-dot Merit for Exalts, and a 5-dot Merit for mortals.<br /> <br /> As well as allow the Exalted to subtract (Esssence) from the attunement cost of artifacts, attuned this way to a minimum of 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do the mortals get the mote pool for attuning? It only states using sorcerous motes to power evocations. Or is the implication that the cost is offset as a difficulty on shape sorcery actions? Because if it's the latter, there's nothing to stipulate that the sorcerer simply learns the initiation and then never tries to cast sorcery, and simply has an artifact for free. All weapon/armor artifacts have at least an attunement of 5, which is a HUGE difficulty on shaping actions, basically making them unworkable for a mortal. Just some thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:53:54-07:00","id":863687,"title":"","content":"A think I thunk : If I was playing a Crafter-Sorcerer, I'd like a way to spend Craft Points on Workings or Spells. Maybe Silver Points as Sorcerous Motes and Gold or White points as Working exp? Something like that.<br /> <br /> There would be maximums, probably, to avoid spending 3000 points in a scene... although... iirc Pact with an Ifrit Lord doesn't put a limit on how much fire you can consume outside of what's actually there, so setting things on fire (which is super easy for e.g. fire DBs) is a pretty strong source of Sorcerous Motes... hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T08:54:30-07:00","id":863688,"title":"","content":"The Merits:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Right Hand of Power (Merit </b></span></span><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b> or </b></span></span><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>):</b> The Sorcerer may attune to artifacts by use of lengthy, intricate rituals. By succeeding at an extended (Intelligence + Occult) roll with a difficulty equal to the Artifact's rating, a goal number equal to the Artifact's normal attunement cost, a terminus of 5, and a roll interval of one day, the character can attune an Artifact to herself. The three-dot version of this Merit allows attunement to a single Artifact at a time; the five dot allows any number to be attuned.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Puissant Crown Unvanquished (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> The Sorcerer may learn and use Evocations for attuned Artifacts; where applicable, the sorceror is considered on par with a Terrestrial Exalted, though Evocations that specifically depend on Charms or other abilities unique to the Exalted are still inaccessible. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Evocations that cost motes can be used, but the character must use sorcerous motes to empower them.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:37:55-07:00","id":872597,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hey,<br /> <br /> I wanted to share an initiation I put together for a player in my upcoming game. I actually named the shaping rituals because... frankly, it made things easier for me. The first (Storm's Bounty) could easily be exchanged with the example stormy ritual in the book, but I preferred the notion of stunting the storm into the shaping, as did my player.<br /> <br /> Bloodsworn to Tempests</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Awakened by mingling blood with that of a god of storms and swearing binding oaths of loyalty before Heaven, your mind has been set ablaze with new insight. In stillness, patterns reveal themselves to your inner eye. In fury, insight strikes swift and devastating. You may be adopted kin to cloud herders, but it is the storm that speaks to you as a sibling. The sorcerer\u2019s blood brothers and sisters lend their aid, but also their wrath and sorrow. The Merit costs may bear some tweaking. The &quot;start of any journeys&quot; clause in Tempest Harvesting is specifically included under the assumption that journeys = exposure to weather and also to offset the pain of dragging that poor Crafter out of their workshop.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Rituals</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Storm\u2019s Bounty</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The sorcerer gains sorcerous motes when using a stunt to incorporate a storm into a shaping action. If the storm is mere rains and winds, gain motes equal to the stunt\u2019s rating. If the storm represents an environmental hazard, the stunt garners (stunt+3) motes instead. She may only gain these motes once per scene. Her control spell is not subject to the scene limitation.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Storm\u2019s Fury</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Upon gaining or acting on an Intimacy of hostility, anger, or sorrow, the sorcerer may reflexively add sorcerous motes equal to the value of the Intimacy to a shaping action. This expressly allows the sorcerer to maintain an ongoing shaping action while engaging in other actions. She may only draw on one such Intimacy per day with this ritual. Her control spell is exempt from this limitation, but the ritual may only grant up to 10 motes per scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parting Clouds</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once per day when the sorcerer takes time to meditate, appraise the artistry of the Cloud Herders, or otherwise enjoys some time in quiet contemplation under the open sky, she may roll (Wits+Integrity) at a default difficulty of 1. She gains sorcerous motes equal to the number of successes. These motes are lost at the end of the day.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weather Eye (\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab):</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your kinship allows you to intuitively predict weather patterns. Roll Perception+[Lore, Sail, or Survival] at a difficulty determined by the Storyteller. Success allows you to predict the weather for the next 2-3 days. Every threshold success adds another day to that time, to a limit of a week and a day. Predictions may be upset by sorcerous or divine interference.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Voice of Thunder (\u26ab\u26ab):</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When you will it, your voice booms with palpable force. The sorcerer gains double 9s on all rolls where both volume and majesty would prove valuable, such as issuing orders in battle or performing before a large audience. She may also stunt usage of this talent to startle or deafen foes within Short range, but allies will also be at risk. The sorcerer may make herself intelligibly heard by those at Long range, and even those farther away may hear battlecries or incoherent shouts. Use of this ability can prove taxing, especially if used repeatedly or for extended periods.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tempest Harvesting (\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab\u26ab): The sorcerer is able to draw creative inspiration from whispers and howls of the wind, the shapes of clouds, or the rhythms of falling rain.. She gains 2sxp at the start of any journeys or when stunting how the weather is inspiring her creation. The sorcerer may instead utilize especially forceful weather conditions (downpours, driving gales, thunderstorms) as a Means toward sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> Feedback is welcome!<br /> Garg</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11647-gargoyle","name":"Gargoyle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T16:51:46-07:00","id":872731,"title":"","content":"Hey Garg, <br /> First I LOVE it. As in, stole it for a new character instantly love it. I personally would add a knock off of &quot;The Burning Name&quot; as a lightning bolt or concussive force. I would also be careful of the Tempest Harvesting Merit. As Written it makes Ambition 1 workings free. Maybe change the wording to &quot;She reduces the XP cost for workings by 2 (to a minimum of 1) when incorporating storms and/or weather related effects&quot; instead? I also sort of want it to limit the discount effect to workings that are related directly to weather, air, electricity, or sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11664-darthgerg","name":"DarthGerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11664_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T06:05:13-07:00","id":873040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthGerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=872731#post872731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Garg,<br /> First I LOVE it. As in, stole it for a new character instantly love it. I personally would add a knock off of &quot;The Burning Name&quot; as a lightning bolt or concussive force. I would also be careful of the Tempest Harvesting Merit. As Written it makes Ambition 1 workings free. Maybe change the wording to &quot;She reduces the XP cost for workings by 2 (to a minimum of 1) when incorporating storms and/or weather related effects&quot; instead? I also sort of want it to limit the discount effect to workings that are related directly to weather, air, electricity, or sound.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't believe it does. It grants an additional Means. I would look more warily on the ability to gain silver xp from stunts(And clarify that it's Silver XP as opposed to Solar XP, which may have caused the confusion above).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T06:24:37-07:00","id":873047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gargoyle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=872597#post872597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">snip</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I love this. Considering I got a Storm-themed Sorcerer in my game? This is just what I needed.<br /> -looted-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T11:45:27-07:00","id":873911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=873040#post873040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't believe it does. It grants an additional Means. I would look more warily on the ability to gain silver xp from stunts(And clarify that it's Silver XP as opposed to Solar XP, which may have caused the confusion above).</div> </div> </div> </div>HAHAHA, you are totally right, I misread the crap out of that. Good catch, I rescind my objections <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11664-darthgerg","name":"DarthGerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11664_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:59:35-07:00","id":875276,"title":"","content":"This thread now features Initiations based in elemental Air and Earth. Has anyone written anything for Water and Wood?<br /> <br /> What about sorcerous demons and gods besides Mara? I provided one for the Unconquered Sun on page 1, but I didn't have any pleasing ideas for Luna or the Five Maidens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T11:47:54-07:00","id":875807,"title":"","content":"Have a Wood based one... vaguely.<br /> <br /> <b>Draught of Eternity's Venom</b><br /> <br /> In the far east, near the Pole of Wood, there is a horribly old tree, 30 feet in height, ridden with disease and every kind of parasite. In its crown, there is a pool of perfectly black liquid, so utterly poisonous that nothing else grows within fifty feet of the tree. Treat this as environmental hazard 4A/Round, Difficulty 4. Damage takes the form of rapid aging. Actually touching the poison double both the damage and the difficulty, so most people use a branch from the tree itself, the only substance shown to have any resistance to poison except for diamond. If the poison can be retrieved in a vial of diamond and boiled in the fires of the earth(read: Lava), the poison becomes an elixir of incredible potence, able to restore youth and grant knowledge of the truths underlying Creation. However, this only ever works once, and drinking a second draught will cause the imbiber's immediate and painful death.(Well. 12A/Round, Difficulty 12, Duration 20 Rounds, Penalty -5. Have fun, and should you somehow survive, talk with your ST)<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals:</b><br /> <br /> Having imbibed the greatest of Creation's Poisons, the Sorcerer learns to draw enlightenment from lesser poisons. While under the effects of a poison, the Sorcerer may choose to have the penalty become a bonus to all Shape Sorcery Actions and suffer no further damage from the poison. If, however, the Sorcerer is Crashed while using this ritual, it causes a temporary activation of the poison in his blood, causing him to suffer the effects of Eternity's Venom while he is Crashed.<br /> <br /> Once per Story, the Sorcerer may meditate for up to an hour to crystallize some of Eternity's Venom in his stomach, trapping a number of sorcerous motes within the stone. The Sorcerer may roll up to 3 Shape Sorcery Actions and choose the one with the most successes. Each roll requires 20 minutes of uninterrupted meditation, and once the Sorcerer has decided not to trap the motes in the poison, they are lost. Once the Sorcerer accepts a roll, the crystal appears and within the next ten minutes, enters the Sorcerer's bloodstream until it rises as a black mark on his forehead. At any point during the Story, the Sorcerer may cause this crystal to shatter, releasing the the Sorcerous motes into a spell he is Shaping at the time. However, if an enemy manages to strike the mark and the Sorcerer is not currently casting a Spell, burning poisonous essence spills down his face, rendering him blind if he fails a Stamina + Resistance Roll of Difficulty 7, and leaving him hideously scarred for (6-Essence) weeks. Striking the mark requires succeeding on a difficulty 5 gambit.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Wings of Death(3):</b><br /> <br /> The Sorcerer may draw the poison out of his body to grow weak wings of black and green. By spending a point of willpower, these wings can have their strength increased, granting the full benefits of the 5-Dot Wings Merit OR granting the Sorcerer Unarmed Weapons with the Lethal and Flexible tags. What form these enhancements take are unique to the Sorcerer. These wings may also be dismissed or called reflexively, sinking or rising as black-green fog out of the Sorcerer's back<br /> <br /> <b>Font of Venom(2):</b><br /> <br /> The Sorcerer may replicate any lesser poison, drawing from the archtypical Venom in his blood. Provided he has lost at least one health level to another poison, he can copy it and transfer it through his bodily liquids or unarmed attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Fear is the Greatest Poison(2):</b><br /> <br /> The Sorcerer's venomous presence seeps into the mind of those around, allowing a character who does not have the Hideous Merit to apply his appearance bonus as if he were Hideous, if he so desires. This only works on individuals he has had physical contact with in the last hour or so. If the character does have the Hideous Merit, he may instead use his poison to cloud other's vision, making it so that he appears normal. The effects of this merit wear off if the character fails to maintain physical contact with his targets every hour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T19:58:05-07:00","id":876204,"title":"","content":"Eh, not sure on balance, but this is my idea of what a blood tradition would look like.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Path of Blood</b><br /> Blood has held power since the dawn of mankind, when the hearts of mortals were sacrificed for the love of the Unconquered. It is perhaps the most primal of power, and so has ties to the most primal of all magics, sorcery.<br /> <br /> <i>Shaping Rituals</i><br /> <br /> As blood is shed on the battlefield or in an alleyway, you can feel the dying life in it evanescing into the aether. You have learned to pull that energy away before it dissipates, and use it to fuel your spells. The spilled blood turns to ash. Each time an enemy gains or increases his wound penalty in a scene, gain sorcerous motes equal to the value of the wound penalty. You can gain up to 10 sorcerous motes per scene in this fashion. Motes spent on your control spell do not count towards this limit. Any unused sorcerous motes gained from this shaping ritual fade at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> You may reap the essence from your foes as you cut into them directly, in its most honorable form, this is willing sacrifice, in almost all other situations, it is a brutal sheering of flesh in the heat of battle. When you inflict post-soak damage in a decisive attack you may reflexively activate this shaping ritual to gain sorcerous motes equal to the damage dealt (up to essence + willpower). If it is a willing sacrifice, there is no cap. This shaping ritual can be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> Your blood, however, is the most potent of all, steeped in sorcery as it is. Once per scene you can draw on your own blood for power. You may use blood that has already spilled from an open (lethal) wound, or inflict a fresh wound upon yourself. Roll Essence + Willpower + Wound Penalty (as a positive), gaining extra successes equal to the value of the health level filled if you inflicted the wound yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11632-ramaloke","user":"Ramaloke","date":". 04-27-2016, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11632-ramaloke","name":"Ramaloke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T17:57:49-07:00","id":878279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthGerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=872731#post872731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Garg,<br /> First I LOVE it. As in, stole it for a new character instantly love it. I personally would add a knock off of &quot;The Burning Name&quot; as a lightning bolt or concussive force. I would also be careful of the Tempest Harvesting Merit. As Written it makes Ambition 1 workings free. Maybe change the wording to &quot;She reduces the XP cost for workings by 2 (to a minimum of 1) when incorporating storms and/or weather related effects&quot; instead? I also sort of want it to limit the discount effect to workings that are related directly to weather, air, electricity, or sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks to all for the positive responses!<br /> Regarding the quoted text, I seriously considered including something akin to Burning Name, but I felt that Voice of Thunder and another combat-focused Merit would be overkill - and the player who inspired the write-up had mentioned having an interest in possibly ordering troops.<br /> <br /> A bit off-topic, but to anyone who is finding Ex3 a little intimidating due to the amount of homebrew it seems to require... You're not alone. But if you're a Storyteller or an inspired player, take the plunge. And share with the class!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11647-gargoyle","name":"Gargoyle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T21:34:52-07:00","id":884355,"title":"","content":"This came up on Sufficient Velocity and I thought that you folks would like it.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/posts/5950436/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/posts/5950436/\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/posts/5950436/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/posts/5950436/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Broken Fire Long ago there was an age of cold and ruthless glory, where giants walked the earth that were beasts and worlds. Then the gods breathed fire into the souls of men, and lords rose among them; they led men into battle, conquered Heaven and built Hell. So that such a battle may... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2781-bursting-eagerness-soul","name":"Bursting Eagerness Soul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:01:32-07:00","id":911268,"title":"","content":"I hope this is the right thread to ask for help concerning a fitting initiation for my character. I guess first a few infos about her. <br /> <br /> She is a solar chef (also supernal craft) that very much values her freedom of body and mind. Being able to go where she wishes to be and to &quot;see the world she wishes to see in her creations&quot; are very central to her character. Incidentally she even has the 5 point Wings Merit. Her father is a god who has a fetish for ugly women and she barely knows him. The wings are about the only thing she has from him and I as a player don't know much about him. My ST wanted to have it for himself. <br /> <br /> I'm looking for a bit conceptual help as to what would be a fitting theme.<br /> I wouldn't ask if we haven't tried ourself already, but since we are playing out the initiation in the game and we both want it to be an event that really changes her outlook on life and here own powers (she is very timid at the moment since she doesn't know anything about what it actually means to have the powers of a Solar), but that called... for situations we weren't able to accomplish. Everytime something has gone wrong and she stayed where she was.<br /> Example: The wings are treated as Wyld Mutations. Nobody knows (at the start not even she) that her father is a god. She really likes cooking so I thougth &quot;Having a meal with others is the cradle of humanity and much more&quot; would be a fitting thing. Won't work for the near future since she dislikes most of the group she is traveling with with a fiery passion. <br /> <br /> I've tried with other ideas to initiate into sorcery but it went similiar. So I'm slowly running out of ideas. Anyone who can help me with that? I'd really appreciate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:39:18-07:00","id":911298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=911268#post911268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this is the right thread to ask for help concerning a fitting initiation for my character. I guess first a few infos about her.<br /> <br /> She is a solar chef (also supernal craft) that very much values her freedom of body and mind. Being able to go where she wishes to be and to &quot;see the world she wishes to see in her creations&quot; are very central to her character. Incidentally she even has the 5 point Wings Merit. Her father is a god who has a fetish for ugly women and she barely knows him. The wings are about the only thing she has from him and I as a player don't know much about him. My ST wanted to have it for himself.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for a bit conceptual help as to what would be a fitting theme.<br /> I wouldn't ask if we haven't tried ourself already, but since we are playing out the initiation in the game and we both want it to be an event that really changes her outlook on life and here own powers (she is very timid at the moment since she doesn't know anything about what it actually means to have the powers of a Solar), but that called... for situations we weren't able to accomplish. Everytime something has gone wrong and she stayed where she was.<br /> Example: The wings are treated as Wyld Mutations. Nobody knows (at the start not even she) that her father is a god. She really likes cooking so I thougth &quot;Having a meal with others is the cradle of humanity and much more&quot; would be a fitting thing. Won't work for the near future since she dislikes most of the group she is traveling with with a fiery passion.<br /> <br /> I've tried with other ideas to initiate into sorcery but it went similiar. So I'm slowly running out of ideas. Anyone who can help me with that? I'd really appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean- my first thought is a variant on the Soul-Perfecting Elixer, but focused on being a gourmand instead of an ascetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:10:49-07:00","id":911317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=911298#post911298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean- my first thought is a variant on the Soul-Perfecting Elixer, but focused on being a gourmand instead of an ascetic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First of all thank you for your suggestion. <br /> <br /> The thing is though, she isn't your typical 3 star chef. She was raised on the streets so instead of hunting down the finest of the finest she takes what is there and makes that into delicous things. All while hunting down and discovering things nobody thought to be edible (the facts system helps here quite a bit!). <br /> <br /> First I thought it would be cool to take that into the shaping ritual: &quot;Gain Insight after hunting down an and preparing an ingredient so magical and rare that the taste opens up the cosmos for you&quot;. The problem with things like this is, that it is very dependant on the storyteller giving me things to work with. And quite honestly I don't trust him to do that (not anymore). It needs to be more lightweight if that makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:44:27-07:00","id":911339,"title":"","content":"I have this from my post on Dis's giants (It could probably work for any 'demon priest' type, and lacks merits.<br /> <b>Priest of Forgotten Gods</b><br /> There are gods that are dead, gods that have fled, and gods best forgotten. But in the writs and ritual of ancient powers, these old gods rage can be felt and turned to purposes more varied than one might think. The giants remember these older gods, and by their old peity gain power.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Ritual</b><br /> <br /> Offering to the Lost Gods: The Giants remember older powers, before men and women dared raise idols to lesser gods. Recalling the rites of their progenitors, the Gigantes offer human flesh and blood for power. A giant may gain sorcerers motes by sacrificing a bound human and making a (Occult+Charisma) roll. If the sacrifice is an essence user, add the victims (Essence x 3) in automatic successes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":".  Read the whole thread. 06-09-2016, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:05:00-07:00","id":911700,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Salinan Initiation I wrote up? I specifically designed it as a &quot;journey over destination&quot; arrangement. Travelling about to hunt up ingredients and learning occult lessons along the way, leading in due course to a moment of clarity and insight is exactly the sort of thing the Salinan initiation is designed to model.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:13:29-07:00","id":911737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=911700#post911700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the Salinan Initiation I wrote up? I specifically designed it as a &quot;journey over destination&quot; arrangement. Travelling about to hunt up ingredients and learning occult lessons along the way, leading in due course to a moment of clarity and insight is exactly the sort of thing the Salinan initiation is designed to model.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know how I managed it, but somehow I was able to skip over your Salinan Initation while reading through the thread. Yes, it fits quite well! Not exactly what I had in mind, but even better. I can easily see my character growing while going through the lessons and devoloping a new found affection for at least a few parts of creations... Everybody hates her because of the wings, so a sudden outburst of love for other people is a bit of a stretch. But it may be a thing for the future after she found something like a home, where she isn't a hated mutant for once. <br /> <br /> So yeah, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My (mostly) German Exalted blog: <a href=\"http://ryokiseck.de/\" target=\"_blank\">Praise the Spiral!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11185-ryoki","name":"Ryoki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:21:06-07:00","id":911745,"title":"","content":"You're entirely welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:27:45-07:00","id":911785,"title":"","content":"I was playing with an idea of mortal focused initiations based on the Shannara series druids. Then I did a quick search and realized that there is a TV show about it and that version of Allanon will be what most people will think when I reference it and what I write will make no sense whatsoever. Now I'm just sad <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T18:00:06-07:00","id":912009,"title":"","content":"Woo, didn't even realize this one existed when I posted my thread a few days back. I'll just repost this in here!<br /> <br /> I'm helping a friend develop her own form of shaping rituals and merits--she's a demonologist and demon hunter, and while &quot;Bargain with Mara&quot; initially caught her eye, it was too inherently malicious for her concept. So I took some others and reworked/reflavored them for her character (save one from &quot;Scarred by Nightmares&quot; which remains identical), and was wondering if others could take a look to make sure the options are all balanced for working together. Note that I know you can only have 3, but I'm just writing out a list of possibilities for her to choose from.<br /> <br /> <b><u>ADDENDUM:</u></b> She has decided on <b>2</b> (Trapped Pain-Essence), <b>4</b> (Meditation Tattoo Storage), and <b>5</b> (Self-Harm Ritual). Do these, in particular, look acceptable?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Infernal Draught of Enlightenment</b><br /> <br /> You have spilled the blood of the Valethyn, the Fleshreaver, Demon of Pain and Brine. With his blood, you have brewed a draught of sorcerous power, and upon imbibing the searing fluid, your mind was made painfully aware of the essence flows surrounding you. Ominous markings now manifest on your flesh and, though minuscule, infernal blood now pulses through your veins. With focus, you can channel pain and fear into mystic strength.<br /> <br /> ((The first one is adapted from \u201cBargain with Mara,\u201d basically replacing \u201clove\u201d with \u201cfear\u201d.))<ul><li><b>1)</b> Much like the demon before her, the sorcerer draws power from those who fear her. The Essence of their terror is clay in her hands, taking form in her sorcery. Whenever she takes a shape sorcery action while within medium range of a character with an unrequited Tie of Fear (or a similar negative emotion) towards her, she may reap additional sorcerous motes equal to that Intimacy\u2019s value (for example, four motes from a Defining Tie). Intimacies can only be tapped for motes in this fashion once per day, and the sorcerer cannot harvest power from fear she reciprocates. Normally she may only drain one Intimacy to fuel the casting of a spell, but she may draw power from any available Intimacies when casting her control spell. She cannot draw more than ten sorcerous motes per scene with this ritual.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> ((This next one is another Mara-convert, the sex one. Admittedly, you are often more likely to kill than have sex in Exalted, though \u201cconsensual sex\u201d could feasibly happen at least once a day if the seducer goes hunting specifically to stock up\u2014so I used \u201conce a day\u201d as a reasonable balance.))<ul><li><b>2) </b>When the sorcerer kills someone with Essence through physical violence and bloodshed, she may choose to capture the victim\u2019s suffering essence as it escapes in his death throes. The snared energy lingers invisibly around her, tethered to her by umbral chains. As a miscellaneous action, the sorcerer may burn one of these suffering coalescences in exchange for power once per scene, rolling (Essence + Willpower) and gaining that many sorcerous motes. She retains these motes until the end of the scene, and may spend them towards any spells she casts. Additionally, a bound coalescence may be reflexively expended in place of a point of Willpower when paying the cost of the sorcerer\u2019s control spell. She cannot have more than (Essence + Occult) coalescences bound to her at one time, and she cannot collect more than one per day.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> ((These two are super easy conversions from Talisman.))<ul><li><b>3) </b>When the sorcerer takes the first shape sorcery action to begin casting a spell and stunts it with a description of how she casts the spell through channeling the demon's blood within her, she gains (stunt rating + 2) sorcerous motes towards completing this spell. This benefit can only be received once per scene. Stunts to enhance the sorcerer\u2019s control spell do not count against the once per scene limit.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>4) </b>A sorcerer with an Essence pool may spend a scene in meditation to commit ten motes to the infernal essence marking her flesh. Once she begins shaping a spell, she may draw on the power she\u2019s invested, contributing up to (Essence + 2) sorcerous motes towards the spell until the full commitment of ten motes has been converted into ten sorcerous motes, or the spell is cast (or countered). Committed motes are converted to sorcerous motes on a one-to-one basis normally, but are converted into two sorcerous motes when casting the sorcerer\u2019s control spell. The sorcerer must wait until she\u2019s had a full night\u2019s sleep before she can charge her demonic markings again.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> (( This is one taken from \u201cPact with an Ifrit Lord\u201d, but because of the new power source, I had to tinker with the mechanics and I\u2019m not sure how to properly balance it. <b>NOTE</b><b>:</b> This is the one I'm most unsure about, but it's also the most thematically fitting of them. I lowered the difficulty start from 5 to 3 since aggravated damage might be more difficult to compensate for compared to a traveling Exalted with crazy loot, but I then increased it to 4 because unlike the original, where you could burn something so small as to count for Resources 0 and just make a prayer roll at difficulty 5, you <i>have</i> to take at least one level of damage just to start (so effectively the max difficulty is still 3). All that said, should I have gone the other way?))<ul><li><b>5) </b>The sorcerer has learned that pain is power, and through a ritual of self-harm in which she spills her own blood, her markings may flush with the power of her sacrifice. The sorcerer focuses on the infernal power within and inflicts a chosen amount of aggravated damage to herself. At the moment of affliction, she rolls (Stamina + Occult, difficulty 4 minus the levels of self-inflicted damage), attempting to maintain ritualistic focus while converting her agony into sorcerous might. Success grants her sorcerous motes equal to (her Essence + extra successes on the roll). The motes last for the duration of the story, and can be spent towards any spell she casts. She must fully heal from one ritual\u2019s damage to attempt the process again, and any new motes replaces motes obtained from previous rituals.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> ((Then of course there\u2019s always the dreams from &quot;Scarred by Nightmares&quot; which works identically.))<ul><li><b>6) </b>When the sorcerer sleeps, her player may describe the strange visions that haunt her. She recovers no Willpower from sleep, instead rolling (Wits + Occult) and gaining one sorcerous mote per success. These motes last until the next time she sleeps, and can be spent towards any spell she casts. If the sorcerer spends all of the sorcerous motes granted by a dream casting her control spell, each counts as two motes towards meeting the spell\u2019s cost. Once per story, the sorcerer\u2019s player may stunt to describe how the current situation was somehow symbolized by her dreams, essentially declaring that her past dreams retroactively foreshadow the present. Doing so awards her a number of sorcerous motes equal to (her Essence x [stunt level + 1]), which last for the duration of the scene.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And here we have the merits, taken almost word-for-word from others and reflavored for this initiation.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Merits</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Infernal Threat (Merit \u2022/\u2022\u2022):</b> Demons recognize the sorcerer as one who has forcefully taken the power of Valethyn. First Circle demons are treated as having a Minor Tie of Terror towards her, while Second and Third Circle demons have a positive Minor Tie of Grudging Distrust, or some variation suited to their nature. [<b>NOTE:</b> For balance, I figured this would be 2-dot if included with the \u201cfear-absorbing\u201d ritual, 1-dot otherwise]<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerous Blood (Merit \u2022\u2022):</b> The demonic essence within the sorcerer reacts when it comes within ten miles of dangerous sorcerous forces\u2014a sorcerer wreaking havoc with spells, a demon bound to ill ends or unbound and rampaging, an ancient curse fallen upon the land. Any tracking rolls the wearer makes to pinpoint or chase down such perils enjoys double 9s.<br /> <br /> <b>Suffering Unhindered (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> The sorcerer draws her occult power from various forms of pain, such that her mind has grown resistant. Deprivation penalties and wound penalties do not apply to any mental actions that the sorcerer takes, including shape sorcery actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Demonic Tattoos:</b> Valethyn\u2019s blood manifests as ominous tattoo-like markings on the sorcerer\u2019s flesh. The sorcerer may unlock Evocations from these tattoos that allow her to manipulate or gain power from pain or fear, alter her control spell to incorporate elements alluding to her infernal power source, or manipulate or empower summoned demons in similar allusions.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Artifact Journeyman?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11797-seeker","name":"Seeker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T19:55:08-07:00","id":912049,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I posted this initially here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/907843-bond-of-the-familiar-sorcery-rituals-peach\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-rituals-peach</a><br /> <br /> Let me know what you think!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bond of the Familiar</b><br /> The sorcerer uses his bond with a familiar or spirit familiar to fuel his magic. There is a power in the bond between a sorcerer and his familiar as their souls almost seem to merge together. These merged souls transform the sorcerer and familiar on a spiritual level, turning them into something far more than human and beast. This allows the sorcerer to reach beyond his normal capabilities and command the Essence of the world.<br /> <br /> This method of learning sorcery always requires the sorcerer to have the Familiar Merit or a spirit familiar. The sorcerer does not need to be within a certain range band of the familiar to cast spells, but some rituals have a range restriction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Shaping Rituals</i></b><br /> <br /> Drawing upon his bond with his familiar, their shared soul flares with power and life. Whenever the sorcerer takes a shape sorcery action, he may draw an additional (Essence) sorcerous motes from his familiar if they are in physical contact with each other (such as riding a horse or an eagle perched on his shoulder). Calling on the bond in this manner causes faint supernatural occurrences to manifest around the sorcerer and familiar, such as both of their eyes glowing or transparent flames rising around them.<br /> When used to draw sorcerous motes for his control spell, the sorcerer draws additional (Essence + 2) motes instead.<br /> <br /> Once per scene, the sorcerer surges with power in response to seeing his familiar harmed. If the sorcerer has a positive Intimacy towards his familiar, and witnesses the familiar being injured, he can reflexively roll (Occult), adding bonus dice equal to the intensity of the Intimacy. The sorcerer gains sorcerous motes for each success on the roll. These motes last until the end of the scene.<br /> When these motes are used to cast his control spell, he gains additional sorcerous motes for the casting equal to twice the inverse of his familiar\u2019s current wound penalty. For example, 2 sorcerous motes if the familiar is at a -1 health level, 4 sorcerous motes at a -2 health level, and 8 sorcerous motes at the -4 health level. If the familiar is at a -0 health level, the sorcerer only gains 1 additional sorcerous mote. If the familiar is incapacitated, the sorcerer instead casts his control spell without needing to spend Willpower.<br /> <br /> Not all bonds are forged in war and strife, some of the strongest bonds are formed through friendship and happiness. Once per story, the sorcerer spends an hour or more playing or relaxing with his familiar, allowing him to roll (Essence + Willpower) with bonus dice equal to the intensity of a positive Intimacy towards the familiar. The sorcerer gains sorcerous motes equal to the number of successes rolled, which last for that story\u2019s duration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Other Benefits</i></b><br /> <b>Master Trainer (*):</b> Your familiarity with animals has made it easier to teach them new tricks and practice their abilities. The training difficulty determined by the animal\u2019s attitude is reduced by 1 to a minimum of 1.<br /> <br /> <b>Sense the Bond (*) - Prerequisites (Familiar Merit or a spirit familiar):</b> Your familiar bond goes deeper than normal. You are always aware of your familiar\u2019s location and your familiar can always sense where you are.<br /> In addition, you and your familiar have a sense of each other\u2019s emotional states across any distance. This allows you and your familiar to know when the other is scared, hurt, happy, and so on.<br /> This Merit can be re-purchased any number of times, each time it applies to another familiar.<br /> <br /> <b>Shared Soul (***) - Prerequisites (Familiar Merit or a spirit familiar): </b>The charged bond between master and familiar is so powerful, it starts to radiate power. For every hour that you remain in short range of your familiar, you regain 3 motes of Essence. This does not stack when you have multiple familiars nearby, but you only need one to remain within range to gain the benefit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11898,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11898-quill3688","user":"Quill3688","date":". 06-10-2016, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11898-quill3688","name":"Quill3688","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T22:12:57-07:00","id":917797,"title":"","content":"I'd like some feedback on one I brewed up this afternoon.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Tyrant's Flame</span></b><br /> The draconic will of the Desert Tyrant burns within the Sorcerer, an inferno of energy that shapes sorcerous motes with it's presence alone.<br /> Once per story, the Sorcerer may roll (Temporary Willpower+Occult), forcing their will onto Creation to gather sorcerous. For each success, the Tyrant Flame within his heart feeds on the sorcerous motes gathered, channeling the amplified essence and burning it onto the Sorcerer's own flesh which appears as bands of runes, one each per success.<br /> Once per scene, the Sorcerer may reflexively consume a band of tattoos, instantly receiving a surge of (Essence*2) Sorcery Motes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11858-seibahismaiwaifu","name":"SeibahIsMaiWaifu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T08:12:30-07:00","id":918048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SeibahIsMaiWaifu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=917797#post917797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like some feedback on one I brewed up this afternoon.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Tyrant's Flame</span></b><br /> The draconic will of the Desert Tyrant burns within the Sorcerer, an inferno of energy that shapes sorcerous motes with it's presence alone.<br /> Once per story, the Sorcerer may roll (Temporary Willpower+Occult), forcing their will onto Creation to gather sorcerous <b>motes</b>. For each success, the Tyrant Flame within his heart feeds on the sorcerous motes gathered, channeling the amplified essence and burning it onto the Sorcerer's own flesh which appears as bands of runes, one each per success.<br /> Once per scene, the Sorcerer may reflexively consume a band of tattoos, instantly receiving a surge of (Essence*2) Sorcery Motes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's good. I'd make it a standard Shape Sorcery action rather than Temporary Willpower + Occult, but in the end it simply amounts to (Essence*2) motes/scene so it's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T20:49:01-07:00","id":921327,"title":"","content":"And I only found this after making a thread for my idea. Wonderful. Ah well, I'll put it here too.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> <br /> Martial Enlightenment<br /> <br /> Shaping Ritual<br /> <br /> Having dedicated themselves fully to the practice of their martial art, the practitioner has seen into the mystical truths her style embodies. After a night's sleep the Martial Artist may roll (Willpower+[Martial Arts Style]) while practicing the katas of their art and gain a sorcerous mote for each success. These motes last until they next go to sleep.<br /> <br /> Merit:<br /> <br /> [Style] Enlightenment<br /> The martial artist may learn the charms of his style as if they were spells without an essence prerequisite, and may use sorcerous motes to fuel them. If one of these charms is the practitioner's control spell, he respires 5 sorcerous motes per round in a fight which may only be used for the charms of his style.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> So, good idea or bad idea? Also, I'm thinking the merit should be 5 dots, but I'm not sure. Obviously the idea is for mortal MAists to be able to do their style's charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T23:01:30-07:00","id":922474,"title":"","content":"I can't sleep again so I decided I might as well repost this from the other forum I shared this on.<br /> A spell, an archtype, and a few shaping rituals<br /> Yes. The inane and pointless HTML for emphasis is extremely important to both the spell and the archetype.<br /> <hr /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Explosion!</span></i></b></span>(1wp, 20sm, Celestial Circle Sorcery)<br /> Keywords: Decisive Only, Perilous, Terrestral <br /> Duration: Instant<br /> <br /> A Molten Vortex of plasma churning in a sea of sorcerous dust and motes, a spiral galaxy that forms high above the Sorcerer. A promulgation of the Rules of Nature, the burning name of the destruction incarnate, ancient sorcery drawn from the Five Poles of Creation. The Hammer of Eternity descends from it's core, a star born of fire and destruction, the semblance of Sol Invictus in his Glorious Radiance that descends upon the singularity of inevitability: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><i><b>Explosion!</b></i></span><br /> <br /> A miniature sun surges forth from the galaxy of sorcerous essence towards a single point in space within Long range of the Sorcerer's sight, rolling (Occ. + Perc. + Essence) as a decisive attack. The star embodies the pure destructive will of the Sorcerer, with base damage equal to (her Initiative + current temporary Willpower + Essence), and resets her to (base Initiative + Essence) on a successful attack. The star strikes in massive area of effect, incinerating everything in a sphere within Medium range of the point struck and is unparriable with mundane weapons which melt on contact with the star. Battlegroups are especially vulnerable to this spell and suffer -2 their defense value. Each target that takes at least 5 damage to their health track is ignited in an inferno (environmental hazard equal to Lava, p. 230 of Core) that englufs him all terrain within close range of him, and burns until the next day.<br /> <br /> A Sorcerer who knows Explosion! as her control spell may expend her entire periphery essence pool towards the attack, adding 1 die to the raw damage of the spell for every 2m of essence spent.<br /> <hr /><br /> Archetype:<b><i><span style=\"color:#B22222\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">8-Ignition Way | Darker than Black and Blacker than Dark: Brilliance that Burns with the Fury of the Crimson Demon Clan\u2013 The Path of Explosions</span></span></i></b><br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals:<br /> <br /> Flames and explosions dance with the Crimson Demon Clan as if they were sisters. As she gives life to and shapes new infernos into the world as she walks the Path of Explosions, her conflagrations breathe new essence into her. Once per round, the Sorcerer may draw up to (Essence) sorcery motes from any bonfire or greater ignition she has caused. These sorcery motes last until sunrise and may only be spent towards casting fire or explosive based spells.<br /> <br /> Those of the Crimson Demon Clan are naturally inclined towards unnecessarily longwinded spell-chants. When the Sorcerer stunts a shape sorcery action to cast a fire or explosion spell, that spell's cost is reduced by (1 + 2*Stunt Rating) sorcery motes until the end of the round.<br /> <br /> The sorcerers who follow the Path of Explosions are forever changed by the power and warmth that flows through them when the shape the essence of creation into a spell, harnessing it for their explosions. Their idea of a proper introduction however, lacks the same sort of impressiveness. Once per story, the Sorcerer may stunt her over the top and theatrical introduction to a unknown group, gathering (3*Stunt Rating) sorcery motes that last until the story ends.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers who adopt the <b><i><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">8-Ignition Way | Darker than Black and Blacker than Dark: Brilliance that Burns with the Fury of the Crimson Demon Clan\u2013 The Path of Explosions</span></span></i></b> share the same merits as those who make a Pact with an Ifrit Lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11858-seibahismaiwaifu","name":"SeibahIsMaiWaifu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T12:44:19-07:00","id":926568,"title":"","content":"Just created one for a home-brewed Second Circle Demon: Pretty similar to Mara's, but has its own twists. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/2016/07/05/sorcerous-initiation-of-cecaelia/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg?m=1383295312i\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/2016/07/05/sorcerous-initiation-of-cecaelia/\" target=\"_blank\"> Sorcerous Initiation of Cecaelia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/2016/07/05/sorcerous-initiation-of-cecaelia/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://tentacledvitriol.wordpress.com/2016/07/05/sorcerous-initiation-of-cecaelia/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sorcery, in 3E, has changed significantly. &nbsp;Not only do you now draw motes in from the environment rather than spending your own to power spells, the various sorcery Charms now come with their own &hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T13:40:50-07:00","id":927764,"title":"","content":"This is kind of weird, but hey.<br /> <br /> <b>SURROGATE OF KAL'KAYA</b><br /> Kal'Kaya is a Second Circle Demon with a strange obsession with birth and motherhood. She appears as a teenage girl, many-armed and bearing the swell of pregnancy, her eyes the slot-pupiled gaze of goats and her feet like those of a great landbound predator bird. The sorcerer gained their power through a pact with the Barren Mother; they allowed her to use them as a conduit for the birth of one of her children, and in turn she has granted them sorcerous enlightenment. They gain a supernatural Major Principle toward protecting pregnant women, new mothers, and babies; if this is reduced below Major intensity, they take a -4 penalty to all sorcerous rolls until the Principle resumes Major or higher intensity. They also gain a mundane Minor Tie of some positive nature toward Kal'Kaya, but this has no bearing on their sorcery in particular.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Shaping Ritual:</u> Miracle of Birth</b><br /> Kal'Kaya's obsession with procreation allows her surrogates to draw on it for sorcerous power. Once per day, when the sorcerer contributes to a procreative act, they may roll (Charisma + Occult) with (Essence) automatic successes, each success being a sorcerous mote held in a pool whose maximum capacity is 10 sm. The definition of &quot;contributing to a procreative act&quot; is fairly broad; while becoming pregnant or impregnating another person obviously counts, it is also valid to play an important part in the procreation of others---for example, inspiring two lovers to have procreative sex. Serving as a midwife also counts. A sorcerer who is themselves pregnant gets to double up, so to speak, in that they may make this roll when the child is conceived and when the child is born (the tradeoff obviously being the difficulties of pregnancy).<br /> Participating in nonprocreative sex gives a reduced benefit; Kal'Kaya appreciates the symbol of the act, but not as much as the real thing. This allows the same roll, but with no automatic successes and 10s do not double on it.<br /> The motes thus gained last for one week.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Associated Merits</b></u><br /> <b>Demonchild Familiar (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b>: Kal'Kaya sees fit to leave her child with their surrogate parent; the demonchild functions as a three-dot Familiar. They have a Major Tie of love to their surrogate parent and a Defining Tie of love to Kal'Kaya. They share their surrogate parent's Major Principle of protection toward pregnant woman, new mothers, and babies.<br /> <b>Infernal Nobility (\u2022)</b>: As in the core; First Circle Demons have a Minor Tie of terrified awe, while Second and Third Circle Demons have a positive Minor Tie of respect or something similar.<br /> <b>Matchmaker's Eyes (\u2022\u2022)</b>: When making rolls to see if characters have Ties of romantic and/or erotic love for one another, the surrogate gets their Essence in automatic successes.<br /> <br /> If this is unbalanced or anything, I'd love to see what people think would make it more balanced. This is really just a weird idea I had driving home, but thought it could be hammered into something interesting. Ideas for other shaping rituals for this Initiation would be cool to hear as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 07-09-2016, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T14:46:00-07:00","id":931029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SeibahIsMaiWaifu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=922474#post922474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't sleep again so I decided I might as well repost this from the other forum I shared this on.<br /> A spell, an archtype, and a few shaping rituals</div> </div> </div> </div>I got back to you on the other forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:04:47-07:00","id":951386,"title":"","content":"Howdy hey. Reviving an old thread to ask for some help with a new sorcerous initiation. This is revisiting an older subject mentioned on this thread about a Wood-themed counterpart to the Pact with an Ifrit Lord initiation.<br /> <br /> One of my characters is a Haltan giant (as per the Merit) with maxed out Strength, Supernal Athletics, and three dots of Mighty Thew. I'm hoping that those traits and her reverence for nature might endear her to an elder greenmaw (3e pg. 518). What could a pact with such an elemental offer her in terms of shaping rituals and merits?<br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals:<br /> - In terms of shaping rituals, perhaps I could refluff Mara's third ritual to depend on plant-based cover/concealment instead of shadow?<br /> - This one's a bit more of a stretch, but it might be possible to mirror the ifrit lord's second ritual with a (Wits + Craft or Survival) roll reflecting a project to care for plants, e.g. farming or planting saplings.<br /> - The third Soul-Perfecting Elixir ritual might be admissible as-is.<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> - Perhaps Giant could be allowed as a Purchased Merit through this initiation, though there might be some obvious supernatural effects similar to the Wood Aspect markings. Those who are already giant might add (Stamina/2) dice to feats of strength. Subsequent supernatural Merits like bark-themed Unusual Hide might be admissible.<br /> - On a similar note, a mirror of Tempered by the Elements (Forests and Jungles) wouldn't be out of place, and it might provide an additional bonus to those who already have that Merit, such as {Essence/2) additional dice on Survival rolls in appropriate terrain.<br /> - A mirror of Infernal Nobility with regard to wood elementals and appropriate gods in place of demons.<br /> - Living Spirit Cultivation from the Soul-Perfecting Elixir initiation already specifies the element of wood.<br /> <br /> Let me know what you think, and if you have any further suggestions. Thanks for your help! :-3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","name":"Yatogami Odin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:44:33-07:00","id":951452,"title":"","content":"While I don't see any mechanical problem with a concealment-based ritual, it doesn't feel very greenmaw to me. They are big, and they smash. Possibly something based on stunting environmental destruction? Or, if you want, something based on blending in with the background (the way greenmaws could be mistaken for trees or vines) (i they were very small).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T20:24:57-07:00","id":951464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=951452#post951452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't see any mechanical problem with a concealment-based ritual, it doesn't feel very greenmaw to me. They are big, and they smash. Possibly something based on stunting environmental destruction? Or, if you want, something based on blending in with the background (the way greenmaws could be mistaken for trees or vines) (i they were very small).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, it's not so much that it's based on concealment, but that having enough plants around that you <i>could</i> conceal yourself is the criterion for the ritual. In other words, &quot;you need to be surrounded by plants&quot; is (mechanically) ambiguous, where &quot;you need to be surrounding by plants capable of providing at least light cover&quot; is not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","name":"Yatogami Odin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T21:33:40-07:00","id":951487,"title":"","content":"Oh, that sounds like a pretty good plan!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T22:20:52-07:00","id":951505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=927764#post927764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Associated Merits</b></u><br /> <b>Demonchild Familiar (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b>: Kal'Kaya sees fit to leave her child with their surrogate parent; the demonchild functions as a three-dot Familiar. They have a Major Tie of love to their surrogate parent and a Defining Tie of love to Kal'Kaya. They share their surrogate parent's Major Principle of protection toward pregnant woman, new mothers, and babies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not as an ally? Or is the demon child inhuman enough to count as a familar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:57:07-07:00","id":951892,"title":"","content":"In some traditions, a familiar is a demon or spirit, embodied in either animal form or a more, well, demonic shape. They're never very humanlike, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:02:52-07:00","id":953215,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">Here's a write-up of the concept I posted earlier. Please let me know what you think. :-3<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ______________________<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Pact with an Elder Greenmaw</b></span><br /> <br /> As greenmaws age, they become stronger, wiser, and more keenly attuned to the flow of Essence. Some of these elders may be willing to pass on their insights to those who swear to revere and protect nature.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Shaping Rituals</b></i><br /> <br /> The sorcerer borrows power from the profusion of flora around her. Whenever she begins a scene amidst foliage or other plant life in sufficient size or quantity to provide cover or concealment, she gains three sorcerous motes, which last until the end of the scene and can be spent toward any spell she casts.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer's patron offers her power in exchange for her service in protecting and maintaining the life and beauty of the realm. At the end of a project where she cares for plants, the sorcerer may make a prayer roll (Wits + Survival or an appropriate Craft) with a difficulty commensurate to the scale of the project: difficulty 5 for a project on par with maintaining a garden, difficulty 3 for a farm, and difficulty 1 for a forest or similarly large region. Success grants her sorcerous motes equal to (her Essence + extra successes on the roll). These motes last for the duration of the story, and can be spent toward any spell she casts. She cannot pray for power more than once a day, and receiving new motes replaces any granted by past prayers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">So long as the sorcerer abides by an ascetic lifestyle where she does not consume or use products made from animals or from inorganic materials<span style=\"color:#000000\">, she receives (Stamina) sorcerous motes after a <span style=\"color:#000000\">night of sleep, plus additional sorcerous mote for every <span style=\"color:#000000\">point of deprivation penalties she suffers. These sorcerous <span style=\"color:#000000\">motes last until she next sleeps, and can be spent towards <span style=\"color:#000000\">any spell she casts. Additionally, once per story, she may <span style=\"color:#000000\">spend a scene in meditation to unlock (Essence + Stamina) <span style=\"color:#000000\">sorcerous motes which last the duration of the story. <span style=\"color:#000000\">Compromising the ascetic lifestyle of this shaping ritual <span style=\"color:#000000\">causes the sorcerer to lose all motes granted by it, and <span style=\"color:#000000\">denies her its benefits for the remainder of the story.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Notes: I'm not entirely satisfied with the first or last ritual, as the first (copied from Mara's third) lacks a secondary condition under which the sorcerer can gather sorcerous motes, and the requirements for the last are a bit nebulous. I was trying for something like a vegan lifestyle combined with a DnD druid's oath not to use metal, but I'm not sure if that's appropriate; greenmaws themselves frequently eat animals in the early stages of their lives.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Merits</b></i><br /> <br /> - <b>Brimming with Life</b> (Merit <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): This</span> Merit functions as the Giant Merit, except that it is not considered Innate. If the sorcerer already has the Giant Merit, she may add (Stamina/2) in non-Charm dice when attempting feats of strength. However, the sorcerer becomes so infused with life that she gains plant-like traits, such as a pine-like aroma, brilliant emerald skin, or flowers in her hair. This imposes an additional -4 penalty to disguise rolls and may cause people to perceive her as a Wyld mutant. In dubious compensation, possessing this Merit allows the sorcerer to purchase additional supernatural Merits that are appropriate to plants, e.g. bark-like skin or a poisoned body.<br /> <br /> - <b>Green Warden</b> (Merit <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022)</span>: Wilderness gods and wood elementals recognize the sorcerer as a protector of their domain, and are treated as having a Minor Tie of respect towards her, or some variation suitable to their individual natures.<br /> <br /> - <b>Woodland Stride</b> (Merit <span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022\u2022)</span>: This Merit functions as Tempered by the Elements in jungle and forest terrain. If the sorcerer already has this Merit, she gains an additional (Essence/2) non-Charm dice on Survival rolls in these areas.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","user":"Yatogami Odin","date":". 09-09-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","name":"Yatogami Odin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T05:30:17-07:00","id":953759,"title":"","content":"<b>The Art of the Sword</b><br /> <br /> The Art of the Sword was developed by Demon Hunters and craftsmen in the far North. Using an alloy of feather-steel and powdered Blue Jade, the apprentice spends hours within the cold caves on the slopes of Ascension, forging the blade without flame. Those who fail this test invariably are possessed by their lower soul and become horrible, twisted monsters. For those who pass, they are brought up to Ascenion, where they spend several weeks training in the arts of swordsmanship, and learning the mannerisms of the various enemies of Creation. Finally, before they complete their apprenticeship they are brought beyond the edge of the world, to a floating island. They are left there, to learn the final secret of their Art, meditating on a massive Old Realm character of Blue Jade that rests amidst the island. Within a week, those who's minds are too weak will have flung themselves off the edge of the island, driven insane by revelations they cannot understand; however, this is a rare event as most who come this far have cultivated both mind and body to incredible extremes.<br /> <br /> Most individuals who leave the island have developed Stormwind Rider or Cirrus Skiff as their control spell, but there are occasionally those who instead develop the Infallible Messenger. The Order then divides them between the Dervishes, itnerants, riding their storms to wherever they are needed, the Lords, who often make pacts with various elementals of the air and travel in slow, majestic processions across the North, waging terrible war on their foes, and the Eyes, who use their Messengers to co-ordinate the Order in its ceaseless quest to rid the North of the Undead, vicious demons and fae. Sometimes, they will even fight rogue gods. But one thing they all have in common is a strange serenity.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> <br /> The Swordsman has sealed his Po soul within his sword. It feeds on those slain by the sword, and upon striking a killing blow, the wielder may gain 3+(Wielder's essence + Victim's essence) Sorcerous Motes which last until the next sunrise. However, if the wielder slays more than 5 creatures this way, the Po soul grows violent, and immediately expends all gathered Sorcerous Motes, creating a Bonefire Hazard that lasts one turn and is centered on the Swordsman, reaching out to short range. This Shaping Ritual allows the purchase of the Flying Sword Merit below.<br /> <br /> The Swordsman takes joy in practicing the sword. By performing a mystical sword kata each morning and on every night of the full moon, he attains a deeper understanding of swordsmanship and how it relates to the world around him. While wielding the sword, the sorcerer adds his melee/2(round up) to as many as (Melee) Shape Sorcery Actions per scene. This Ritual is gained for free alongside the previous one.<br /> <br /> The Swordsman has sealed his entire soul inside the sword, becoming an abomination outcast by the Order. By drawing on the vital force of whichever unfortunate person happens to wield such a cursed blade(easily recognisable by the colour of the steel, which becomes pure white), the sorcerer within the sword may gain sorcerous motes equal to the wielders permanent willpower although this reduces the wielders permanent willpower by 1. This Shaping Ritual requires the purchase of the Flying Sword Merit and the Sword-Body Forging Merit, but is gained for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Flying Sword(3-dot familiar)</b><b>:</b> The Swordsman seals his Po within the sword, giving it an animating force. The sword may fly and make melee attacks using its wielders Wits+Melee or Int+Melee. However, if the Swordsman fails to roll even a single success, the blade will refuse to obey, and must be picked up again by hand and flung in the air before it will fly again.<br /> <br /> <b>The True Sword(4-dot Merit):</b> The Order teaches its members how to strike with swords in such a manner that they may strike even invisible and intangible creatures. Although they suffer penalties for blindness as normal, those who possess this merit may expend 2 Sorcerous motes to strike immaterial beings with their attacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Sword-Body Forging(5-dot Merit): </b>The Swordsman truly becomes one with his sword, commencing a second forging process, much like his first in the caves below Ascension. As the forging progresses, the Swordsman slowly finds his body absorbed by the blade as his soul comes back together within the blade. At the end of the forging process, the sword becomes a sentient being with the memories of its wielder. However, it also gains a Defining Principle to slay any demon, ghost or fae it comes across. However, it is also immortal unless completely destroyed, slowly regrowing from a core of white diamond. The grip and hilt grow first, followed by the blade.<br /> <br /> Only one Exalt has ever attempted the Sword-Body Forging. The Lunar's Exaltation remained inside its body a few days more, which did not assimilate with the blade. The creature wreaked havoc across the north, driven mad by the division of Soul and Exaltation, before the Order bright the creature down with the help of the Wyld Hunt. However, this is not to say that fusing one's soul with the sword is impossible for the Exalted; such limits after all, can be overcome. However, unless the blade is made entirely of magical materials, it will not contain the Exaltation, and the use of Charms still requires a suitable body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:01:44-07:00","id":954053,"title":"","content":"Here's an initiation for all of you Clash-monkeys out there.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiate of Strife</b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Students of countless quarrels, the Initiates of Strife find enlightenment through conflict. Learned at the feet of countless War gods, Fae, Demons, or elder Chosen, this tradition stretches back to the Primordial Age, passed down through various dojos, gladiatorial academies, warrior fraternities, and the patronage of not a few Third Circle Demons. Though outwardly gruff and quick to anger, practitioners of this path place a deep reverence on honest conflict and the prospect of engaging a worthy opponent.<br /> <br /> <i>Shaping Rituals</i><br /> The sting of battle is food and drink for an Initiate of Strife, the ebb and flow of conflict attuning him to the Essence of Creation. Whenever the Initiate would normally be subject to Wound or Onslaught penalties, regardless of any Charms he has active or Merits he would benefit from, he gains Sorcerous Motes equal to the sum of those penalties, to a maximum of 10 Sorcerous Motes. Additionally, whenever he gains or loses Initiative as the result of hitting or being hit by a Withering attack, he may Reflexively take a Shape Sorcery Action, provided he was not Crashed by the attack.<br /> <br /> Initiates are always perceptive of opportunity on the battlefield, turning a moment of advantage into fuel for their magics. Whenever the Initiate would succeed at performing a Gambit, he gains Sorcerous Motes equal to the Threshold Successes on the Initiative roll, to a maximum of 10 Sorcerous Motes.<br /> <br /> The ultimate expression of their style of magic comes in meeting might with might and parlaying that exchange into sorcerous power. Whenever the Initiate Clashes, regardless of who wins the Clash, he gains Sorcerous Motes equal to the Threshold Successes on the Clash roll, to a maximum of 10 Sorcerous Motes.<br /> <br /> <i>Merits</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ferocious Countermagic (Merit \u2022\u2022):</b> The Initiate learns to confront enemy magics head-on, with harrowing effects. Whenever the Initiate attempts to counter a spell, he inflicts Withering Damage equal to the amount of Sorcerous Motes drained to the caster.<br /> <br /> <b>Last-Ditch Counter (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Initiates live by the maxim that the best defense is a stronger offense, and in the face of magic they can not counter, they fall back on the strength of their connection to Strife to overwhelm enemy spells. Whenever they are target by a spell that rolls to hit, an Initiate may spend Sorcerous Motes to Reflexively Clash that attack with an Intelligence + Occult roll. The Initiate must be within Close range of the casting Sorcerer, and must spend Sorcerous Motes based on the Circle of the Spell being Clashed: 5 motes for Terrestrial Spells, 10 for Celestial Spells, 20 for Solar Spells. If the Initiate wins the Clash, the casting Sorcerer takes Withering Damage equal to the Initiate\u2019s Intelligence + Essence + Threshold Successes - soak.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Any good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":".  I want feedback. 09-01-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:29:53-07:00","id":957971,"title":"","content":"Does anyone think that the Occult Charm &quot;Carnal Spirit Rending&quot; could be used to make a sorcerous initiation? Just thinking that it grants power by consuming the essence and powers of spirits, it seems like it could make for an interesting initiation. What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12042-zyxtal","name":"Zyxtal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T05:42:46-07:00","id":958167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zyxtal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=957971#post957971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone think that the Occult Charm &quot;Carnal Spirit Rending&quot; could be used to make a sorcerous initiation? Just thinking that it grants power by consuming the essence and powers of spirits, it seems like it could make for an interesting initiation. What do you all think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something similar has previously crossed my mind, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:07:34-07:00","id":960628,"title":"","content":"<b>Divine Law</b><br /> <br /> By studying the laws of divinity, left behind by the Primordials, the sorcerer gains insight into the workings of the world. However, the laws are hidden. In one place, a mountain range depicts half of the law of waves while it's reflection in the lake below show the other half. In the far west, a whirlpool and a storm form in turns in the same place, declaring the law of seasons. The course of the sun and moon still occasionally divide the stars in such a manner that someone who knows what he's looking for can understand the basics of the law of time. Those rare souls who seek this knowledge are often consumed by the search for the laws and the study of them. Most are already initiated into sorcery, and Exalted. Indeed, this initiation is most common among Sidereals seeking initiation into the arts of Celestial Sorcery. Below are some examples.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> <br /> The Law of Seasons dictates the turning of the great wheel of seasons. By drawing on the symbols of an appropriate season in a stunt the sorcerer may gain (Stunt Rating) Sorcerous Motes once per spell. If the sorcerer casts a spell that draws on the symbology of the season that follows a spell that he has just cast - For example, casting Claws of the Wood Dragon and then immediately casting Flight of the Brilliant Raptor - The sorcerer may conserve any excess motes for the following spell. He may continue doing this so long as he follows the cycle of Air, Water, Wood, Fire, Earth and Calibration. A spell without clear seasonal associations may be cast at the end of the cycle. Otherwise, the sorcerer may cast any spell at that point without breaking the spell. <i>This one I changed</i><br /> <br /> The Law of Time is the most esoteric of Laws. It allows a Sorcerer to take two Shape Sorcery Actions and then choose the better one as he glimpses into the future or draws on some power from the past. However, the use of such a power has a price; the Sorcerer suffers a cumulative -1 penalty to all perception rolls as past, present and future overly into constantly more confusing messes as he reaches further forward or back. <i>And this one I like.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Bonus General Ritual:</i> By meditating on a Law related to his control spell, the sorcerer may cast his control spell ahead of time and disperse it into the law of Creation. At any later point, the sorcerer may call upon the spell, provided that the related Law affects his current area. The sorcerer may store 1 Celestial or 2 Terrestrial Spells, and no more, in such a manner.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Crowned King of the World(5-dot merit)</b> The sorcerer may freely call upon all natural phenomena, summoning fire, ice or lightning, waves of water or causing the roots and branches of trees to grasp his foes. He may shake the earth or call boulders from the sky. He is crowned king of the earth, and granted a crown of 12 perfect diamonds which grow out of his skull. He may spend 1 mote to activate 3 of the gems for a scene. For each 3 gems so activated, he may upgrade the statistics of a weapon. With no gems active, he has merely the powers of a light mundane weapon, equivalent to a bow. With 3 gems active, this becomes a medium weapon. At 6, a heavy mundane weapon. At 9, it becomes a light artifact weapon. To activate the final 3 gems, however, he must also expend a willpower point, and takes one level of unstoppable lethal damage. However, he gains access to a medium artifact weapon. Mortals may fuel this merit with sorcerous motes gathered specifically for that purpose. <i>The Exalted may develop Evocations for this crown, that function at any time, along the themes of Laws they have discovered and studied. Laws may be purchased as specific Lore or Occult specialties (E.g The Law of Time) but one may never truly understand more than (Essence x 2) such laws. Solars may teach Laws beyond such limits as they are the Givers of Law.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","user":"Myradmir","date":".  It was confusing. And I like complicated things, so I added some complicated things. But I think it's improved. 09-01-2016, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:48:54-07:00","id":960652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myradmir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=960628#post960628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T16:12:16-07:00","id":960730,"title":"","content":"I think it's an initiation based on the laws of physics? Honestly, I think it would be better to make Waves their own initiation with a shaping ritual each for sound, light and water/wind, and then one based on Seasons and Time, but I did quite like the fluff at the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T07:27:31-07:00","id":961653,"title":"","content":"Note to self: Do not write without being actually in a coherent state of mind. I like the fluff, but I can't execute it properly it seems. So I'll drop the rituals(Except for the wave one, since that seems good... Just redivided) and replace it with something else.<br /> <br /> <b>The Art of Waves</b><br /> Arising on the shores of the North-East where voices echo in valleys of ice, light is bent through age-old frozen waves and the great Western ocean slowly eats away even the greatest of mountains, those sorcerers who study the art of waves seek to understand and become part of this mesmerizing dance. <br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> <br /> The waves of the sea are chaotic, influenced by the wind and the movement of celestial bodies, as well as being repelled by the earth. However, they may erode mountains, given time. While away from the sea, the Sorcerer may perform this ritual by imitating the movement of waves in a short dance. This always grants 3 sorcerous motes. While at sea, the Sorcerer may instead add (Craft) or (Performance) dice to a shape sorcery roll as he moves with the waves or folds them into the creation of his spell. <br /> <br /> The sorcerer recalls the Echoes of Power, and draws in sounds. While sounds can always be called into creation in even the stillest of caves, their widespread existence is confused, twisted by walls and drowned by the vastness of the sky. Thus they only grant limited amounts of power and may only be called on once a scene, granting (Performance) Sorcerous Motes.<br /> <br /> Waves of light grant varying amounts of power as the sun and moon move across the sky. Artificial light or firelight can also be a source of power, but even the greatest inferno produces less power than the Moon. The Sun provides 5 Sorcerous motes. The Moon provides 4, while artificial light grants between 1-3 motes depending on the strength of the source. Light sources may not be drawn on more than once a scene, and colour spells appropriately: The sun will turns flames gold, for example, while the moon will turn them silver. This has no mechanical effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Call of the Waves(3-dot merit): </b>As the Burning Name, save that the manipulation of light and sound waves also allows for a greater variety of stunts, and as such the cost of the merit has been adjusted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:45:09-07:00","id":962692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SeibahIsMaiWaifu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=917797#post917797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like some feedback on one I brewed up this afternoon.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800080\">Tyrant's Flame</span></b><br /> The draconic will of the Desert Tyrant burns within the Sorcerer, an inferno of energy that shapes sorcerous motes with it's presence alone.<br /> Once per story, the Sorcerer may roll (Temporary Willpower+Occult), forcing their will onto Creation to gather sorcerous. For each success, the Tyrant Flame within his heart feeds on the sorcerous motes gathered, channeling the amplified essence and burning it onto the Sorcerer's own flesh which appears as bands of runes, one each per success.<br /> Once per scene, the Sorcerer may reflexively consume a band of tattoos, instantly receiving a surge of (Essence*2) Sorcery Motes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who/what is the Desert Tyrant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T21:40:00-07:00","id":963090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=962692#post962692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Who/what is the Desert Tyrant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some sort of dragon, presumably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T04:22:27-07:00","id":963160,"title":"","content":"<b>Divine Lotus Meditation</b><br /> <br /> Those individuals who have amassed worship find themselves empowered; sorcerers thus empowered can find the truly perfect form of meditation, allowing the prayers of their people to wash over them. Some few among these discover how to take these prayers and form them into raw sorcerous power. Those that do manifest a massive lotus flower of essence when they meditate.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> <br /> Rather than drawing willpower from his cult, the Sorcerer may enter a state of meditation for a few minutes in the morning, taking time to hear the prayers of their people and drawing in their worship. For the day, they may not draw on willpower from their Cult, nor may they do this if the amount of willpower they could draw from their cult per story is already exhausted. Instead, they gain (Cult Rating x 3) Sorcerous Motes for the day.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Lightning-Flame Sutra(3-dot Story Merit):</b> This is an exercise in divine power, allowing the sorcerer to generate and manipulate flames, although flames so controlled become clearly unnatural. Most commonly the flame is streaked with small lightnings. This Merit works like the Burning Name, however it also allows the Sorcerer to parry fire-based attacks without a stunt and add the Flame tag to his attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:30:36-07:00","id":966346,"title":"","content":"Just tossing an idea out there, since I have nowhere near enough experience with the system to actually put this into the game, but would Martial Arts as an initation work? Simply the perfect understanding of yourself, relative to the world around you, and the discipline granted by MA allowing you to do sorcery? <br /> <br /> <br /> On the one hand, I'm not sure if this even works lore-wise. On the other hand, I also have no idea if this is even balanced; depending on how you gain motes (Doing katas, I guess? Doing MA charms to generate Sorcery Motes seems like it'd be a recipe for disaster), it might be way too easy to gain them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">BEHOLD! GLORIOUS SOLAR MONKEY!</span><br /> <br /> <br /> My avatar was made by <b>Jen!</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12377-raaabr","name":"raaabr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12377_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T12:20:18-07:00","id":966375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>raaabr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=966346#post966346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just tossing an idea out there, since I have nowhere near enough experience with the system to actually put this into the game, but would Martial Arts as an initation work? Simply the perfect understanding of yourself, relative to the world around you, and the discipline granted by MA allowing you to do sorcery?<br /> <br /> <br /> On the one hand, I'm not sure if this even works lore-wise. On the other hand, I also have no idea if this is even balanced; depending on how you gain motes (Doing katas, I guess? Doing MA charms to generate Sorcery Motes seems like it'd be a recipe for disaster), it might be way too easy to gain them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have a martial arts flavor, no prob, but keep in mind that shaping sorcery is its own action - you'd definitely be pushing into potential game-breaker territory if you allow a character to gain sorcerous motes while taking other combat actions.<br /> <br /> The Soul-Perfecting Elixir initiation could be refluffed into using martial arts rather easily. For instance, the elemental Merits could stem from mastering an associated kata rather than harmonization of one's body. The key here would be creating a shaping ritual that fits the image you're looking for.<br /> <br /> I'm not all that experienced with writing these things either, but maybe it could be something like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sorcerer draws power from embodying the principle of a style. This shaping ritual requires that the sorcerer activated a Form Charm earlier in the scene. If she performs an action that would allow her to reflexively activate the Form Charm she is currently using, she gains two additional sorcerous motes on her next shape sorcery action as long as that action is taken before the end of her next turn. If she has fully mastered the style associated with that Form Charm, she gains four additional sorcerous motes instead. She cannot draw more than ten sorcerous motes per scene with this ritual. </div> </div> </div>This is loosely modeled after Mara's first shaping ritual. The idea is if you had, say, a sorcerer who knows Snake Style, she could gain +2sm on her shape sorcery action if she was already in Snake Form when she withered an enemy from Initiative higher than her own to lower than her own. If she had learned Essence Venom Strike, she'd gain +4sm instead. Those two values fall within the range provided by Mara's first ritual, and I copied the 10sm/scene limit as well.<br /> <br /> That being said, it's generally much easier to perform a combat action than instill exploitable Intimacies (unless you happen to also be a Black Claw stylist or something), and there's also the potential concern that some Form Charms have easier special activation conditions than others, so this ritual might not be balanced for all styles.<br /> <br /> I wrote the ritual with the intent of it coming into play once every other turn at most, i.e. by alternating between combat and shape sorcery actions; perhaps that should be a hard-coded limitation. In any case, I just thought I'd throw it out there as possible inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","user":"Yatogami Odin","date":". 09-09-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","name":"Yatogami Odin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:34:18-07:00","id":968896,"title":"","content":"Hrm... so... idea:<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Initiation based off of the consumption of Chalcanth / Azoth (Demons melted down into liquid). How would that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1955-andoriol","name":"Andoriol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1955_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:56:01-07:00","id":968912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andoriol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=968896#post968896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm... so... idea:<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Initiation based off of the consumption of Chalcanth / Azoth (Demons melted down into liquid). How would that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you want the chalcanth to do for you. Once again, the Soul-Perfected Elixir provides a good starting place - the first shaping ritual could easily be refluffed to use eau de d\u00e9mon instead of conventional alchemical reagents, and the Merits could be refluffed to the internalization of and resonance with a particular demon species' Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","name":"Yatogami Odin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T20:54:55-07:00","id":968977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yatogami Odin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=968912#post968912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on what you want the chalcanth to do for you. Once again, the Soul-Perfected Elixir provides a good starting place - the first shaping ritual could easily be refluffed to use eau de d\u00e9mon instead of conventional alchemical reagents, and the Merits could be refluffed to the internalization of and resonance with a particular demon species' Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing(s) are:<br /> <br /> Chalcanth / Azoth shouldn't go bad, how does that affect the balance? Not to mention how much more dangerous rendering a demon into Chalcanth is than the brewing of the potion.<br /> <br /> The abstaining doesn't really fit into the whole 'decadant consumption of sapient / sentient beings for power' bit of consuming chalcanth.<br /> <br /> None of the merits the soul perfecting elixer provides are really in line with what I'd expect of Chalcanth, as they all link back up to the whole ascetic lifestyle thing. Something to do with Demonic Tattoos made from the Chalcanth-turned-demons would probably be more appropriate, but I'm struggling for ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1955-andoriol","name":"Andoriol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1955_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:09:24-07:00","id":968984,"title":"","content":"Didnt we discuss an initiation based on potions before?<br /> <br /> If not, we need to make one. Alchemy maybe a required skill though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:46:20-07:00","id":969005,"title":"","content":"Like I said, it's a starting point. However, what you're looking for seems to be much more involved than a sorcerous initiation; it sounds like what you want is closer to an artifact and a collection of Evocations. Shaping rituals aren't meant to be something that requires all that much effort - usually it's a simple roll or set of thematic conditions that give you a small boost of sorcerous motes. Brewing a potion is about as complex/difficult as it should get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","name":"Yatogami Odin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T21:54:46-07:00","id":969010,"title":"","content":"Well, my crunch-fu is not strong yet, so this is probably a horrible idea. Lets give this a try anyway though.<br /> <br /> <b>Elit Druin</b><br /> In North West Creation their lives an small group who have taken the mantle of defenders of Creation upon themselves. These shamans and druids originally began soon after the Great Contagion. Noticing that knowledge was being lost at an astounding rate, since people were burning books for warmth instead of reading them, the Elit Druin was formed by a former scholar named Walker in an attempt to reclaim and restore as much of the First Age knowledge as possible. From their home in the formally abandoned First Age fortress renamed to Cumhacht and partially converted into a library, the Elit Druin move freely though the area, being outside the tribal structure entirely. With Wyld mutants and Fair Folk incursions being a not unknown experience, these druids do occasionally have to answer the call to fight these monsters from beyond the border. However, since the loss of even one druid is seen as an enormous loss because of the knowledge and experience that she contains, more often the druid will attempt to move behind the scenes in order to produce similar results.<br /> <br /> Two areas embody the true core of the Elit Druin\u2019s power. While their actual names are lost to history, these areas are just called the Well and the Lake. Because of magically binding oaths that are taken while still alive, after the death of a druid her Po soul is immediately sucked into the Well while her Hun soul is taken to the Lake. Receiving the blessings of the dwellers of both Well and Lake is required in order for a person to be considered a member.<br /> <br /> <i>Shaping Rituals:</i><br /> A druid cannot make a normal Shape Sorcery Action. Instead she has a Sorcery Essence pool of Int + Lore x 3 that naturally recharges at one point per day. After the pool is depleted, casting spells ages the character at the rate of one year per 5 motes (round down). The only way to reverse this is by the Taste of Death ritual.<br /> <br /> <i>Other Benefits:</i><br /> <b>Living Fire</b> (Merit 2)<b>:</b> As The Burning Name but change to dice pool to (Intelligence + Lore). This fire is dark blue in color.<br /> <br /> <b>The Breath of Life</b> (Merit 2): As Astral Meditation.<br /> <br /> <b>The Taste of Death</b> (Merit 2): The Taste of Death is a twelve hour long ritual that must be conducted at the Lake. Upon the ritual\u2019s completion a dark, robed figure emerges out of the waters. The druid and the figure then bother sink beneath the still waters. During the druid\u2019s time in the Lake she begins to reverse the aging done to her by the casting of spells at a rate of one year of suspended animation for one year of spell induced aging. This will continue until the she is the same age as when The Taste of Death was bought. The Taste of Death also makes the character sterile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1882,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","user":"Ghost","date":". 09-14-2016, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:04:38-07:00","id":969060,"title":"","content":"I see what you did there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:13:43-07:00","id":969205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=969060#post969060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you did there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I sure hope so, it's a blatant rip off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T08:20:46-07:00","id":969237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yatogami Odin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=969005#post969005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, it's a starting point. However, what you're looking for seems to be much more involved than a sorcerous initiation; it sounds like what you want is closer to an artifact and a collection of Evocations. Shaping rituals aren't meant to be something that requires all that much effort - usually it's a simple roll or set of thematic conditions that give you a small boost of sorcerous motes. Brewing a potion is about as complex/difficult as it should get.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not disagreeing, but I'm also struggling to figure out how to do <i>any </i>of it. To either simplify it or to turn it into a sorcerous 'artifact' of sorts. That's <i>why</i> I'm asking for help XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1955-andoriol","name":"Andoriol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1955_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T11:15:26-07:00","id":969333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=969205#post969205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I sure hope so, it's a blatant rip off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What is it ripping off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T12:39:04-07:00","id":969388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andoriol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=969237#post969237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not disagreeing, but I'm also struggling to figure out how to do <i>any </i>of it. To either simplify it or to turn it into a sorcerous 'artifact' of sorts. That's <i>why</i> I'm asking for help XD</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're looking to simplify it, go with my earlier suggestion and peel off the abstinence bits since you didn't like those. For the refluffed Merits, maybe you'd instead need to maintain a lifestyle consistent with the imbibed demon's Essence.<br /> <br /> Take for instance the sesseljae, the stomach bottle bugs who eat poison and other such taint. If yours is the kind of character who would rather internalize the Essence of a sesseljae than actually summon and host one, you could revise Living Spirit Cultivation so that it grants the bonus vs. poison but requires you to ingest poison on a regular basis in lieu of maintaining an ascetic lifestyle to maintain its effect. This emulates the need to keep a sesseljae fed, but requires that the sorcerer expose herself to somewhat greater risk.<br /> <br /> You could go on and look through the other listed demons or make up your own to fit the other Merits. As a second example, maybe internalizing the songs of the angyalkae give clarity of mind analogous to Vital Focus Cultivation. Go with what you like and what you want, then come back and present concrete ideas. You'd be lucky to find someone willing to do all the work for you. ;-P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12245-yatogami-odin","name":"Yatogami Odin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T15:10:59-07:00","id":969484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=969333#post969333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is it ripping off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Terry Brooks' <i>Shannara</i> series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:20:06-07:00","id":979583,"title":"","content":"Hello all, I was just wondering if anyone has any ideas to get a sorcerous initiation similar to that of the Crystal Warrior series by William R. Fostchen? I really enjoyed the book series and I was thinking someone along the lines of a jewel-crafting character and this just seemed to coincide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T23:35:28-07:00","id":980606,"title":"","content":"Here is one me and my ST made together. Hope you enjoy.<br /> <span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tao Teh Ching Martial Sorcery</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theme</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The sorcerer learned their sorcery through rigorous training of martial arts and katas and hand seals. Through discipline, meditation, and determination the sorcerer delves into the corners of his mind and joins with the natural world to shape the world and essence around them.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> In the Monastery of Dreams both martial arts and sorcerous skills are taught. All students learn to cultivate their minds in meditation and their bodies in learning the katas and forms that shape them into masters of their respective paths. Most students only choose one of the two paths but the ancient masters of the monastery occasionally have a student who sees two roads to the same end and masters both martial and sorcerous skills. The Monastery martial arts focuses on weapon based arts and in using hand seals and wards for sorcery. Students of both paths have achieved some notable reputations around the Dreaming Sea as formidable warriors and dangerously competent sorcerers. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Ritual</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minds Inner Peace</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Once per day, By spending an hour in a quiet area in meditation the sorcerer can gain (MA rating) motes of essence that last until they goes to sleep. Also Once per Month, the sorcerer may take a misc action to focus himself through martial katas and making the motes stored by this ritual count for double for his spells, or triple for his control spell.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Ritual</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kata of the Formless Stance</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Once per day, the sorcerer perform breathing exercises and katas for at least 15 minutes to center himself and gains (MA rating) motes till they next rest. Alternatively, Once per week, If the sorcerer performs these exercises while leading a group of at least 5 disciples he gains(MA+Occ rating) motes instead. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Ritual</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerous Reaping Prana</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Through focused respiration and intense breathing techniques, the Martial Sorcerer may reap sorcerous motes from the shed blood of his enemies as he fights. Any attack against a non-trivial opponent that deals at least 5 points of initiative damage, or 1 level of decisive damage, he may gain and store 1sm. Additionally, any attack the Sorcerer successfully defends against with their martial arts derived parry, that is accompanied with a thematic stunt gains them an additional 1sm.These motes last til the end of scene and cap at (Ess+MA+Occ) motes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind\u2019s Maze Defense</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (4) - The sorcerer\u2019s mind is an inhospitable landscape for those that would try to manipulate or infiltrate it. The Martial Sorcerer gains +2 resolve against any magical effect that tries to sway/corrupt/confuse/mislead his mind. This works equally against charms like \u201cmental invisibility technique\u201d and against attempts of the fair folk to consume pieces of his soul, to sorcerous spells like \u201csilent words of dreams and nightmares\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind Over Body Resilience</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (2 or 4) - By drawing upon their inner strength the sorcerer can continue actions long after others grow to tired to carry on. For 2 points, the character may apply a -2 difficulty to all fatigue rolls, rolls to defer sleep, or any roll involving physical or mental endurance, including resisting the effects of torture and similar rolls.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For 4 points, the character gains the above benefit, and on top of that, he can ignore the effects of all but the most grievous of wounds. By spending a point of willpower, the character can ignore -1 wound penalties for scene though -2, -4 and incap still affect him normally.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:22:46-07:00","id":981653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=980606#post980606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is one me and my ST made together. Hope you enjoy.<br /> <span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tao Teh Ching Martial Sorcery</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Theme</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: The sorcerer learned their sorcery through rigorous training of martial arts and katas and hand seals. Through discipline, meditation, and determination the sorcerer delves into the corners of his mind and joins with the natural world to shape the world and essence around them.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> In the Monastery of Dreams both martial arts and sorcerous skills are taught. All students learn to cultivate their minds in meditation and their bodies in learning the katas and forms that shape them into masters of their respective paths. Most students only choose one of the two paths but the ancient masters of the monastery occasionally have a student who sees two roads to the same end and masters both martial and sorcerous skills. The Monastery martial arts focuses on weapon based arts and in using hand seals and wards for sorcery. Students of both paths have achieved some notable reputations around the Dreaming Sea as formidable warriors and dangerously competent sorcerers. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Ritual</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minds Inner Peace</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Once per day, By spending an hour in a quiet area in meditation the sorcerer can gain (MA rating) motes of essence that last until they goes to sleep. Also Once per Month, the sorcerer may take a misc action to focus himself through martial katas and making the motes stored by this ritual count for double for his spells, or triple for his control spell.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Ritual</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kata of the Formless Stance</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Once per day, the sorcerer perform breathing exercises and katas for at least 15 minutes to center himself and gains (MA rating) motes till they next rest. Alternatively, Once per week, If the sorcerer performs these exercises while leading a group of at least 5 disciples he gains(MA+Occ rating) motes instead. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shaping Ritual</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sorcerous Reaping Prana</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> - Through focused respiration and intense breathing techniques, the Martial Sorcerer may reap sorcerous motes from the shed blood of his enemies as he fights. Any attack against a non-trivial opponent that deals at least 5 points of initiative damage, or 1 level of decisive damage, he may gain and store 1sm. Additionally, any attack the Sorcerer successfully defends against with their martial arts derived parry, that is accompanied with a thematic stunt gains them an additional 1sm.These motes last til the end of scene and cap at (Ess+MA+Occ) motes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Merits</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind\u2019s Maze Defense</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (4) - The sorcerer\u2019s mind is an inhospitable landscape for those that would try to manipulate or infiltrate it. The Martial Sorcerer gains +2 resolve against any magical effect that tries to sway/corrupt/confuse/mislead his mind. This works equally against charms like \u201cmental invisibility technique\u201d and against attempts of the fair folk to consume pieces of his soul, to sorcerous spells like \u201csilent words of dreams and nightmares\u201d</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind Over Body Resilience</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (2 or 4) - By drawing upon their inner strength the sorcerer can continue actions long after others grow to tired to carry on. For 2 points, the character may apply a -2 difficulty to all fatigue rolls, rolls to defer sleep, or any roll involving physical or mental endurance, including resisting the effects of torture and similar rolls.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For 4 points, the character gains the above benefit, and on top of that, he can ignore the effects of all but the most grievous of wounds. By spending a point of willpower, the character can ignore -1 wound penalties for scene though -2, -4 and incap still affect him normally.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Appropriative but interesting. Name is a mouthful, and is guaranteed to discomfort people. Third Shaping Ritual doesn't make sense in context with the theme or the other Rituals. And as has been said multiple times in these forums, <b>always paste from a word processor as plain text.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:41:20-07:00","id":981667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>drakor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=980606#post980606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#4a86e8\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind\u2019s Maze Defense</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (4) - The sorcerer\u2019s mind is an inhospitable landscape for those that would try to manipulate or infiltrate it. The Martial Sorcerer gains +2 resolve against any magical effect that tries to sway/corrupt/confuse/mislead his mind. This works equally against charms like \u201cmental invisibility technique\u201d and against attempts of the fair folk to consume pieces of his soul, to sorcerous spells like \u201csilent words of dreams and nightmares\u201d</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I am missing something in your description or reading too much into of course, but I think this is quite strong for 4 merit points considering it has no other costs. Normally this costs 4 motes with an Integrity Excellency for just a moment. Empowered Soul Technique lets you do it cheaper for a single excellency use, but its still 2 motes. There might be other charms like Demure Carp Feint, but my point is that all of these have a 2m+ cost whereas this does it for free all the time versus any magical attack. I realize it limits the classiifcation somewhat, but its still quite strong for a merit. Its sort of like giving a person +2 Evasion versus all archery attacks for 4 merit points.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T17:41:04-07:00","id":990710,"title":"","content":"I wanted to create something which reflected a &quot;vampirism&quot; concept that embodied the elements of human sacrifice modeled in stories where sorcerers drain the &quot;life force&quot; of others to empower their dark arts, including where a sorcerer works a terrible ritual upon an entire city. I gave the thrust of it to the Shaping Ritual, then used the Merits to expand on it. The biggest challenge is creating a sense of temptation to purchase the (inherently horrifying) Merits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Essence Vampirism</b></span></span><br /> You have learned to harness the magic which sustains mortal life. Maybe you had an inborn talent which blossomed, or perhaps the revelation came from your own studies into human nature. You may tap into reservoirs of power within yourself which others can only dream of, but your talent extends beyond your own frame. Draining the life of others grants you a kind of power that inspires fascination and terror, both for the heights which you may achieve, and the horrors you must inflict to gain such strength.<br /> <br /> <i>Shaping Ritual</i><br /> <br /> The sorcerer may draw upon the life force of lesser mortals to empower his own sorcery. The sorcerer simply touches the victim and rolls Essence + Willpower to draw power from their victim. Successes drain motes, converting them into sorcerous motes on a 1-for-1 basis, first from peripheral, then from personal. If the victim has been drained entirely of motes (or, as in the case of mortals, has no motes in the first place), successes inflict Bashing damage instead.<br /> <br /> If in combat, treat this as a Gambit, with a Difficulty equal to the number of sorcerous motes you wish to drain. This represents reaching out, grabbing your opponent bare-handed in mid-combat, and sucking the life out of them.<br /> <br /> <i>Other Benefits</i><br /> <br /> <b>A Means to an End (5-dot Merit): </b>You may drain the lives of mere mortals to empower wondrous workings beyond their imagining. By draining several dozen lives, you may use their collective energy to your own ends, adding one to the Terminus of a roll/Means of a sorcerous working. The experience is harrowing, and all victims must make a Stamina + Resistance roll (difficulty depending on the project they are empowering) in order to survive, with a bonus equal to the group's Size. A sorcerer may instead gain two Means if they use this Merit to willingly drain enough people to death that it constitutes an unspeakable horror (such as the death of an entire city). Performing this requires either physically restraining individual victims or using a sorcerous working to create a magic circle which drains the victims (such a circle can potentially surround an entire city).<br /> <br /> <b>Detect Life (2-dot Merit): </b>You are attuned to the life force of others. As a simple action, the Sorcerer may detect whether there are any creatures nearby which possess an Essence rating. This costs 1WP and requires a successful Difficulty 1 Perception + Occult roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence Inspiration (5-dot Merit)</b><i>: </i>The life of others inspires your genius. By draining a victim to death, the sorcerer may convert their life force into Crafting Experience. Each dot of Essence converts into either 10 Silver Experience or 1 Gold Experience. To gain this benefit, the Sorcerer must describe a project which will benefit from this Merit. A project may benefit from only one expenditure of this Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Pyramid of Bones (4-dot Merit): </b>You have learned how to twist the Essence of mortals into the stuff of legends. They shall join something greater. You may take a slain being's Essence and use it as a component part in crafting Artifacts. The more powerful or exotic the Essence, the more useful it is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T21:49:36-07:00","id":990791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Sword Emperor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=990710#post990710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Detect Life (2-dot Merit): </b>You are attuned to the life force of others. As a simple action, the Sorcerer may detect whether there are any creatures nearby which possess an Essence rating. This costs 1WP and requires a successful Difficulty 1 Perception + Occult roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a better way to write this out would be to say that it may detect living creatures, both because that narrows its target down enough and because the core does not suggest that Essence 0 is a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T22:32:35-07:00","id":990802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=990791#post990791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a better way to write this out would be to say that it may detect living creatures, both because that narrows its target down enough and because the core does not suggest that Essence 0 is a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a good idea. I'd written it that way to encompass things like spirits and walking statues, as opposed to theoretical constructs and the like which don't possess their own Essence rating. However, that's a small enough category (potentially to the point of non-existence) that it's more confusing than helpful to suggest it.<br /> <br /> So, I'd go with either &quot;living creatures&quot; or revise it to specify &quot;anything with an Essence rating&quot;. More likely the former, in keeping with the theme that the vampirism focuses on mortal lives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T11:48:19-07:00","id":991053,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest &quot;naturally material living being.&quot; Demons are alive, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T09:34:49-07:00","id":994628,"title":"","content":"If this looks similar to anything in real-life, then it's probably a coincidence<br /> <br /> <b>The Power of Hate</b><br /> <br /> People said that hate make you weak and miserable, you said they are wrong ! You have been enlightened by the orange God-King, you have swallowed the red pill, and with this newly gained power, you'll show them, you'll show them all !<br /> <br /> <i>Shaping Ritual</i><br /> <br /> Anger and hate fuel the sorcerer with great power. By paying an additional Willpower when taking a shape sorcery action, the sorcerer gain sorcerous motes equal to half the number of his negative Ties. If the spell being cast is aimed at one of his negative Tie, then the additional Willpower cost is waived, this function can only be used once per Scene.<br /> <br /> Great power surged within the sorcerer when he makes other people depressed. He gains sorcerous mote every time he successfully create negative feelings in people: two motes for Instill a Minor Intimacy, three motes for a Major Intimacy, and four motes if it's a Defining Intimacy. Inspiring bitterness and resentment also give him three sorcerous motes if he successes.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer devise a plan to bring harm toward one of his negative Tie with a number of Steps equals to the Tie's intensity, these Steps are intermediary goals that meaningfully contribute to the sorcerer's actual goal. He can roll [Intelligent + Occult] and gain one sorcerous mote per success every time he complete one of the Step. These motes can only be used for spell with the intention of causing harm, whether physical or psychological, to the aforementioned Tie.<br /> <br /> <i>Other Benefits</i><br /> <br /> <b>Basket of Deplorables </b>(Merit \u2022): The sorcerer's sense is attuned to negative thoughts in such a deep level that he can sense it in other people, whether it's a feeling of anger or negative Tie. The sorcerer experiences a slight pull in the head anytime a person having these feelings is nearby, he'll need other means to locate the person and the exact nature of the negative thoughts however.<br /> <br /> <b>Heart of Centipedes </b>(Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022): Spite is the sorcerer lifeblood, literally. Time spends planning to bring harm to people counts as sleeping for the sorcerer. If the harm is aimed at one of the sorcerer's negative Tie then he also gains two Willpower instead of one after 8 hours &quot;sleep&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Thinskin Orangutan's Tantrump </b>(Merit \u2022\u2022): The humble gentlemen is surrounded with the evil vagenda of manocide inflicted again him everyday, and thus will needs a weapon to defend himself, one that's cultural and compassionate. Channeling a deep hatred within his heart, the sorcerer's insult can physically hurt the enemies, it has the stat of a ranged Light weapon with the Lethal and Throw (Short) tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 03-05-2017, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:59:53-07:00","id":994689,"title":"","content":"I think you left off the Merit where you erect a sorcerous wall around yourself and force your opponents to pay for it. Either way, I regret that I have only one like to give.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T19:04:12-07:00","id":996392,"title":"","content":"Has anyone done Sorcerous Initiations based on the 6 remaining <b>Living Books of Shaped in Malachite</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T05:06:38-07:00","id":997088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=994689#post994689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you left off the Merit where you erect a sorcerous wall around yourself and force your opponents to pay for it. Either way, I regret that I have only one like to give.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jen also forgot the Shaping Ritual wherein the sorcerer gains sorcerous motes from sexual assault, bragging about being powerful enough to get away with sexual assault, <i>or</i> from denying a former victim's accusation of wrongdoing by claiming the victim is too ugly for the sorcerer to target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-02-2016, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T12:50:32-07:00","id":1073835,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the thread necromancy! I'm looking for an initiation that's appropriate to a sorta Eclipse steppe horseman character, a Temujin of sorts. So I've been brainstorming a lot of ideas - occult theories that build upon the relationship between the herd/horse and the keeper, appeals to the spirits of the sky and earth, etc. But I lack any mechanical chops! Does anybody have any great ideas or contributions to this?<br /> <br /> I tried to examine the vast thread that preceded my request and I -think- I did a pretty good survey but if I missed anything that might be appropriate in there that you notice, please let me know!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T13:04:42-07:00","id":1073846,"title":"","content":"I'd do something about the sky and appeals to a sky god who taught it to them, potentially based in Tengrism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T15:29:11-07:00","id":1073906,"title":"","content":"Here are some Tengrism inspired shaping rituals, and merits. These are in a very crude and rough draft format (written on the fly on a break at work). None of this play tested, spell checked, or proof read.. <br /> <br /> <br /> By contemplating the vastness of creation, in the domain of Heparkus (SP?) (on an open plain touching dirt), under the open sky (able to see the sky as in unobscured clouds are fine), before &quot;Sky God&quot; initiate a ritual prayer (Charisma + Performance) (Prayer) roll gaining 1 SM per success up to a maximum of 10 + essence. These SM last until the next week and the sorcerer can spend a maximum of essence or 3 (whichever is lower) per turn to supplement a shape sorcery action to cast a spell. <br /> <br /> Emulating the thunderous power and righteous fury of the sky god, the sorcerer scream and cries ferociously during spellcasting. She performs a reflexive a threaten action against a single or all opponents. Threshold successes over the subjects resolve grant either 3+ threashold (group) or threshold successes in sorcerous motes to the shape sorcery action. The subject is not subject to the effects of the threaten action as the trembling fear of her opponents is transmogrified into sorcerous motes. These motes must be used by the end of the turn or they are lost. <br /> <br /> Spilling her blood in a sacrifice to the earth and Heparkus, the earth responds to her in kind. She gains 1 sorcerous mote for each health level sacrificed + the wound penalty of each health level to a total maximum of 10. These motes last a scene and may be spend in any amounts. <br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b>: <br /> <b>Furious Storming Hooves (OOO)</b>: Any environmental penalties to actions while mounted translate into non-charm bonus dice instead.<br /> <b>Blessing of the Sky and Earth (OO)</b>: If the sorcerous sleeps under the open sky upon unworked earth (read natural not city streets or castle ruins or what have you) She heals at twice the normal speed unaided by charms. <br /> <b>Summon the Storms Wrath (OOOO)</b>: Any shape sorcery action to summon bitter cold, lightening, or any other weather related spell receives (essence) bonus dice. Performing a shape sorcery action during a storm (defined as any weather strong enough to levy penalties to rolls) grant 1 additional sorcerous mote per roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T00:11:57-07:00","id":1074037,"title":"","content":"<b>World Shaping Glory</b><br /> Your character has learned to fuel his sorcerous power through his own fame and pride. Whether through the (surprisingly)secret arts of the Order of Stars Society, learned it under the feet of Nimb ,The Circling Light of Virdigis or just being an incredibly egotistical and sorcerously knowledgeable person.<br /> <br /> <i>Merits</i><br /> <i>Showtime </i>(ooooo): Once per story, when you are doing a stunted action seen by at least Size 3 people you may spend up to an additional 3 extra willpower that can only be used to add successes, one for one. This ability cannot be used on an Extended action.<br /> <i>Golden Tongue </i>(oo): The sorcerer decreases her social penalty by half of her (higher of individual Influence or Cult) round-up.<br /> <i>Ego Crushing Ego</i> (ooo). If she stunt a contested roll and wins, he gains 1 willpower point. This can only happen once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> The sorceror may draw power from the hearts of any adoring fans. Whenever he takes a shape sorcery action in medium range of a crowd who has a Tie of awe, amazement, fear, or other similar emotions then he gains additioal sorcerous motes equal to the crowds size(minimal 1), if there are multiple distinct crowds then he uses the one with the biggest Size and adds 1 for every group beyond the biggest.<br /> <br /> The sorceror\u2019s fame allows him to command the occult power of the world, for his glory must be acknowledged. By making a dramatic action, The sorceror gains sorcerous motes equal to (highest of individual Influence or Cult x 3) sorcerous motes which can be used on any spell, this motes last for the duration of the story. If his Influence or Status increases, whether increasing her existing ones or gaining a new one, the he gains another 3 sorcerous motes that last for the story.<br /> <br /> The sorceror\u2019s marks is something to prove her mastery of the world and her mastery of the world marks him. When she stunts a shape sorcery action involving the effects of her control spell or a sorcerous working then she gains (Essence+stunt rating) sorcerous motes, once per scene unless she rises back to Iconic Anima after falling down to Dim in the same scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11724,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","user":"backtoback","date":". 04-06-2017, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T02:58:04-07:00","id":1074069,"title":"","content":"-Which soul of the Demon City can teach this initiation?<br /> <br /> -How many successes does the &quot;Showtime&quot; Merit add?<br /> <br /> -What is &quot;Status?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-06-2017, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T03:34:51-07:00","id":1074075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1074069#post1074069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-How many successes does the &quot;Showtime&quot; Merit add?</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood the Merit to raise the cap on how many WP you can spend to add success to a single action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T03:40:50-07:00","id":1074078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1074075#post1074075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understood the Merit to raise the cap on how many WP you can spend to add success to a single action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and corrected other issues","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T20:08:51-07:00","id":1074485,"title":"","content":"The Great and Powerful Trixie appears to have acquired a minion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:52:42-07:00","id":1078515,"title":"","content":"Right now I've been watching a new anime called <i>Akashic Record of the Badtard Magical Instructor </i>, and the new episode had some sonething interesting. In the shiw, mages cast spells by 'runic chant', where they recite incantations (which in written form sre in a runic script). But, the instructor explained the words arent what's creating the spell. What they do is reformat the caster's subconscious to focus it on affecting the world around them. Now that sounds likecan awesome basis for a Sorcerous Initiation.<br /> <br /> so, what I need is ideas on how to flesh it out. I suck at crunch, so am looking for suggestions on the actual Initiations and Merits. Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T15:08:51-07:00","id":1079070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Hymns are Power (***) \u2013 With two dots in this merit, a sorcerer may substitute her Performance for her Occult when using shape sorcery actions.</i> </div> </div> </div>I'm considering something like this for an Orpheus based Sorcerer, but I'm guessing that it needs a rules caveat that you can't apply any Performance dice-tricks that don't have Occult equivalent Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T17:14:13-07:00","id":1079123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1079070#post1079070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm considering something like this for an Orpheus based Sorcerer, but I'm guessing that it needs a rules caveat that you can't apply any Performance dice-tricks that don't have Occult equivalent Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>A simpler option would be to allow the spellcaster to use Charisma instead of Intelligence for shaping rolls, or granting (Performance) doubled 9s on appropriate spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T03:56:48-07:00","id":1081373,"title":"","content":"<b>The Force of Principle</b><br /> <br /> This Shaping Ritual is an ancient one, but sees little practice in the modern day. First, it requires an individual to uphold a broad principle, such as valor, compassion, temperance or similar at a defining level. Next, the aspiring Sorcerer must find either someone who already knows this ritual and is attuned to the same principle, a temple dedicated to a divine entity that embodies this principle. If the principle in question is otherworldly, or foul, such as Hatred or Nihilism, this may require questing into the Wyld, or Hell, or the forgotten corners of the world. Once she has found such a temple, the aspirant meditates and prays, finally receiving enlightenment after three days and nights of continued prayer. During this time she may not act in any way contrary to the principle she seeks to embody, as judged by the God. If she instead finds a human teacher, the process is much the same, though she will be judged by a human rather than a God.<br /> <br /> Once she has passed this first trial, the god or teacher demands of her twelve services, each of which embodies a different aspect of the principle. For those expression valor, this often involves battles against mighty foes, questing to the most horrifying places of Creation and similar quests, while one charged for compassion might find himself doing long years of service in the most destitute and disease-ridden boroughs of the world. Each quest brings further and greater enlightenment, though completing the first suffices to initiate the Aspirant into Sorcery. However, if she deliberately fails to complete the following quests, she finds herself cast out of society entirely as she is cursed with an intangible mark that causes men and beasts to shy away from her, and causes her to be regarded with disgust even by the Fae and the denizens of Hell.<br /> <br /> A famous example of these twelve quests, and one of the major reasons this Shaping Ritual sees few practitioners in the modern day, are the quests imparted by a Nephwrack to a mortal who came to be known simply as the Shogun of the End. His first quest was to desecrate a pristine valley, sacred to Gaia. He burnt the forest within to the ground and salted the earth. His next quest was to poison all the water in a certain area in the South. To do this, he slew a great behemoth and watered the desert with its poisonous blood. His third quest and fourth quests are unknown, but tales abound of massive pyres of corpses, or some say still-living humans, of kingdoms toppled and castles shattered, but no scholar can confirm such rumours. His fifth quest is well known - Sink an inhabited island into the Underworld, so that the dead may feast on the flesh and blood of the living. The Shogun of the End raised a new island from the waters of the West, richly laden with gold and Jade. Atop the island, he planted a spear of Moonsilver whose siren song brought the Anathema from the edge of Creation. But the island was cursed so that all who saw it would desire it for themselves. War followed as the Anathema clashed with each other and with pirates, while armies were brought to bear against each other, and terrible sorceries twisted the world and shattered the ocean floor. Finally, the Shogun stepped forward, a staff of burning black stone in his hand and with him came a thousand thousand of the living dead, sailing on ships of bone. Three Lunars died that day, as did several pirate kings, their armies left stranded on the island as the weight of death and greed dragged it beneath the waves and below the world. Not only had the Shogun completed his fifth quest, but by slaying the Lunars he had accomplished his sixth as well. The quests continued in that vain, spreading death and destruction across the South and West, until they eventually threatened the Blessed Isle itself. Unfortunately for the Shogun, the Balorian Crusade put an end to his scheming and questing, and he and his armies perished before the eye of Balor long before he could fulfill his quest. His ghost, however, lingers on in the Underworld, where he still works towards the completion of his final quest, a steady adherent to the will of the Neverborn, the whims of the Nephwracks and the commands of the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> Not all quests are as demanding as those of the Shogun of the End, but he is one of the most legendary adherents of this Ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>Shaping Rituals</b><br /> <br /> Successful completion of a quest immediately garners the Sorcerer 20sm that she may use any time within the next three days.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer may stunt how a spell reinforces her Principle, and gains (3+Stunt rating)sm once per scene.<br /> <br /> The Sorcerer may violate her Principle by paying up to 3 points of willpower. For every point so spent, she reduces the intensity of her Principle by one and gains 5sm in addition to any she gains from a Shape Sorcery action. However, she may only do this in a scene where her principle starts at a defining level, and should she ever reduce her principle to nothing, she loses access to this shaping ritual and any related until she atones by retaking her vigil, and questing once more until her Principle is once more at Defining. None have ever been granted another chance after reducing their Principle to nothing a second time, and indeed are cursed like those who intentionally failed to complete their quests.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Fires of Passion(2-dot Merit):</b> The Sorcerer may unleash blasts of force appropriate to her principle. Those who follow Valor often hurl blasts of cold, harsh light, or call lightning from the sky to strike their foes, while those follow Temperance often call up gray mists that turn the flesh of their foes to stone or marble. Those who follow Compassion, while their weapons do deal lethal damage just like all others, need never fear the infection of wounds or death falling upon their foes if they do not wish it. Mechanically, the merit is otherwise identical to The Burning Name. No training time is needed to learn this power in the days following the completion of the 2nd or subsequent quests.<br /> <br /> <b>Visions of a Perfect World(4-dot Merit):</b> The Sorcerer gains an additional means to any Working that aids her Principle. If the Working would embody her Principle instead of merely aiding it, she also reduces its difficulty by 1. No training time is required to learn this power in the days following the completion of the 5th or subsequent quests.<br /> <br /> <b>Enlightenment of (Principle) (5-dot Merit):</b> The Sorcerer gains +1 dice to all actions that embody her principle, and reduces any difficulties of such actions by 1. Furthermore, her body now acts as a perfect channel of essence for such Principle. Design a Greater Hearthstone that represents the Principle. This grows out of the Sorcerers body at some point appropriate to the Principle. Compassion might produce a Stone of Innocents Protection, for example. No training time is necessary to develop this power following the completion of the 8th or subsequent quests.<br /> <br /> <b>Embodying the Force of Principle(5-dot Merit): </b>The Sorcerer gains the use of a charm identical to Glorious Solar Sabre, save that the cost of the charm may be paid in sorcerous motes left over after she casts a spell. She may develop evocations for this artifact as normal. This merit requires no training time after the Twelfth Quest is completed.<br /> <br /> <b>The Eternal Quest(3-dot Merit): </b>So long as she holds the Principle at a defining level, any time the sorcerer upholds her Principle and this brings her hardship that could have been avoided by violating the Principle, treat it as the completion of a Quest. This merit may only be purchased after completing the Twelfth Quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9312-myradmir","name":"Myradmir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T04:51:17-07:00","id":1081385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1079070#post1079070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm considering something like this for an Orpheus based Sorcerer, but I'm guessing that it needs a rules caveat that you can't apply any Performance dice-tricks that don't have Occult equivalent Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a reasonable assumption, yeah. I was writing it at a time before I really grasped how many dice tricks there were in the Solar charmset, so it didn't occur to me to do that. Generally, I think I wrote it with the assumption that it would change the excellency, possibly the dice pool, and very little else, though I might do it differently if I had the time to rewrite it in a significant way at this point in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T18:31:28-07:00","id":1126539,"title":"","content":"Has anyone converted the Salinan, Silurian, or Devonian schools to 3rd ed as initiations with shaping rituals and merits yet?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Just found Salinian by LadyLens<br /> Comment <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=804494#post804494\">#108</a> in this thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":977,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","user":"Major","date":". 08-12-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T22:02:24-07:00","id":1126580,"title":"","content":"I'm sure that coming.<br /> <br /> Or SHOULD be. Get on it writers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T10:15:27-07:00","id":1126758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1126539#post1126539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone converted the Salinan, Silurian, or Devonian schools to 3rd ed as initiations with shaping rituals and merits yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could swear I've seen a homebrew of the Salinan initiation, but I can't find it for the life of me. If I did, it was over a year ago at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T01:10:38-07:00","id":1145733,"title":"","content":"(PEACH)<br /> Hello all, this Sorcerous Initiation came to me while a player and I were working out a initiation similar to Mara's, but in this case the player asked for something from Orabilis so I used the Roll of Glorious Divinity write up for him, and had a little flash of inspiration crossing him with Hemaeus Mora from Skyrim in my head, and the awful stuff that happened to Pablo on Ash vs. Evil Dead. My biggest concerns are the balance of the evocations with the shaping rituals.<br /> <br /> Secrets of Orabilis<br /> This sorcerous initiation draws upon the ancient secrets that Orabilis has tried to conceal, taking his knowledge within yourself is the easy part, however surviving the experience and learning to shift his curses upon others is the difficult part.<br /> <br /> Shaping Rituals:<br /> Power from Black Secrets<br /> Like Orabilis you draw power from forbidden knowledge, however unlike him your power grows the more his attention is diverted by others learning these dark secrets. Whenever you take a shape sorcery action while within medium range of a character who knows any of the dark secrets of Orabilis you gain additional sorcerous motes equal to the depth of their knowledge. This is calculated through their Lore skill on a 1 for 1 basis, however if they are afflicted by the Dark Secrets evocation this increases by 3, and by 5 if they have been exposed to the Blasphemous Secrets evocation. The sorcerer can not draw more than 10 motes from this shaping ritual per scene.<br /> <br /> Punish the Seeker<br /> When the sorcerer teaches a willing mortal, the dark secrets of Orabilis she may choose to immediately feed their soul to Orabilis by directing his attention to them. In return he provides further power of sorcery to this seeker. The extracted soul visibly burns in chains forged of your anima, as you see the ultimate punishment for those who seek forbidden knowledge without the wisdom to protect themselves. As a miscellaneous action, the sorcerer may roll (Essence + Willpower) and gaining that many sorcerous motes. She retains these motes until the end of the scene, and may spend them towards any spells she casts. Additionally, a bound soul may be reflexively expended in place of a point of Willpower when paying the cost of the sorcerer\u2019s control spell. She cannot have more than (Essence + Occult) souls bound to her at one time.<br /> <br /> The Black Book<br /> The sorcerer draws power from ancient knowledge drawing it's power directly into him or her. Whenever she begins a scene near books she has yet to read, she gains 3 sorcerous motes, which last until the end of the scene and can be spent towards any spells he or she casts. Additionally, whenever she takes a shape sorcery action to shape a spell while within a library, she gains an additional sorcerous mote as long as the spell affects the sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> Infernal Nobility (Merit \u2022): Demons recognize the sorcerer as one who has avoided the wrath of Orabilis. First Circle demons are treated as having a Minor Tie of terrified awe towards her, while Second and Third Circle demons have a positive Minor Tie of respect, or some variation suited to their nature.<br /> <br /> Demonic Tutor (Merit \u2022\u2022): One of the Black Tutors of this path appears in the sorcerer\u2019s dreams, feeding her with fragments of the incinerated souls that Orabilis has punished. Once per story, the sorcerer\u2019s player may declare that she is visited by a Tutor in a dream while sleeping. She does not recover Willpower from that sleep, but receives some significant benefit determined by the Storyteller such as tutelage in a new spell in a single night, double 9s on all shape sorcery spells for the next day, the service of a First Circle demon as an enslaved spirit, or something similar. She also wakes with a Minor Principle of \u201cI take pleasure in sharing cursed knowledge,\u201d or strengthens that Intimacy if she already possesses it.<br /> <br /> Demonic Script Tattoos (Merit \u2022\u2022\u2022): The Black Tutors have marked the sorcerer, taking one or more of the destroyed souls and rendering it down into a midnight-black tattoo that contains the forbidden knowledge of Orabilis. The sorcerer may unlock the following Evocations from these tattoos, or manipulate or empower summoned demons, such as by turning them into the seekers of old.<br /> Evocations:<br /> Black Secrets<br /> Cost: 3m; Mins: Essence 1<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Decisive-only, Black Secrets<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisites: None, (Free with purchase of the Demonic Script Tattoos)<br /> <br /> This evocation is the first of those provided by the Demonic Script Tattoos, it allows you to target an enemy within the range of your voice, and pass onto them the blackest of secrets this spreads across across the ground like a black shadow before crawling up their skin revealing lines of text, it then sweeps over their eyes blinding them as these dark things demand to be read.<br /> <br /> This works in one of two ways either as a Decisive Gambit, that ignores cover and uses an artifact thrown attack with the dice pool being Manipulation + Linguistics roll at up to medium range to curse your foe, or as a normal Decisive Attack at up to medium range. As a Gambit, if you hit or miss you spend 4 initiative, but do not reset your initiative as normal for a gambit.<br /> \u2022 Blinding Words (Difficulty 3): If you get 3 successes on the decisive damage roll your target is blind for the scene. This applies a -3 penalty to all actions requiring sight for the scene. This penalty will also draw the attention of any of Orabilis Seekers that are in the area, likely causing more harm to the unfortunate soul so cursed.<br /> \u2022 Words of the Damned: Instead of blinding someone with these secrets you may instead scar and burn their flesh with these secrets as they try to burrow within this new vessel.<br /> <br /> Blasphemous Secrets<br /> Cost: 5m; Mins: Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Blasphemous Secrets<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Prerequisites: Black Secrets<br /> <br /> This evocation is even more powerful than Dark Secrets allowing withering attacks and adding \u00bd of the speakers willpower to their decisive damage roll, and ignores hardness. If this attack kills a target the soul is immediately torn from their body and cast to the space between the shells of Malfeas where it will be burnt to ash providing the caster sorcery motes equal to their current initiative or the health levels they took in the attack whichever is higher.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1635,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","user":"Citadel97501","date":". 10-19-2017, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T08:31:26-07:00","id":1145800,"title":"","content":"Hey! <br /> For some reason, metric ton of tags in your post <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1635\" data-vbnamecard=\"1635\">Citadel97501</a> <br /> So I'm going to comment here, instead of working through quotes.<br /> <br /> The shaping rituals seem...niche. The first two bascially requires an evocation to be generally useful (As the secrets of Orabilis aren't something most mortals know anyway), although the second one is basically a pedagogical version of Mara. Something with general knowledge or secrets might be more appropiate. The third one seems fine.<br /> <br /> Demonic Script Tatoos need to note that only Essence Users have their evocations.<br /> I'm a tad confused as to what the gambit does (Is it just a blinding gambit instead of damage? Is Words of the Damned just the name for the decisive attack?). It does give me this image of a sorcerer in a library tower, hording knowledge and surrounded by poor sods he's inflicted secrets on, so they can no longer see.<br /> <br /> Does blasphemous secrets help the gambit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T22:47:11-07:00","id":1145984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1145800#post1145800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey!<br /> For some reason, metric ton of tags in your post <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1635\" data-vbnamecard=\"1635\">Citadel97501</a><br /> So I'm going to comment here, instead of working through quotes.<br /> <br /> The shaping rituals seem...niche. The first two bascially requires an evocation to be generally useful (As the secrets of Orabilis aren't something most mortals know anyway), although the second one is basically a pedagogical version of Mara. Something with general knowledge or secrets might be more appropiate. The third one seems fine.<br /> <br /> Demonic Script Tatoos need to note that only Essence Users have their evocations.<br /> I'm a tad confused as to what the gambit does (Is it just a blinding gambit instead of damage? Is Words of the Damned just the name for the decisive attack?). It does give me this image of a sorcerer in a library tower, hording knowledge and surrounded by poor sods he's inflicted secrets on, so they can no longer see.<br /> <br /> Does blasphemous secrets help the gambit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about the tags, the shaping rituals were heavily built off of Mara's initiation. Power from Black Secrets, my intent was its more that any points of lore provide the bonus as it's more the caster is using his own knowledge of the secrets &amp; guile to blame his target which gets him the extra points of sorcery motes. The Blindness gambit does just blind them but as they were struck by the evocation it's keyword should add more motes to be drained with Power from Black Secrets. Words of the Damned is just a cool name for the decisive attack I thought a thematic name was a good idea. Blasphemous Secrets would make the damage higher allowing the gambit to work more often, and it would make the withering or decisive damage attacks much higher by adding 1/2 of willpower to the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T11:10:14-07:00","id":1146387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citadel97501</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1145984#post1145984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry about the tags,</div> </div> </div> </div>The tags are a result of copy-pasting into the forum text window. You can;t see them when you copy paste because the formatting tags are hidden from you. They are not hidden when someone goes to quote you. You can remove the formatting by either going to edit your post, open the text formatting toolbar (The big 'A' in the top right of the text window) and click the remove format button (looks like: &quot;<u><i>T</i></u><sub>X</sub>&quot; second from the left in the formatting toolbar OR by using the paste as plain text button in the toolbar (clipboard with a T in a box in the bottom right) and just replacing your old entry..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T05:16:34-07:00","id":1254140,"title":"","content":"<br /> Inspired by <i>Princess Mononoke </i>and, for the third shaping ritual, <i>Brother Bear's</i> aurora-spirits, I give you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Kin of the Unbroken Earth</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">It is said that the Dogs of the Unbroken Earth, night-black hound-deities of the remote places of Creation, take abandoned or orphaned children into their packs, raising them to maturity as defenders of the wild. Such children most often become God-Blooded of the Dogs, but sometimes they gain insight into the deep workings of the world beyond the dominion of mankind and become masters of strange sorceries that lay curses on interlopers and their works.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Shaping Rituals</span></span></b><ul><li>In destroying the artifice of humanity, the sorcerer releases power into her hands. Whenever the sorcerer destroys an artificial object, from a sword to a house, he may roll (Wits + the objects Resource cost) to capture that power, gaining sorcerous motes equal to the successes. These motes remain until the end of the scene, at which point they fade away.</li> <li>Once per day when the sorcerer takes time to meditate, admire the beauty of the tree-gods, play with her canine adopted family or otherwise enjoys some time in a place of unspoiled nature, she may roll (Wits + Integrity + 2). She gains sorcerous motes equal to the number of successes. These motes are lost at the end of the day.</li> <li>Upon hunting and killing an animal, the sorcerer may make a prayer roll (Charisma + Performance, difficulty 3 minus the sorcerer\u2019s Essence, minimum 1), asking her prey to aid her. Success causes the animal\u2019s spirit to linger invisibly around her, though if she is Exalted it will be visible as a vague outline in her Bonfire anima. As a miscellaneous action, the sorcerer may draw from her attendant spirits, rolling (Essence + number of spirits) and gaining that many sorcerous motes. If she does this, one of her spirits finds its obligation fulfilled, passing on into the Essence of Creation. She retains these motes until the end of the scene, and may spend them towards any spells she casts. Additionally, a spirit may be reflexively released in place of a point of Willpower when paying the cost of the sorcerer\u2019s control spell. She cannot have more than (Essence + Survival) spirits bound to her at one time.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><i>Other Benefits</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Wisdom</b><b> of the Wild (\u2022\u2022):*</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Those who have completed this initiation can draw insight from the natural world, studying at the feet of god-trees instead of in classrooms or from dusty tomes. Locating a source for a spell is modelled as a sorcerous working of Ambition 1 and the same Circle as the spell desired. Failure of the working merely indicates that the sorcerer must look elsewhere; a botch indicates that the source had been damaged in some way. This working costs no XP; the learning of the spell does. Time and assistance can affect the terminus, but components and infrastructure do not normally apply.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Tongue</b> of Beasts (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> The sorcerer understands the secret speech of animals, allowing him to communicate ideas with them commensurate to their intelligence - dogs, wolves, ravens and similar are able to understand more complex concepts than a sparrow or fish, while communicating with insects or mice is largely fruitless.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>*This was largely lifted from the Salinan Working Initiation a few pages back, because I wanted my wild-sorcerers to not need books.<br /> <br /> Commentary, ideas and criticism welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 09-14-2018, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T07:46:44-07:00","id":1254202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=727129#post727129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a reversal of Mara's initiation would be cool.<br /> <br /> <b>COVENANT WITH THE SUN</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Just curious, but did anyone think of the Warriors of Sunlight covenant from Dark Souls when they read this? I didn\u2019t include lightning or hammer the point home by calling Fed By Virtue \u201cJolly Cooperation\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T11:14:42-07:00","id":1254264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1254140#post1254140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...dogs, wolves and similar are able to understand more complex concepts than a bird...</div> </div> </div> </div>Corvids are <i>scary</i>-smart. Ravens can build tools, lie, recognize human faces, hold grudges, and <i>teach each other</i> all those previous things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 09-14-2018, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T11:40:49-07:00","id":1254272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1254264#post1254264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corvids are <i>scary</i>-smart. Ravens can build tools, lie, recognize human faces, hold grudges, and <i>teach each other</i> all those previous things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my favourite raven story is how in Japan (I think it was) ravens had figured out how to use cars to crack nuts for them. The process went like this:<br /> <br /> step 1 - wait until walk light activates on a crossing<br /> step 2 - run out into road and leave nut roughly in path of wheels<br /> step 3 - wait until traffic runs over nut<br /> step 4 - wait until walk signal goes off again and retrieve nut.<br /> step 5 - TEACH TRICK TO ALL OTHER RAVENS","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T12:01:12-07:00","id":1254280,"title":"","content":"Crows are smarter than canids. In fact, Crows and Parrots are on par with primates as far as intelligence vs body size index. With some beating chimpanzees there<br /> <br /> Only Humans and Dolphins still beat them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T12:55:04-07:00","id":1254307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/719260-ex3-in-which-we-brainstorm-sorcerous-initiations?p=1254264#post1254264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corvids are <i>scary</i>-smart. Ravens can build tools, lie, recognize human faces, hold grudges, and <i>teach each other</i> all those previous things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, I'd completely forgotten them. I was thinking of, like, sparrows. Lemme go edit that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-14T21:22:59-07:00","id":1254395,"title":"","content":"Yup. Modern dinosaurs are on par with modern mammals after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",